window.TLI_DATA = {"project": "tli.cloud: English in Cambodia", "projectKey": "tli-english-cambodia", "version": "1.3", "built": "2026-11-05 09:04", "builtISO": "2026-11-05T09:04:48+01:00", "parts": [{"id": "L.0", "title": "Grade 1 English starter course – overview", "order": 0, "goals": ["Place the course in the MoEYS Curriculum Framework (2016) for primary Foreign Languages.", "Show the lesson template, the Feed up step and the RTTI rubric used in every lesson.", "Explain how each lesson works with a teacher and in the self-paced app."], "metadata": {"status": "draft", "audience": "teachers, school leaders, app developers", "grade": "1 (age 6–7)", "subject": "Foreign Languages (English)", "moeys_reference": "Curriculum Framework of General Education and Technical Education (2016) – framework level verified; Grade 1 English syllabus to be checked", "cefr_cross_reference": "Pre-A1 (adapted descriptors)", "updated": "2026-11-05 (v1.3)"}, "file": "l0-course-overview.md", "notes": ["<p>Assumptions for Herbert to confirm: (1) no Grade 1 syllabus was mapped earlier; this is a first draft; (2) pupils are Khmer speakers with no English and are only starting to read Khmer; (3) the 2016 framework lists Foreign Languages from Grade 1, but in practice many public schools start English only in Grade 4 (MoEYS announced English for Grades 4–6, 2 × 40 min a week), so Grade 1 English is most likely to run in private or NGO-supported schools first.</p>\n", "<p>Source: MoEYS, Curriculum Framework of General Education and Technical Education, January 2016 (English version, sections 3.1, 4.2, 5.6, 6.2 Table 2, 7.1, 8.1), copy at nepcambodia.org. Activity names and the Function / Form / Vocabulary table: MoEYS, English Grade 4 Student's Book (2020). English for Grades 4–6, twice a week for 40 minutes: Phnom Penh Post, \"English instruction to expand to new grades\". Not verified: an official MoEYS Grade 1 English syllabus or textbook outcomes and codes (the MoEYS digital library lists an \"English Grade 1\" title but no details could be read), and any MoEYS-prescribed lesson-step names. Lesson outcomes in this course are draft wording.</p>\n", "<p>No MoEYS teacher guide with lesson steps was found. The activity names (Listen and say, Pair work, Letter practice) and the Function / Form / Vocabulary table follow the MoEYS English Grade 4 Student's Book (2020); the other step names are our own.</p>\n", "<p>CEFR does not prescribe an order for teaching the alphabet; Pre-A1 only describes recognising letters and, later, spelling one's own name. The alphabetical order follows the MoEYS English Grade 4 book (\"The letters\" A B C D). Khmer-friendly cues to be checked by a Khmer-speaking teacher.</p>\n", "<p>Khmer spellings of the names to be checked by a native speaker (Vichea and Chantha also have other spellings).</p>\n"], "blocks": [{"ref": "L.0 §0 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.0-0-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "e6f3b78022", "text": "Grade 1 English starter course – overview"}, {"ref": "L.0 §1 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.0-1-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "686c4978fc", "text": "The Cambodian frame (MoEYS)"}, {"ref": "L.0 §1 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.0-1-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "cbd290b8bb", "text": "The course follows the Curriculum Framework of General Education and Technical Education (MoEYS, 2016) first. CEFR is used only as a cross-reference."}, {"ref": "L.0 §1 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.0-1-2", "kind": "table", "h": "179ffd43ea", "text": "MoEYS reference What the framework says What this course does Place in the curriculum Foreign Languages (English or French) is a primary subject; the framework recommends international languages from Grade 1 to 6 as core subjects. English as Living language 1, Grade 1 Core competency 4.2 \"Learners can adequately use foreign languages for communication, research and continued study.\" Every lesson outcome serves this competency. Foreign Languages goals (section 5.6, quoted) \"Possess competencies in communication in all four skills (listening, speaking, reading and writing).\" \"Become life-long learners with creativity and confidence.\" Lessons start with Listening and Speaking and add letter recognition from Lesson 2. Subject components Listening, Reading, Speaking, Writing Grade 1 starts with Listening and Speaking, plus letter recognition from Lesson 2; writing comes later. Study time, Grades 1–6 2 study hours of Foreign Languages per week; 1 study hour = 40 minutes (6 days, 5 study hours a day) One lesson = one study hour of 40 minutes; two lessons a week. Expected primary outcome (quoted) \"Construct basic knowledge of Science, Information and Communications Technology (ICT) and Foreign Languages.\" Six lessons build the first words, chunks and letters. Teaching principle 7.1 Teaching facilitates learning \"through learner centered approaches\". Pupils move, speak in pairs and groups, and play; the teacher talks less. Assessment principle 8.1 Assess learners' knowledge, skills, attitude and application skills; assessment gives feedback to improve learning. Feed up and the RTTI rubric in every lesson; observation, not written tests."}, {"ref": "L.0 §2 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.0-2-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "f7340444ea", "text": "Who this course is for"}, {"ref": "L.0 §2 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.0-2-1", "kind": "list", "h": "813360009d", "text": "Pupils: Grade 1, about 6–7 years old, Khmer as first language, no English yet. Setting: primary schools that teach English from Grade 1 – most likely private or NGO-supported schools at first. Classes of 30–50 pupils are expected. Reading and writing: the focus is Listening and Speaking. Pupils see written English words next to pictures, but they are not asked to read or write sentences yet."}, {"ref": "L.0 §3 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.0-3-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "97f4de08ec", "text": "Feed up, feed back, feed forward"}, {"ref": "L.0 §3 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.0-3-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "4c3a5ef6f1", "text": "Every lesson uses the three feedback questions of Hattie and Timperley (2007):"}, {"ref": "L.0 §3 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.0-3-2", "kind": "list", "h": "b78adb0661", "text": "Feed up – Where am I going? The teacher says the learning goal and shows two or three success criteria in pupil words, in English and Khmer, each with a picture or gesture cue. Feed back – How am I going? During and at the end of the lesson the teacher tells pupils what they can already do, using the rubric's \"feed back\" sentences. Feed forward – Where to next? The teacher gives one small next step from the rubric."}, {"ref": "L.0 §4 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.0-4-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "12630d1ae8", "text": "The RTTI rubric"}, {"ref": "L.0 §4 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.0-4-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "36620a8822", "text": "RTTI (Drost and Verra) describes four levels of learning. Every lesson has a rubric with these rows:"}, {"ref": "L.0 §4 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.0-4-2", "kind": "table", "h": "80dee521d3", "text": "Level Meaning In Grade 1 English this looks like R – Reproduction Repeat what was taught Repeats words after the teacher T1 – Training Use it in the practised activity Answers or acts correctly in the class game T2 – Transfer Use it in a new situation Uses the words with a new person, picture or object I – Insight Understand why Explains with a gesture or in Khmer why an answer fits"}, {"ref": "L.0 §4 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.0-4-3", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "4d69cbee80", "text": "The rubric's last column uses colours for what to expect after one lesson: green = expected for all or most pupils, yellow = with help, red = stretch goal, not expected yet."}, {"ref": "L.0 §5 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.0-5-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "5f71879c44", "text": "Lesson template"}, {"ref": "L.0 §5 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.0-5-1", "kind": "table", "h": "bec44f0184", "text": "Step Time What happens Warm-up and feed up 5 min Hello song, review, say the learning goal and show the success criteria cues Listen and say 8 min New words with pictures, gestures and real objects; pupils repeat Pair work (or Practice) 8 min (10 in Lesson 1) Pupils ask and answer in pairs; \"Practice\" where the step is whole-class Letter practice (from Lesson 2) 5 min Two or three letters: see the letter, hear the sound, point to the picture; no writing yet Game, song or TPR 8 min (10 in Lesson 1) Total Physical Response: pupils move to show understanding Wrap-up and feed back 6 min (7 in Lesson 1) Pupils show what they can do per success criterion; one feed-forward tip; Goodbye song"}, {"ref": "L.0 §5 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.0-5-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "367dd158a9", "text": "Every lesson also has a small Function / Form / Vocabulary table, the syllabus format of the official MoEYS English Grade 4 textbook. The activity names Listen and say, Pair work and Letter practice come from that book too."}, {"ref": "L.0 §6 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.0-6-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "eacfc03f32", "text": "Teacher mode and app mode"}, {"ref": "L.0 §6 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.0-6-1", "kind": "list", "h": "60738bd57d", "text": "Teacher mode: flashcards, gestures and songs. No electronics needed. Every lesson lists activities for 30–50 pupils with only a board and chalk. App mode (self-paced): audio first, pictures instead of written instructions, instant spoken feedback. Instructions in Khmer audio; target words in English audio. No typing; tap, drag and \"say it\" (record and play back). Quiz in both modes: every quiz question is tagged with a success criterion and an RTTI level, so the result says which levels a pupil reached and what to try next."}, {"ref": "L.0 §7 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.0-7-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "2402ea3632", "text": "Materials"}, {"ref": "L.0 §7 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.0-7-1", "kind": "list", "h": "0e4c9b99a6", "text": "Flashcards (A4 pictures) for every target word; success criteria cue cards. Real classroom objects (pencil, book, bag) and coloured paper. Audio recordings of every word, chunk and song, plus Khmer instruction audio. A simple puppet (a sock puppet is enough) as the \"English friend\"."}, {"ref": "L.0 §8 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.0-8-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "8eaa2ae1d5", "text": "The first six lessons"}, {"ref": "L.0 §8 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.0-8-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "78939094b4", "text": "The topics lead into the official MoEYS English Grade 4 book (Unit 1 Greetings, name and age, numbers 1–10; Unit 2 Things; Unit 3 Animals; later Family):"}, {"ref": "L.0 §8 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.0-8-2", "kind": "table", "h": "bcffa8a597", "text": "Lesson Topic Letters Leads into Grade 4 1 Hello! – greetings and my name – Unit 1 Greetings 2 Numbers 1–5 – How old are you? A, B Unit 1 Lesson 3 (age, numbers) 3 Colours C, D – 4 In my classroom (pen, pencil, book, bag, desk) E, F, G Unit 2 Things 5 My family H, I, J Unit 7 Family 6 Animals – numbers to 10 K, L, M Unit 3 Animals; Unit 1 numbers 1–10"}, {"ref": "L.0 §8 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.0-8-3", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "e31510d178", "text": "Progress checklist and review quiz (R.1) covers Lessons 1–5; it is not part of the lesson sequence. Every lesson ends with its own wrap-up and feed back, so there are no separate review lessons."}, {"ref": "L.0 §9 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.0-9-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "9bd9f65a5e", "text": "Letters and sounds"}, {"ref": "L.0 §9 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.0-9-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "9410a58bb7", "text": "From Lesson 2, each lesson adds two or three letters in alphabet order: A B · C D · E F G · H I J · K L M. Pupils recognise the capital and small letter, hear the sound and match a picture word (apple, ball, cat, dog, egg, fish, goat, hen, insect, jump, kite, lemon, mango). Each letter has a Khmer-friendly cue, for example \"B is like ប\", and a warning where Khmer has no such sound (F, G). There is no heavy writing in Grade 1."}, {"ref": "L.0 §10 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.0-10-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "0a010fad25", "text": "Names in dialogues"}, {"ref": "L.0 §10 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.0-10-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "a86975635a", "text": "The course uses four common Khmer names, two girls and two boys, in every lesson. They are deliberately not the names used in the MoEYS textbooks. The class puppet is Teddy."}, {"ref": "L.0 §10 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.0-10-2", "kind": "table", "h": "5be161dda0", "text": "Name Khmer Sreymom ស្រីមុំ girl Chantha ចន្ថា girl Vichea វិជ្ជា boy Piseth ពិសិដ្ឋ boy"}, {"ref": "L.0 §11 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.0-11-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "b8efd777f4", "text": "CEFR cross-reference"}, {"ref": "L.0 §11 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.0-11-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "9179c97120", "text": "Secondary reference only. The lessons aim at CEFR Pre-A1 , moving towards A1. Can-do statements are adapted from the CEFR Companion Volume (2020) Pre-A1 descriptors; they are not an official CEFR test. Letter work matches the Pre-A1 idea of recognising letters (later: spelling one's own name)."}], "html": "<div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"e6f3b78022\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.0 §0 ¶0\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.0-0-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §0 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §0 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶0</button><h1 data-body=\"1\">Grade 1 English starter course – overview</h1></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"686c4978fc\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.0 §1 ¶0\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.0-1-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §1 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §1 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">The Cambodian frame (MoEYS)</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"cbd290b8bb\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.0 §1 ¶1\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.0-1-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §1 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §1 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">The course follows the <strong>Curriculum Framework of General Education and Technical Education</strong> (MoEYS, 2016) first. CEFR is used only as a cross-reference.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"179ffd43ea\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.0 §1 ¶2\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.0-1-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §1 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §1 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>MoEYS reference</th>\n<th>What the framework says</th>\n<th>What this course does</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Place in the curriculum</td>\n<td>Foreign Languages (English or French) is a primary subject; the framework recommends international languages from Grade 1 to 6 as core subjects.</td>\n<td>English as Living language 1, Grade 1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Core competency 4.2</td>\n<td>\"Learners can adequately use foreign languages for communication, research and continued study.\"</td>\n<td>Every lesson outcome serves this competency.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Foreign Languages goals (section 5.6, quoted)</td>\n<td>\"Possess competencies in communication in all four skills (listening, speaking, reading and writing).\" \"Become life-long learners with creativity and confidence.\"</td>\n<td>Lessons start with Listening and Speaking and add letter recognition from Lesson 2.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Subject components</td>\n<td>Listening, Reading, Speaking, Writing</td>\n<td>Grade 1 starts with Listening and Speaking, plus letter recognition from Lesson 2; writing comes later.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Study time, Grades 1–6</td>\n<td>2 study hours of Foreign Languages per week; 1 study hour = 40 minutes (6 days, 5 study hours a day)</td>\n<td>One lesson = one study hour of 40 minutes; two lessons a week.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Expected primary outcome (quoted)</td>\n<td>\"Construct basic knowledge of Science, Information and Communications Technology (ICT) and Foreign Languages.\"</td>\n<td>Six lessons build the first words, chunks and letters.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Teaching principle 7.1</td>\n<td>Teaching facilitates learning \"through learner centered approaches\".</td>\n<td>Pupils move, speak in pairs and groups, and play; the teacher talks less.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Assessment principle 8.1</td>\n<td>Assess learners' knowledge, skills, attitude and application skills; assessment gives feedback to improve learning.</td>\n<td>Feed up and the RTTI rubric in every lesson; observation, not written tests.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"f7340444ea\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.0 §2 ¶0\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.0-2-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §2 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §2 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Who this course is for</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"813360009d\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.0 §2 ¶1\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.0-2-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §2 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §2 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Pupils:</strong> Grade 1, about 6–7 years old, Khmer as first language, no English yet.</li>\n<li><strong>Setting:</strong> primary schools that teach English from Grade 1 – most likely private or NGO-supported schools at first. Classes of 30–50 pupils are expected.</li>\n<li><strong>Reading and writing:</strong> the focus is Listening and Speaking. Pupils see written English words next to pictures, but they are not asked to read or write sentences yet.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"97f4de08ec\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.0 §3 ¶0\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.0-3-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §3 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §3 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Feed up, feed back, feed forward</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"4c3a5ef6f1\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.0 §3 ¶1\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.0-3-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §3 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §3 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Every lesson uses the three feedback questions of Hattie and Timperley (2007):</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b78adb0661\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.0 §3 ¶2\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.0-3-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §3 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §3 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶2</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Feed up – Where am I going?</strong> The teacher says the learning goal and shows two or three success criteria in pupil words, in English and Khmer, each with a picture or gesture cue.</li>\n<li><strong>Feed back – How am I going?</strong> During and at the end of the lesson the teacher tells pupils what they can already do, using the rubric's \"feed back\" sentences.</li>\n<li><strong>Feed forward – Where to next?</strong> The teacher gives one small next step from the rubric.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"12630d1ae8\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.0 §4 ¶0\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.0-4-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §4 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §4 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">The RTTI rubric</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"36620a8822\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.0 §4 ¶1\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.0-4-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §4 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §4 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">RTTI (Drost and Verra) describes four levels of learning. Every lesson has a rubric with these rows:</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"80dee521d3\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.0 §4 ¶2\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.0-4-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §4 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §4 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Level</th>\n<th>Meaning</th>\n<th>In Grade 1 English this looks like</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>R – Reproduction</td>\n<td>Repeat what was taught</td>\n<td>Repeats words after the teacher</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T1 – Training</td>\n<td>Use it in the practised activity</td>\n<td>Answers or acts correctly in the class game</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T2 – Transfer</td>\n<td>Use it in a new situation</td>\n<td>Uses the words with a new person, picture or object</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>I – Insight</td>\n<td>Understand why</td>\n<td>Explains with a gesture or in Khmer why an answer fits</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"4d69cbee80\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.0 §4 ¶3\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.0-4-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §4 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §4 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶3</button><p data-body=\"1\">The rubric's last column uses colours for what to expect after one lesson: <strong>green</strong> = expected for all or most pupils, <strong>yellow</strong> = with help, <strong>red</strong> = stretch goal, not expected yet.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"5f71879c44\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.0 §5 ¶0\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.0-5-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §5 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §5 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Lesson template</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"bec44f0184\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.0 §5 ¶1\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.0-5-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §5 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §5 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶1</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Step</th>\n<th>Time</th>\n<th>What happens</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Warm-up and feed up</td>\n<td>5 min</td>\n<td>Hello song, review, say the learning goal and show the success criteria cues</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Listen and say</td>\n<td>8 min</td>\n<td>New words with pictures, gestures and real objects; pupils repeat</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pair work (or Practice)</td>\n<td>8 min (10 in Lesson 1)</td>\n<td>Pupils ask and answer in pairs; \"Practice\" where the step is whole-class</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Letter practice (from Lesson 2)</td>\n<td>5 min</td>\n<td>Two or three letters: see the letter, hear the sound, point to the picture; no writing yet</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Game, song or TPR</td>\n<td>8 min (10 in Lesson 1)</td>\n<td>Total Physical Response: pupils move to show understanding</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Wrap-up and feed back</td>\n<td>6 min (7 in Lesson 1)</td>\n<td>Pupils show what they can do per success criterion; one feed-forward tip; Goodbye song</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"367dd158a9\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.0 §5 ¶2\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.0-5-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §5 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §5 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\">Every lesson also has a small <strong>Function / Form / Vocabulary</strong> table, the syllabus format of the official MoEYS English Grade 4 textbook. The activity names Listen and say, Pair work and Letter practice come from that book too.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"eacfc03f32\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.0 §6 ¶0\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.0-6-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §6 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §6 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Teacher mode and app mode</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"60738bd57d\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.0 §6 ¶1\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.0-6-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §6 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §6 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Teacher mode:</strong> flashcards, gestures and songs. No electronics needed. Every lesson lists activities for 30–50 pupils with only a board and chalk.</li>\n<li><strong>App mode (self-paced):</strong> audio first, pictures instead of written instructions, instant spoken feedback. Instructions in Khmer audio; target words in English audio. No typing; tap, drag and \"say it\" (record and play back).</li>\n<li><strong>Quiz in both modes:</strong> every quiz question is tagged with a success criterion and an RTTI level, so the result says which levels a pupil reached and what to try next.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"2402ea3632\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.0 §7 ¶0\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.0-7-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §7 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §7 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Materials</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"0e4c9b99a6\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.0 §7 ¶1\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.0-7-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §7 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §7 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>Flashcards (A4 pictures) for every target word; success criteria cue cards.</li>\n<li>Real classroom objects (pencil, book, bag) and coloured paper.</li>\n<li>Audio recordings of every word, chunk and song, plus Khmer instruction audio.</li>\n<li>A simple puppet (a sock puppet is enough) as the \"English friend\".</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"8eaa2ae1d5\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.0 §8 ¶0\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.0-8-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §8 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §8 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">The first six lessons</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"78939094b4\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.0 §8 ¶1\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.0-8-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §8 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §8 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">The topics lead into the official MoEYS English Grade 4 book (Unit 1 Greetings, name and age, numbers 1–10; Unit 2 Things; Unit 3 Animals; later Family):</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"bcffa8a597\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.0 §8 ¶2\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.0-8-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §8 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §8 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Lesson</th>\n<th>Topic</th>\n<th>Letters</th>\n<th>Leads into Grade 4</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Hello! – greetings and my name</td>\n<td>–</td>\n<td>Unit 1 Greetings</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Numbers 1–5 – How old are you?</td>\n<td>A, B</td>\n<td>Unit 1 Lesson 3 (age, numbers)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>Colours</td>\n<td>C, D</td>\n<td>–</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>In my classroom (pen, pencil, book, bag, desk)</td>\n<td>E, F, G</td>\n<td>Unit 2 Things</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>My family</td>\n<td>H, I, J</td>\n<td>Unit 7 Family</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>Animals – numbers to 10</td>\n<td>K, L, M</td>\n<td>Unit 3 Animals; Unit 1 numbers 1–10</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"e31510d178\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.0 §8 ¶3\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.0-8-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §8 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §8 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶3</button><p data-body=\"1\">Progress checklist and review quiz (R.1) covers Lessons 1–5; it is not part of the lesson sequence. Every lesson ends with its own wrap-up and feed back, so there are no separate review lessons.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9bd9f65a5e\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.0 §9 ¶0\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.0-9-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §9 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §9 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Letters and sounds</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9410a58bb7\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.0 §9 ¶1\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.0-9-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §9 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §9 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">From Lesson 2, each lesson adds two or three letters in alphabet order: A B · C D · E F G · H I J · K L M. Pupils recognise the capital and small letter, hear the sound and match a picture word (apple, ball, cat, dog, egg, fish, goat, hen, insect, jump, kite, lemon, mango). Each letter has a Khmer-friendly cue, for example \"B is like ប\", and a warning where Khmer has no such sound (F, G). There is no heavy writing in Grade 1.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"0a010fad25\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.0 §10 ¶0\" data-sec=\"10\" id=\"p-L.0-10-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §10 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §10 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§10 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Names in dialogues</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"a86975635a\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.0 §10 ¶1\" data-sec=\"10\" id=\"p-L.0-10-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §10 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §10 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§10 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">The course uses four common Khmer names, two girls and two boys, in every lesson. They are deliberately not the names used in the MoEYS textbooks. The class puppet is Teddy.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"5be161dda0\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.0 §10 ¶2\" data-sec=\"10\" id=\"p-L.0-10-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §10 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §10 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§10 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Name</th>\n<th>Khmer</th>\n<th></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Sreymom</td>\n<td>ស្រីមុំ</td>\n<td>girl</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Chantha</td>\n<td>ចន្ថា</td>\n<td>girl</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Vichea</td>\n<td>វិជ្ជា</td>\n<td>boy</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Piseth</td>\n<td>ពិសិដ្ឋ</td>\n<td>boy</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b8efd777f4\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.0 §11 ¶0\" data-sec=\"11\" id=\"p-L.0-11-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §11 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §11 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§11 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">CEFR cross-reference</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9179c97120\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.0 §11 ¶1\" data-sec=\"11\" id=\"p-L.0-11-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §11 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §11 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§11 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Secondary reference only. The lessons aim at CEFR <strong>Pre-A1</strong>, moving towards A1. Can-do statements are adapted from the CEFR Companion Volume (2020) Pre-A1 descriptors; they are not an official CEFR test. Letter work matches the Pre-A1 idea of recognising letters (later: spelling one's own name).</p></div>"}, {"id": "L.1", "title": "Lesson 1: Hello! – greetings and my name", "order": 1, "goals": ["MoEYS (draft lesson outcome): Pupils use simple English greetings and say their own name in class (Listening and Speaking).", "Success criterion 1: I can say Hello and Goodbye.", "Success criterion 2: I can say my name: I'm …", "Success criterion 3: I know when to say Hello and when to say Goodbye."], "metadata": {"status": "draft", "grade": "1", "subject": "Foreign Languages (English)", "moeys_reference": "Curriculum Framework of General Education and Technical Education (2016) – framework level verified; Grade 1 English syllabus wording to be checked", "cefr_cross_reference": "Pre-A1 (adapted, CEFR Companion Volume)", "duration": "one study hour (40 min)", "updated": "2026-11-05 (v1.3)"}, "file": "l1-hello.md", "notes": ["<p>Verified in the 2016 Curriculum Framework: core competency 4.2 wording, the four subject components, Grade 1 time allocation (2 study hours a week, 40 minutes each), the assessment principles. The Function / Form / Vocabulary table and the activity names (Listen and say, Pair work, Letter practice) follow the official MoEYS English Grade 4 Student's Book (2020). NOT found: an official MoEYS Grade 1 English syllabus, its outcome wording or codes, and a MoEYS teacher guide with lesson steps. The lesson outcome above is our draft wording, not an official MoEYS outcome. See open-items.md.</p>\n", "<p>Khmer pupil-friendly sentences to be verified by a native speaker (Grade 1 level).</p>\n", "<p>Khmer to be verified by a native speaker, especially the most natural classroom word for \"goodbye\" for small children (លាហើយ or ជំរាបលា).</p>\n"], "blocks": [{"ref": "L.1 §0 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-0-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "400b3a7b02", "text": "Lesson 1: Hello! – greetings and my name"}, {"ref": "L.1 §0 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-0-1", "kind": "figure", "h": "da39a3ee5e", "text": ""}, {"ref": "L.1 §0 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.1-0-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "755830834e", "text": "In this lesson pupils meet the class puppet and learn to say hello, goodbye and their name."}, {"ref": "L.1 §1 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-1-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "025eec04ab", "text": "MoEYS frame"}, {"ref": "L.1 §1 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-1-1", "kind": "table", "h": "5dcb1f565f", "text": "MoEYS reference This lesson Framework Curriculum Framework of General Education and Technical Education (MoEYS, 2016) Subject and grade Foreign Languages (English), Grade 1 (primary) Core competency 4.2 Foreign Languages: \"Learners can adequately use foreign languages for communication, research and continued study.\" Foreign Languages goals (section 5.6, quoted) \"Possess competencies in communication in all four skills (listening, speaking, reading and writing).\" \"Become life-long learners with creativity and confidence.\" Expected outcome for primary (quoted) \"Construct basic knowledge of Science, Information and Communications Technology (ICT) and Foreign Languages.\" Subject components Listening and Speaking in this lesson (Reading and Writing come later) Study time Grade 1 has 2 study hours of Foreign Languages per week; one study hour is 40 minutes. This lesson is one study hour. Lesson learning outcome (draft) Pupils use simple English greetings and say their own name in class (Listening and Speaking). Assessment (framework section 8.1) Knowledge, skills, attitude and application skills – observed with the RTTI rubric below"}, {"ref": "L.1 §1 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.1-1-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "3119e881c9", "text": "Lesson syllabus (in the Function / Form / Vocabulary format of the MoEYS English Grade 4 textbook):"}, {"ref": "L.1 §1 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.1-1-3", "kind": "table", "h": "d2acf06242", "text": "Function Form Vocabulary Greeting each other; saying your name Hello! / Hi! / Goodbye! – What's your name? – I'm … hello, hi, goodbye, I'm, name"}, {"ref": "L.1 §2 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-2-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "27efc58195", "text": "Feed up: where are we going?"}, {"ref": "L.1 §2 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-2-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "8875fc3408", "text": "Learning goal (say it at the start): Today we learn to say hello, goodbye and our name."}, {"ref": "L.1 §2 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.1-2-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "dc194cd0d6", "text": "In Khmer: ថ្ងៃនេះ យើងរៀននិយាយ Hello, Goodbye និងប្រាប់ឈ្មោះរបស់យើង។"}, {"ref": "L.1 §2 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.1-2-3", "kind": "table", "h": "b02e263660", "text": "# Success criterion (pupil words) Khmer (pupil words) Picture or gesture cue 1 I can say Hello and Goodbye. ខ្ញុំអាចនិយាយ Hello និង Goodbye។ wave hand 2 I can say my name: I'm … ខ្ញុំអាចប្រាប់ឈ្មោះខ្ញុំ៖ I'm … hand on chest 3 I know when to say Hello and when to say Goodbye. ខ្ញុំដឹងថា ពេលណានិយាយ Hello ពេលណានិយាយ Goodbye។ point to the door"}, {"ref": "L.1 §2 ¶4", "anchor": "p-L.1-2-4", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "1a15caa138", "text": "Draw the three cues on the board and point to them at the start and at the end of the lesson."}, {"ref": "L.1 §3 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-3-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "a343dabcab", "text": "RTTI rubric for the teacher"}, {"ref": "L.1 §3 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-3-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "ee6f09a57a", "text": "RTTI levels: R Reproduction (repeat what was taught), T1 Training (use it in the practised activity), T2 Transfer (use it in a new situation), I Insight (understand and explain why). The last column shows what to expect after this lesson: green = expected for all or most, yellow = with help, red = stretch goal, not expected yet."}, {"ref": "L.1 §3 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.1-3-2", "kind": "table", "h": "ceea7b25be", "text": "Level What the pupil does Teacher looks for Feed back (say) Feed forward (say) Expected after this lesson R – Reproduction Repeats Hello, Goodbye and I'm … after the teacher. Says the words in the choral drill, with the wave. \"You said Hello clearly!\" \"Now say it to your friend, without me.\" expected for all (rated green) T1 – Training Answers \"What's your name?\" with I'm … in the ball toss. Answers alone when the ball comes, no whispering help. \"You answered by yourself.\" \"Next time, ask the question back: What's your name?\" expected for most (rated green) T2 – Transfer Greets a new person (visitor, puppet, head teacher) without a prompt. Greets someone at the door or a visitor on their own. \"You greeted our visitor – that is real English!\" \"Tomorrow, say Hello to a teacher at the gate.\" with help (rated yellow) I – Insight Chooses Hello or Goodbye for a picture of arriving or leaving, and shows why (points to door, sun, bag). Explains in Khmer or with a gesture why it is Hello or Goodbye. \"You know why we say Goodbye here.\" \"Can you find another time we say Hello?\" stretch goal (rated red)"}, {"ref": "L.1 §4 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-4-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "5a2137d2b9", "text": "Target vocabulary"}, {"ref": "L.1 §4 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-4-1", "kind": "table", "h": "0128bdd2b7", "text": "English Khmer Sound hint Picture idea hello សួស្តី he-LOH child waving goodbye លាហើយ good-BYE child waving at a door name ឈ្មោះ naym name tag teacher គ្រូ TEE-cher teacher at the board friend មិត្តភក្តិ frend two children holding hands"}, {"ref": "L.1 §5 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-5-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "f137c97e3d", "text": "Target language"}, {"ref": "L.1 §5 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-5-1", "kind": "list", "h": "9742c2c24f", "text": "Hello! / Hi! Goodbye! / Bye! What's your name? I'm (name). Dialogue: Sreymom: \"Hello! I'm Sreymom. What's your name?\" – Vichea: \"Hi! I'm Vichea.\""}, {"ref": "L.1 §6 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-6-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "1bd537eb12", "text": "Teacher-led lesson (one study hour, 40 min)"}, {"ref": "L.1 §6 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-6-1", "kind": "list", "h": "b17223aafb", "text": "Warm-up and feed up (5 min): Say the learning goal and point to the success criteria cues. The teacher waves and says \"Hello!\" to the class until pupils wave back. Introduce the puppet: \"Hello! I'm Teddy.\" Listen and say (8 min): Show the flashcards hello, goodbye, teacher, friend. Say each word three times with a gesture. Model \"What's your name? – I'm …\" with the puppet. Pair work (10 min): Choral repetition: whole class, then boys, then girls, then rows. Then pairs: \"Hello! What's your name?\" – \"I'm …\". Game (10 min): Hello–Goodbye. Teacher says \"Hello!\", pupils stand and wave. \"Goodbye!\", pupils sit and wave. Speed up. Wrap-up and feed back (7 min): Point to each success criterion cue; pupils show thumbs up (I can), sideways (with help) or down (not yet). Give one feed-forward tip from the rubric. Sing a hello/goodbye song. Five pupils say \"I'm …\" to the puppet."}, {"ref": "L.1 §7 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-7-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "beb8224862", "text": "Self-paced app lesson"}, {"ref": "L.1 §7 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-7-1", "kind": "list", "h": "2b162ed6cb", "text": "Meet Teddy: the puppet waves; audio \"Hello! I'm Teddy.\" Khmer audio: \"Tap Teddy to say hello.\" Listen and tap: two pictures (waving hello, waving goodbye). Audio \"Hello!\" – the pupil taps the right one. Right: \"Great!\" with a star. Wrong: the right picture wiggles and the word plays again. Say it: the pupil presses the microphone and says \"Hello!\". The app plays it back next to the model. My name: the pupil records \"I'm (name).\" The recording is saved for the parent or teacher to hear. Song: hello song with tap-along actions."}, {"ref": "L.1 §8 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-8-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "07cd9e0db6", "text": "Activities without electronics"}, {"ref": "L.1 §8 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-8-1", "kind": "list", "h": "9e38f9490f", "text": "Name chain: in rows, each pupil says \"I'm …\" and the next one says \"Hello, (name)!\". Ball toss: a paper ball goes round; the catcher answers \"What's your name?\". Both work with 50 pupils by running them row by row at the same time."}, {"ref": "L.1 §9 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-9-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "7f57b36be2", "text": "Differentiation"}, {"ref": "L.1 §9 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-9-1", "kind": "list", "h": "37b841320c", "text": "Need more support: may answer with just their name, or wave and say \"Hello\". Ready for more: ask a friend \"What's your name?\" and introduce them: \"This is Sreymom.\""}, {"ref": "L.1 §10 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-10-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "3bd9f3865f", "text": "Quick assessment"}, {"ref": "L.1 §10 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-10-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "400206d473", "text": "The teacher walks round during the ball toss and ticks on the checklist: says Hello / Goodbye, says \"I'm …\"."}, {"ref": "L.1 §10 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.1-10-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "9c2963b303", "text": "Record the RTTI level each pupil reached per success criterion in the progress checklist (R.1)."}, {"ref": "L.1 §11 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-11-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "25c86f6a92", "text": "Quiz"}, {"ref": "L.1 §11 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-11-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "2289a536b9", "text": "Each question checks one success criterion at one RTTI level. After Check , the quiz shows which levels the pupil reached for each criterion and what to try next."}, {"ref": "L.1 §11 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.1-11-2", "kind": "table", "h": "46f07fad6a", "text": "Success criterion RTTI level Question 1 Hello and Goodbye R 1 1 Hello and Goodbye T1 2 2 My name R 3 2 My name T2 4 3 When to say which I 5"}, {"ref": "L.1 §11 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.1-11-3", "kind": "quiz", "h": "8e69109225", "text": "1. 👋 Teddy says \"Hello!\". Say it back. Criterion 1 · RTTI level R Hello! Yes! You said Hello back. Criterion 1, level R. Five! Five is a number. Listen again: Teddy says Hello. Red! Red is a colour. Say Hello back to Teddy. 2. 🧒 A new friend sits next to you in the morning. What do you say? Criterion 1 · RTTI level T1 Bye! Bye is for leaving. Your friend just came: say Hello. Hi! Yes! Hi is a short Hello. You used it with a friend. Six! Six is a number. Greet your friend with Hello or Hi. 3. The teacher asks \"What's your name?\". What do you say? Criterion 2 · RTTI level R I'm six. That is your age. Say your name: I'm … I'm Vichea. Yes! You said your name with I'm. Hello, teacher. That is a greeting. Now say your name: I'm … 4. 🧑‍🏫 A visitor comes to class. She says \"Hello! I'm Chantha. And you?\" Criterion 2 · RTTI level T2 Hello! I'm Vichea. Great! You greeted a new person and said your name. Goodbye, Chantha. She just came. Say Hello and your name. I'm a pencil. Use your own name: I'm Vichea. 5. 🚪🎒 School is over. You take your bag and go to the door. Why do we say Goodbye? Criterion 3 · RTTI level I Because we meet a friend. When we meet, we say Hello. Because we are leaving. Yes! We say Goodbye when we leave. Because it is red. Colours do not tell us. Think: are you coming or leaving? Check Try again"}, {"ref": "L.1 §12 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-12-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "b8efd777f4", "text": "CEFR cross-reference"}, {"ref": "L.1 §12 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-12-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "9ace50ee5c", "text": "Secondary reference only. Pre-A1 can-do statements adapted from the CEFR Companion Volume (2020); not an official CEFR test."}, {"ref": "L.1 §12 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.1-12-2", "kind": "list", "h": "a0a9ff7587", "text": "I can say Hello and Goodbye to my teacher and friends. I can say my name: I'm Vichea. I can understand What's your name? when it is asked slowly with a gesture."}], "html": "<div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"400b3a7b02\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §0 ¶0\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.1-0-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §0 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §0 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶0</button><h1 data-body=\"1\">Lesson 1: Hello! – greetings and my name</h1></div><div class=\"blk blk-figure fl-right\" data-h=\"da39a3ee5e\" data-kind=\"figure\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §0 ¶1\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.1-0-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §0 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §0 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶1</button><figure class=\"fig fig-right\" data-body=\"1\" data-marker=\"right\"><button aria-label=\"Enlarge image: Two children wave and say Hello\" class=\"img-zoom\" type=\"button\"><img alt=\"Two children wave and say Hello\" data-src=\"images/hello-wave.svg\" loading=\"eager\" src=\"assets/images/images/hello-wave.svg\"/></button></figure></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"755830834e\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.1 §0 ¶2\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.1-0-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §0 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §0 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\">In this lesson pupils meet the class puppet and learn to say hello, goodbye and their name.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"025eec04ab\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §1 ¶0\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.1-1-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §1 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §1 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">MoEYS frame</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"5dcb1f565f\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §1 ¶1\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.1-1-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §1 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §1 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶1</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>MoEYS reference</th>\n<th>This lesson</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Framework</td>\n<td>Curriculum Framework of General Education and Technical Education (MoEYS, 2016)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Subject and grade</td>\n<td>Foreign Languages (English), Grade 1 (primary)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Core competency</td>\n<td>4.2 Foreign Languages: \"Learners can adequately use foreign languages for communication, research and continued study.\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Foreign Languages goals (section 5.6, quoted)</td>\n<td>\"Possess competencies in communication in all four skills (listening, speaking, reading and writing).\" \"Become life-long learners with creativity and confidence.\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Expected outcome for primary (quoted)</td>\n<td>\"Construct basic knowledge of Science, Information and Communications Technology (ICT) and Foreign Languages.\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Subject components</td>\n<td>Listening and Speaking in this lesson (Reading and Writing come later)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Study time</td>\n<td>Grade 1 has 2 study hours of Foreign Languages per week; one study hour is 40 minutes. This lesson is one study hour.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Lesson learning outcome (draft)</td>\n<td>Pupils use simple English greetings and say their own name in class (Listening and Speaking).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Assessment (framework section 8.1)</td>\n<td>Knowledge, skills, attitude and application skills – observed with the RTTI rubric below</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3119e881c9\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.1 §1 ¶2\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.1-1-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §1 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §1 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>Lesson syllabus</strong> (in the Function / Form / Vocabulary format of the MoEYS English Grade 4 textbook):</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"d2acf06242\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.1 §1 ¶3\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.1-1-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §1 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §1 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶3</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Function</th>\n<th>Form</th>\n<th>Vocabulary</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Greeting each other; saying your name</td>\n<td>Hello! / Hi! / Goodbye! – What's your name? – I'm …</td>\n<td>hello, hi, goodbye, I'm, name</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"27efc58195\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §2 ¶0\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.1-2-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §2 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §2 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Feed up: where are we going?</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"8875fc3408\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §2 ¶1\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.1-2-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §2 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §2 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>Learning goal (say it at the start):</strong> Today we learn to say hello, goodbye and our name.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"dc194cd0d6\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.1 §2 ¶2\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.1-2-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §2 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §2 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>In Khmer:</strong> ថ្ងៃនេះ យើងរៀននិយាយ Hello, Goodbye និងប្រាប់ឈ្មោះរបស់យើង។</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b02e263660\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.1 §2 ¶3\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.1-2-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §2 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §2 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶3</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>#</th>\n<th>Success criterion (pupil words)</th>\n<th>Khmer (pupil words)</th>\n<th>Picture or gesture cue</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>I can say Hello and Goodbye.</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំអាចនិយាយ Hello និង Goodbye។</td>\n<td>wave hand</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>I can say my name: I'm …</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំអាចប្រាប់ឈ្មោះខ្ញុំ៖ I'm …</td>\n<td>hand on chest</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>I know when to say Hello and when to say Goodbye.</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំដឹងថា ពេលណានិយាយ Hello ពេលណានិយាយ Goodbye។</td>\n<td>point to the door</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"1a15caa138\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"4\" data-ref=\"L.1 §2 ¶4\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.1-2-4\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §2 ¶4\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §2 ¶4 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶4</button><p data-body=\"1\">Draw the three cues on the board and point to them at the start and at the end of the lesson.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"a343dabcab\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §3 ¶0\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.1-3-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §3 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §3 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">RTTI rubric for the teacher</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"ee6f09a57a\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §3 ¶1\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.1-3-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §3 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §3 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">RTTI levels: <strong>R</strong> Reproduction (repeat what was taught), <strong>T1</strong> Training (use it in the practised activity), <strong>T2</strong> Transfer (use it in a new situation), <strong>I</strong> Insight (understand and explain why). The last column shows what to expect after this lesson: green = expected for all or most, yellow = with help, red = stretch goal, not expected yet.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"ceea7b25be\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.1 §3 ¶2\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.1-3-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §3 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §3 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Level</th>\n<th>What the pupil does</th>\n<th>Teacher looks for</th>\n<th>Feed back (say)</th>\n<th>Feed forward (say)</th>\n<th>Expected after this lesson</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>R – Reproduction</td>\n<td>Repeats Hello, Goodbye and I'm … after the teacher.</td>\n<td>Says the words in the choral drill, with the wave.</td>\n<td>\"You said Hello clearly!\"</td>\n<td>\"Now say it to your friend, without me.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">expected for all<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T1 – Training</td>\n<td>Answers \"What's your name?\" with I'm … in the ball toss.</td>\n<td>Answers alone when the ball comes, no whispering help.</td>\n<td>\"You answered by yourself.\"</td>\n<td>\"Next time, ask the question back: What's your name?\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">expected for most<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T2 – Transfer</td>\n<td>Greets a new person (visitor, puppet, head teacher) without a prompt.</td>\n<td>Greets someone at the door or a visitor on their own.</td>\n<td>\"You greeted our visitor – that is real English!\"</td>\n<td>\"Tomorrow, say Hello to a teacher at the gate.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-yellow\">with help<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"yellow\" title=\"Rated yellow\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated yellow)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>I – Insight</td>\n<td>Chooses Hello or Goodbye for a picture of arriving or leaving, and shows why (points to door, sun, bag).</td>\n<td>Explains in Khmer or with a gesture why it is Hello or Goodbye.</td>\n<td>\"You know why we say Goodbye here.\"</td>\n<td>\"Can you find another time we say Hello?\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-red\">stretch goal<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"red\" title=\"Rated red\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-xmark\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated red)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"5a2137d2b9\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §4 ¶0\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.1-4-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §4 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §4 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Target vocabulary</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"0128bdd2b7\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §4 ¶1\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.1-4-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §4 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §4 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶1</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>English</th>\n<th>Khmer</th>\n<th>Sound hint</th>\n<th>Picture idea</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>hello</td>\n<td>សួស្តី</td>\n<td>he-LOH</td>\n<td>child waving</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>goodbye</td>\n<td>លាហើយ</td>\n<td>good-BYE</td>\n<td>child waving at a door</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>name</td>\n<td>ឈ្មោះ</td>\n<td>naym</td>\n<td>name tag</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>teacher</td>\n<td>គ្រូ</td>\n<td>TEE-cher</td>\n<td>teacher at the board</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>friend</td>\n<td>មិត្តភក្តិ</td>\n<td>frend</td>\n<td>two children holding hands</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"f137c97e3d\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §5 ¶0\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.1-5-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §5 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §5 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Target language</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9742c2c24f\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §5 ¶1\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.1-5-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §5 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §5 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>Hello! / Hi!</li>\n<li>Goodbye! / Bye!</li>\n<li>What's your name?</li>\n<li>I'm (name).</li>\n<li>Dialogue: <strong>Sreymom:</strong> \"Hello! I'm Sreymom. What's your name?\" – <strong>Vichea:</strong> \"Hi! I'm Vichea.\"</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"1bd537eb12\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §6 ¶0\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.1-6-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §6 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §6 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Teacher-led lesson (one study hour, 40 min)</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b17223aafb\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §6 ¶1\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.1-6-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §6 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §6 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Warm-up and feed up (5 min):</strong> Say the learning goal and point to the success criteria cues. The teacher waves and says \"Hello!\" to the class until pupils wave back. Introduce the puppet: \"Hello! I'm Teddy.\"</li>\n<li><strong>Listen and say (8 min):</strong> Show the flashcards hello, goodbye, teacher, friend. Say each word three times with a gesture. Model \"What's your name? – I'm …\" with the puppet.</li>\n<li><strong>Pair work (10 min):</strong> Choral repetition: whole class, then boys, then girls, then rows. Then pairs: \"Hello! What's your name?\" – \"I'm …\".</li>\n<li><strong>Game (10 min):</strong> <em>Hello–Goodbye.</em> Teacher says \"Hello!\", pupils stand and wave. \"Goodbye!\", pupils sit and wave. Speed up.</li>\n<li><strong>Wrap-up and feed back (7 min):</strong> Point to each success criterion cue; pupils show thumbs up (I can), sideways (with help) or down (not yet). Give one feed-forward tip from the rubric. Sing a hello/goodbye song. Five pupils say \"I'm …\" to the puppet.</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"beb8224862\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §7 ¶0\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.1-7-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §7 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §7 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Self-paced app lesson</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"2b162ed6cb\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §7 ¶1\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.1-7-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §7 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §7 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Meet Teddy:</strong> the puppet waves; audio \"Hello! I'm Teddy.\" Khmer audio: \"Tap Teddy to say hello.\"</li>\n<li><strong>Listen and tap:</strong> two pictures (waving hello, waving goodbye). Audio \"Hello!\" – the pupil taps the right one. Right: \"Great!\" with a star. Wrong: the right picture wiggles and the word plays again.</li>\n<li><strong>Say it:</strong> the pupil presses the microphone and says \"Hello!\". The app plays it back next to the model.</li>\n<li><strong>My name:</strong> the pupil records \"I'm (name).\" The recording is saved for the parent or teacher to hear.</li>\n<li><strong>Song:</strong> hello song with tap-along actions.</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"07cd9e0db6\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §8 ¶0\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.1-8-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §8 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §8 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Activities without electronics</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9e38f9490f\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §8 ¶1\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.1-8-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §8 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §8 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Name chain:</strong> in rows, each pupil says \"I'm …\" and the next one says \"Hello, (name)!\".</li>\n<li><strong>Ball toss:</strong> a paper ball goes round; the catcher answers \"What's your name?\".</li>\n<li>Both work with 50 pupils by running them row by row at the same time.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"7f57b36be2\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §9 ¶0\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.1-9-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §9 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §9 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Differentiation</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"37b841320c\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §9 ¶1\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.1-9-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §9 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §9 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Need more support:</strong> may answer with just their name, or wave and say \"Hello\".</li>\n<li><strong>Ready for more:</strong> ask a friend \"What's your name?\" and introduce them: \"This is Sreymom.\"</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3bd9f3865f\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §10 ¶0\" data-sec=\"10\" id=\"p-L.1-10-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §10 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §10 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§10 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Quick assessment</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"400206d473\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §10 ¶1\" data-sec=\"10\" id=\"p-L.1-10-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §10 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §10 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§10 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">The teacher walks round during the ball toss and ticks on the checklist: says Hello / Goodbye, says \"I'm …\".</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9c2963b303\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.1 §10 ¶2\" data-sec=\"10\" id=\"p-L.1-10-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §10 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §10 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§10 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\">Record the RTTI level each pupil reached per success criterion in the progress checklist (R.1).</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"25c86f6a92\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §11 ¶0\" data-sec=\"11\" id=\"p-L.1-11-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §11 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §11 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§11 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Quiz</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"2289a536b9\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §11 ¶1\" data-sec=\"11\" id=\"p-L.1-11-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §11 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §11 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§11 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Each question checks one success criterion at one RTTI level. After <strong>Check</strong>, the quiz shows which levels the pupil reached for each criterion and what to try next.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"46f07fad6a\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.1 §11 ¶2\" data-sec=\"11\" id=\"p-L.1-11-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §11 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §11 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§11 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Success criterion</th>\n<th>RTTI level</th>\n<th>Question</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1 Hello and Goodbye</td>\n<td>R</td>\n<td>1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1 Hello and Goodbye</td>\n<td>T1</td>\n<td>2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2 My name</td>\n<td>R</td>\n<td>3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2 My name</td>\n<td>T2</td>\n<td>4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3 When to say which</td>\n<td>I</td>\n<td>5</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-quiz\" data-h=\"8e69109225\" data-kind=\"quiz\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.1 §11 ¶3\" data-sec=\"11\" id=\"p-L.1-11-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §11 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §11 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§11 ¶3</button><div aria-label=\"Quiz\" class=\"quiz\" data-body=\"1\" role=\"group\"><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"R\" data-q=\"1\" data-sc=\"SC1\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">1.</span> 👋 Teddy says \"Hello!\". Say it back.</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 1 · RTTI level R</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Hello!</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! You said Hello back. Criterion 1, level R.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Five!</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Five is a number. Listen again: Teddy says Hello.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Red!</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Red is a colour. Say Hello back to Teddy.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T1\" data-q=\"2\" data-sc=\"SC1\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">2.</span> 🧒 A new friend sits next to you in the morning. What do you say?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 1 · RTTI level T1</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Bye!</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Bye is for leaving. Your friend just came: say Hello.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Hi!</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! Hi is a short Hello. You used it with a friend.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Six!</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Six is a number. Greet your friend with Hello or Hi.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"R\" data-q=\"3\" data-sc=\"SC2\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">3.</span> The teacher asks \"What's your name?\". What do you say?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 2 · RTTI level R</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">I'm six.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That is your age. Say your name: I'm …</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">I'm Vichea.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! You said your name with I'm.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Hello, teacher.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That is a greeting. Now say your name: I'm …</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T2\" data-q=\"4\" data-sc=\"SC2\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">4.</span> 🧑‍🏫 A visitor comes to class. She says \"Hello! I'm Chantha. And you?\"</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 2 · RTTI level T2</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Hello! I'm Vichea.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Great! You greeted a new person and said your name.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Goodbye, Chantha.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">She just came. Say Hello and your name.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">I'm a pencil.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Use your own name: I'm Vichea.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"I\" data-q=\"5\" data-sc=\"SC3\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">5.</span> 🚪🎒 School is over. You take your bag and go to the door. Why do we say Goodbye?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 3 · RTTI level I</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Because we meet a friend.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">When we meet, we say Hello.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Because we are leaving.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! We say Goodbye when we leave.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Because it is red.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Colours do not tell us. Think: are you coming or leaving?</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><div class=\"quiz-actions\"><button class=\"btn btn-primary quiz-check\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-check-double\"></i> Check</button><button class=\"btn btn-outline-secondary quiz-retry\" hidden=\"\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-rotate-left\"></i> Try again</button><span aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-score\" role=\"status\"></span></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-rtti\" hidden=\"\"></div></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b8efd777f4\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §12 ¶0\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.1-12-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §12 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §12 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">CEFR cross-reference</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9ace50ee5c\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §12 ¶1\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.1-12-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §12 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §12 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Secondary reference only. Pre-A1 can-do statements adapted from the CEFR Companion Volume (2020); not an official CEFR test.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"a0a9ff7587\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.1 §12 ¶2\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.1-12-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §12 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §12 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶2</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>I can say <strong>Hello</strong> and <strong>Goodbye</strong> to my teacher and friends.</li>\n<li>I can say my name: <strong>I'm Vichea.</strong></li>\n<li>I can understand <strong>What's your name?</strong> when it is asked slowly with a gesture.</li>\n</ul></div>"}, {"id": "L.2", "title": "Lesson 2: Numbers 1–5 – How old are you?", "order": 2, "goals": ["MoEYS (draft lesson outcome): Pupils listen to and say the numbers 1–5 and say their age (Listening and Speaking).", "Success criterion 1: I can count from 1 to 5.", "Success criterion 2: I can say how old I am: I'm six.", "Success criterion 3: I can count things I have not seen before.", "Success criterion 4: I can find the letters A and B and say their sounds."], "metadata": {"status": "draft", "grade": "1", "subject": "Foreign Languages (English)", "moeys_reference": "Curriculum Framework of General Education and Technical Education (2016) – framework level verified; Grade 1 English syllabus wording to be checked", "cefr_cross_reference": "Pre-A1 (adapted, CEFR Companion Volume)", "duration": "one study hour (40 min)", "updated": "2026-11-05 (v1.3)"}, "file": "l2-numbers.md", "notes": ["<p>Verified in the 2016 Curriculum Framework: core competency 4.2 wording, the four subject components, Grade 1 time allocation (2 study hours a week, 40 minutes each), the assessment principles. The Function / Form / Vocabulary table and the activity names (Listen and say, Pair work, Letter practice) follow the official MoEYS English Grade 4 Student's Book (2020). NOT found: an official MoEYS Grade 1 English syllabus, its outcome wording or codes, and a MoEYS teacher guide with lesson steps. The lesson outcome above is our draft wording, not an official MoEYS outcome. See open-items.md.</p>\n", "<p>Khmer pupil-friendly sentences to be verified by a native speaker (Grade 1 level).</p>\n", "<p>Khmer numerals are standard, but the \"sound hint\" spellings should be tested with Khmer-speaking teachers: the \"th\" in three and the final \"v\" in five are hard for Khmer speakers.</p>\n", "<p>Letters follow the alphabet, two or three per lesson from Lesson 2 (A B, C D, E F G, H I J, K L M); the MoEYS English Grade 4 book also starts with \"The letters\" A B C D. The Khmer-friendly cues are approximate and must be checked by a Khmer-speaking teacher.</p>\n", "<p>CEFR Pre-A1 only describes recognising letters (and later spelling one's own name); it does not prescribe an order for teaching the alphabet. The letter order here is our choice (alphabetical, as in the MoEYS English Grade 4 book).</p>\n"], "blocks": [{"ref": "L.2 §0 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-0-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "80ee4acf65", "text": "Lesson 2: Numbers 1–5 – How old are you?"}, {"ref": "L.2 §0 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-0-1", "kind": "figure", "h": "da39a3ee5e", "text": ""}, {"ref": "L.2 §0 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.2-0-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "295704457c", "text": "Pupils count to five with fingers and objects, and learn to say how old they are. Six and seven are taught as \"age words\" only."}, {"ref": "L.2 §1 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-1-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "025eec04ab", "text": "MoEYS frame"}, {"ref": "L.2 §1 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-1-1", "kind": "table", "h": "bdd3a4a444", "text": "MoEYS reference This lesson Framework Curriculum Framework of General Education and Technical Education (MoEYS, 2016) Subject and grade Foreign Languages (English), Grade 1 (primary) Core competency 4.2 Foreign Languages: \"Learners can adequately use foreign languages for communication, research and continued study.\" Foreign Languages goals (section 5.6, quoted) \"Possess competencies in communication in all four skills (listening, speaking, reading and writing).\" \"Become life-long learners with creativity and confidence.\" Expected outcome for primary (quoted) \"Construct basic knowledge of Science, Information and Communications Technology (ICT) and Foreign Languages.\" Subject components Listening and Speaking in this lesson, plus first letter recognition (Reading and Writing come later) Study time Grade 1 has 2 study hours of Foreign Languages per week; one study hour is 40 minutes. This lesson is one study hour. Lesson learning outcome (draft) Pupils listen to and say the numbers 1–5 and say their age (Listening and Speaking). Assessment (framework section 8.1) Knowledge, skills, attitude and application skills – observed with the RTTI rubric below"}, {"ref": "L.2 §1 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.2-1-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "3119e881c9", "text": "Lesson syllabus (in the Function / Form / Vocabulary format of the MoEYS English Grade 4 textbook):"}, {"ref": "L.2 §1 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.2-1-3", "kind": "table", "h": "5815a95fde", "text": "Function Form Vocabulary Counting; asking and answering about age How many? – Three! – How old are you? – I'm six. one–five, six, seven, how old, how many; letters A, B"}, {"ref": "L.2 §2 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-2-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "27efc58195", "text": "Feed up: where are we going?"}, {"ref": "L.2 §2 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-2-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "3ed3594acc", "text": "Learning goal (say it at the start): Today we learn to count to five and say how old we are."}, {"ref": "L.2 §2 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.2-2-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "e81989a4ee", "text": "In Khmer: ថ្ងៃនេះ យើងរៀនរាប់ពីមួយដល់ប្រាំ និងប្រាប់អាយុរបស់យើង។"}, {"ref": "L.2 §2 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.2-2-3", "kind": "table", "h": "7e6596e81d", "text": "# Success criterion (pupil words) Khmer (pupil words) Picture or gesture cue 1 I can count from 1 to 5. ខ្ញុំអាចរាប់ពី 1 ដល់ 5។ show fingers 2 I can say how old I am: I'm six. ខ្ញុំអាចប្រាប់អាយុខ្ញុំ៖ I'm six។ hold up six fingers 3 I can count things I have not seen before. ខ្ញុំអាចរាប់របស់ថ្មីៗ។ point and count 4 I can find the letters A and B and say their sounds. ខ្ញុំអាចរកអក្សរ A និង B ហើយនិយាយសំឡេងរបស់វា។ point to the letter card"}, {"ref": "L.2 §2 ¶4", "anchor": "p-L.2-2-4", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "956b1a2721", "text": "Draw the four cues on the board and point to them at the start and at the end of the lesson."}, {"ref": "L.2 §3 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-3-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "a343dabcab", "text": "RTTI rubric for the teacher"}, {"ref": "L.2 §3 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-3-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "ee6f09a57a", "text": "RTTI levels: R Reproduction (repeat what was taught), T1 Training (use it in the practised activity), T2 Transfer (use it in a new situation), I Insight (understand and explain why). The last column shows what to expect after this lesson: green = expected for all or most, yellow = with help, red = stretch goal, not expected yet."}, {"ref": "L.2 §3 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.2-3-2", "kind": "table", "h": "386c949107", "text": "Level What the pupil does Teacher looks for Feed back (say) Feed forward (say) Expected after this lesson R – Reproduction Counts 1–5 with the class and the teacher. Says every number in the chant, fingers match. \"Your fingers and words matched!\" \"Now count alone, slowly.\" expected for all (rated green) T1 – Training Shows the right number of fingers when the teacher says a number in random order. Fingers right without looking at a neighbour. \"You heard the number and showed it.\" \"Next, say the number when I show fingers.\" expected for most (rated green) T2 – Transfer Counts new objects (stones, pupils in a row) and says how many. Counts a new set out loud and gives the total. \"You counted the stones by yourself.\" \"At home, count the mangoes or your shoes.\" with help (rated yellow) I – Insight Notices that the last number said is \"how many\", and that age is also a number. Answers \"How many?\" with the last number, or links age to fingers. \"You know the last number tells how many.\" \"How many people are in your family?\" stretch goal (rated red)"}, {"ref": "L.2 §3 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.2-3-3", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "9c5dfe92f5", "text": "Letters (criterion 4):"}, {"ref": "L.2 §3 ¶4", "anchor": "p-L.2-3-4", "kind": "table", "h": "01daeeccfa", "text": "Level What the pupil does Teacher looks for Feed back (say) Feed forward (say) Expected after this lesson R – Reproduction Says the letter sounds after the teacher. Clear sound, not the letter name only. \"You said the A sound well!\" \"Now say it when you see the card.\" expected for all (rated green) T1 – Training Points to the right letter card when the teacher says a sound. Points without looking at a neighbour. \"You found A by its sound.\" \"Next, find the letter in a picture word.\" expected for most (rated green) T2 – Transfer Finds the letter at the start of a new word or a name card. Spots the letter in a word not taught today. \"You found B in a new word!\" \"Look for B in your friends' names.\" stretch goal (rated red)"}, {"ref": "L.2 §4 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-4-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "5a2137d2b9", "text": "Target vocabulary"}, {"ref": "L.2 §4 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-4-1", "kind": "table", "h": "01c58824d1", "text": "English Khmer Sound hint Picture idea one មួយ wun one mango two ពីរ too two mangoes three បី three three mangoes four បួន for four mangoes five ប្រាំ fiyv five mangoes six ប្រាំមួយ siks birthday cake, six candles seven ប្រាំពីរ SEV-en birthday cake, seven candles"}, {"ref": "L.2 §5 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-5-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "f137c97e3d", "text": "Target language"}, {"ref": "L.2 §5 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-5-1", "kind": "list", "h": "a6676799bc", "text": "One, two, three, four, five. How old are you? – I'm six. / I'm seven. How many? – Three!"}, {"ref": "L.2 §6 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-6-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "3f5171041f", "text": "The letters"}, {"ref": "L.2 §6 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-6-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "b5d6d64121", "text": "Letter recognition and sounds only – no writing yet. Pupils see the capital and small letter, hear the sound and match it to a picture."}, {"ref": "L.2 §6 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.2-6-2", "kind": "table", "h": "7110c92086", "text": "Letter Sound Picture word Khmer-friendly cue A a /æ/ – short, mouth wide open 🍎 apple no Khmer letter is the same: open the mouth wide and say it short B b /b/ ⚽ ball like ប"}, {"ref": "L.2 §7 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-7-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "1bd537eb12", "text": "Teacher-led lesson (one study hour, 40 min)"}, {"ref": "L.2 §7 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-7-1", "kind": "list", "h": "944fcc6b3e", "text": "Warm-up and feed up (5 min): Say the learning goal and point to the success criteria cues. Hello song. Puppet asks five pupils \"What's your name?\". Listen and say (8 min): Count fingers 1–5 slowly. Hold up mangoes, stones or pencils and count them together. Pair work (8 min): Teacher shows fingers, class shouts the number. Then pupils show fingers in pairs. Letter practice (5 min): Show the letter cards A and B (capital and small). Say the sound and the picture word: A – apple, B – ball. Pupils repeat, draw the letter in the air, and point to the right card when they hear the sound. No writing yet. Game (8 min): Jump and count. Teacher says \"Three!\", pupils jump three times. Then clap, stamp, nod. Wrap-up and feed back (6 min): Point to each success criterion cue; pupils show thumbs up (I can), sideways (with help) or down (not yet). Give one feed-forward tip from the rubric. Puppet asks \"How old are you?\" – class answers together, then a few pupils alone. Goodbye song."}, {"ref": "L.2 §8 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-8-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "beb8224862", "text": "Self-paced app lesson"}, {"ref": "L.2 §8 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-8-1", "kind": "list", "h": "aa31e24b1b", "text": "Count with me: mangoes appear one by one with audio \"one, two, three…\". How many?: a picture of three mangoes; the pupil taps 1, 2, 3, 4 or 5. Feedback: \"Yes, three!\" or the mangoes are counted again aloud. Drag: drag four balls into a basket when the audio says \"four\". Say it: record \"I'm six\" (or seven) after a cake with candles. Song: a counting song with finger animation."}, {"ref": "L.2 §9 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-9-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "07cd9e0db6", "text": "Activities without electronics"}, {"ref": "L.2 §9 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-9-1", "kind": "list", "h": "4ec498c0e5", "text": "Finger flash: whole class, no materials. Number groups: teacher says \"Three!\", pupils make groups of three. Works in a yard with 50 pupils. Chalk dots: pupils come to the board and draw the number of dots the class says."}, {"ref": "L.2 §10 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-10-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "7f57b36be2", "text": "Differentiation"}, {"ref": "L.2 §10 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-10-1", "kind": "list", "h": "5ba3b3b63a", "text": "Need more support: show fingers only, without speaking. Ready for more: count backwards from five, or count objects for the class."}, {"ref": "L.2 §11 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-11-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "3bd9f3865f", "text": "Quick assessment"}, {"ref": "L.2 §11 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-11-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "673818f161", "text": "Teacher shows 1–5 fingers in random order to small groups and ticks who can name them."}, {"ref": "L.2 §11 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.2-11-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "9c2963b303", "text": "Record the RTTI level each pupil reached per success criterion in the progress checklist (R.1)."}, {"ref": "L.2 §12 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-12-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "25c86f6a92", "text": "Quiz"}, {"ref": "L.2 §12 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-12-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "2289a536b9", "text": "Each question checks one success criterion at one RTTI level. After Check , the quiz shows which levels the pupil reached for each criterion and what to try next."}, {"ref": "L.2 §12 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.2-12-2", "kind": "table", "h": "c666a8afe4", "text": "Success criterion RTTI level Question 1 Count 1–5 R 1 1 Count 1–5 T1 2 2 Say my age T1 3 3 Count new things T2 4 3 Count new things I 5 4 Letters A and B R 6 4 Letters A and B T1 7"}, {"ref": "L.2 §12 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.2-12-3", "kind": "quiz", "h": "f6478a326e", "text": "1. Listen: \"one, two, three, …\". What comes next? Criterion 1 · RTTI level R four Yes! One, two, three, four. five Five comes after four. Count again: one, two, three, … two Two came already. Count again: one, two, three, … 2. ✋ How many fingers? Criterion 1 · RTTI level T1 four Count again – every finger and the thumb. five Yes! A whole hand is five. one Look again: the whole hand. 3. The puppet asks \"How old are you?\". You are six. Criterion 2 · RTTI level T1 I'm six. Yes! You said your age. I'm Chantha. That is your name. Say your age: I'm six. Hello! That is a greeting. Say your age: I'm six. 4. 🪨🪨🪨🪨 How many stones? Criterion 3 · RTTI level T2 three Point and count each stone again. four Yes! You counted new things: four stones. five Point and count each stone again. 5. 🥭🥭 You count \"one, two\". How many mangoes are there? Criterion 3 · RTTI level I one The last number we say tells how many. two Yes! The last number tells how many. three We stopped at two. The last number tells how many. 6. 🍎 Which letter does \"apple\" start with? Criterion 4 · RTTI level R A Yes! \"apple\" starts with A. C Listen again: \"apple\" – the first sound is A. D Listen again: \"apple\" – the first sound is A. 7. This is the letter B. Which picture starts with B? Criterion 4 · RTTI level T1 🍎 apple That starts with A. Find the B sound. ⚽ ball Yes! \"ball\" starts with B. 🐱 cat That starts with C. Find the B sound. Check Try again"}, {"ref": "L.2 §13 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-13-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "b8efd777f4", "text": "CEFR cross-reference"}, {"ref": "L.2 §13 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-13-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "9ace50ee5c", "text": "Secondary reference only. Pre-A1 can-do statements adapted from the CEFR Companion Volume (2020); not an official CEFR test."}, {"ref": "L.2 §13 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.2-13-2", "kind": "list", "h": "be424a8047", "text": "I can count from 1 to 5 in English. I can show a number with my fingers when I hear it. I can answer How old are you? with I'm six. or I'm seven. I can recognise the letters A and B and say their sounds."}], "html": "<div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"80ee4acf65\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §0 ¶0\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.2-0-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §0 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §0 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶0</button><h1 data-body=\"1\">Lesson 2: Numbers 1–5 – How old are you?</h1></div><div class=\"blk blk-figure fl-full\" data-h=\"da39a3ee5e\" data-kind=\"figure\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §0 ¶1\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.2-0-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §0 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §0 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶1</button><figure class=\"fig fig-full\" data-body=\"1\" data-marker=\"full\"><button aria-label=\"Enlarge image: Numbers one to five shown as dots\" class=\"img-zoom\" type=\"button\"><img alt=\"Numbers one to five shown as dots\" data-src=\"images/fingers-1-5.svg\" loading=\"eager\" src=\"assets/images/images/fingers-1-5.svg\"/></button></figure></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"295704457c\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.2 §0 ¶2\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.2-0-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §0 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §0 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\">Pupils count to five with fingers and objects, and learn to say how old they are. Six and seven are taught as \"age words\" only.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"025eec04ab\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §1 ¶0\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.2-1-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §1 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §1 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">MoEYS frame</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"bdd3a4a444\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §1 ¶1\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.2-1-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §1 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §1 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶1</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>MoEYS reference</th>\n<th>This lesson</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Framework</td>\n<td>Curriculum Framework of General Education and Technical Education (MoEYS, 2016)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Subject and grade</td>\n<td>Foreign Languages (English), Grade 1 (primary)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Core competency</td>\n<td>4.2 Foreign Languages: \"Learners can adequately use foreign languages for communication, research and continued study.\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Foreign Languages goals (section 5.6, quoted)</td>\n<td>\"Possess competencies in communication in all four skills (listening, speaking, reading and writing).\" \"Become life-long learners with creativity and confidence.\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Expected outcome for primary (quoted)</td>\n<td>\"Construct basic knowledge of Science, Information and Communications Technology (ICT) and Foreign Languages.\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Subject components</td>\n<td>Listening and Speaking in this lesson, plus first letter recognition (Reading and Writing come later)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Study time</td>\n<td>Grade 1 has 2 study hours of Foreign Languages per week; one study hour is 40 minutes. This lesson is one study hour.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Lesson learning outcome (draft)</td>\n<td>Pupils listen to and say the numbers 1–5 and say their age (Listening and Speaking).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Assessment (framework section 8.1)</td>\n<td>Knowledge, skills, attitude and application skills – observed with the RTTI rubric below</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3119e881c9\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.2 §1 ¶2\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.2-1-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §1 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §1 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>Lesson syllabus</strong> (in the Function / Form / Vocabulary format of the MoEYS English Grade 4 textbook):</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"5815a95fde\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.2 §1 ¶3\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.2-1-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §1 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §1 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶3</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Function</th>\n<th>Form</th>\n<th>Vocabulary</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Counting; asking and answering about age</td>\n<td>How many? – Three! – How old are you? – I'm six.</td>\n<td>one–five, six, seven, how old, how many; letters A, B</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"27efc58195\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §2 ¶0\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.2-2-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §2 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §2 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Feed up: where are we going?</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3ed3594acc\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §2 ¶1\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.2-2-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §2 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §2 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>Learning goal (say it at the start):</strong> Today we learn to count to five and say how old we are.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"e81989a4ee\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.2 §2 ¶2\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.2-2-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §2 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §2 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>In Khmer:</strong> ថ្ងៃនេះ យើងរៀនរាប់ពីមួយដល់ប្រាំ និងប្រាប់អាយុរបស់យើង។</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"7e6596e81d\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.2 §2 ¶3\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.2-2-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §2 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §2 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶3</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>#</th>\n<th>Success criterion (pupil words)</th>\n<th>Khmer (pupil words)</th>\n<th>Picture or gesture cue</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>I can count from 1 to 5.</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំអាចរាប់ពី 1 ដល់ 5។</td>\n<td>show fingers</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>I can say how old I am: I'm six.</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំអាចប្រាប់អាយុខ្ញុំ៖ I'm six។</td>\n<td>hold up six fingers</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>I can count things I have not seen before.</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំអាចរាប់របស់ថ្មីៗ។</td>\n<td>point and count</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>I can find the letters A and B and say their sounds.</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំអាចរកអក្សរ A និង B ហើយនិយាយសំឡេងរបស់វា។</td>\n<td>point to the letter card</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"956b1a2721\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"4\" data-ref=\"L.2 §2 ¶4\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.2-2-4\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §2 ¶4\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §2 ¶4 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶4</button><p data-body=\"1\">Draw the four cues on the board and point to them at the start and at the end of the lesson.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"a343dabcab\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §3 ¶0\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.2-3-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §3 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §3 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">RTTI rubric for the teacher</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"ee6f09a57a\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §3 ¶1\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.2-3-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §3 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §3 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">RTTI levels: <strong>R</strong> Reproduction (repeat what was taught), <strong>T1</strong> Training (use it in the practised activity), <strong>T2</strong> Transfer (use it in a new situation), <strong>I</strong> Insight (understand and explain why). The last column shows what to expect after this lesson: green = expected for all or most, yellow = with help, red = stretch goal, not expected yet.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"386c949107\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.2 §3 ¶2\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.2-3-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §3 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §3 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Level</th>\n<th>What the pupil does</th>\n<th>Teacher looks for</th>\n<th>Feed back (say)</th>\n<th>Feed forward (say)</th>\n<th>Expected after this lesson</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>R – Reproduction</td>\n<td>Counts 1–5 with the class and the teacher.</td>\n<td>Says every number in the chant, fingers match.</td>\n<td>\"Your fingers and words matched!\"</td>\n<td>\"Now count alone, slowly.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">expected for all<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T1 – Training</td>\n<td>Shows the right number of fingers when the teacher says a number in random order.</td>\n<td>Fingers right without looking at a neighbour.</td>\n<td>\"You heard the number and showed it.\"</td>\n<td>\"Next, say the number when I show fingers.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">expected for most<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T2 – Transfer</td>\n<td>Counts new objects (stones, pupils in a row) and says how many.</td>\n<td>Counts a new set out loud and gives the total.</td>\n<td>\"You counted the stones by yourself.\"</td>\n<td>\"At home, count the mangoes or your shoes.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-yellow\">with help<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"yellow\" title=\"Rated yellow\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated yellow)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>I – Insight</td>\n<td>Notices that the last number said is \"how many\", and that age is also a number.</td>\n<td>Answers \"How many?\" with the last number, or links age to fingers.</td>\n<td>\"You know the last number tells how many.\"</td>\n<td>\"How many people are in your family?\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-red\">stretch goal<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"red\" title=\"Rated red\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-xmark\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated red)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9c5dfe92f5\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.2 §3 ¶3\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.2-3-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §3 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §3 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶3</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>Letters (criterion 4):</strong></p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"01daeeccfa\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"4\" data-ref=\"L.2 §3 ¶4\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.2-3-4\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §3 ¶4\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §3 ¶4 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶4</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Level</th>\n<th>What the pupil does</th>\n<th>Teacher looks for</th>\n<th>Feed back (say)</th>\n<th>Feed forward (say)</th>\n<th>Expected after this lesson</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>R – Reproduction</td>\n<td>Says the letter sounds after the teacher.</td>\n<td>Clear sound, not the letter name only.</td>\n<td>\"You said the A sound well!\"</td>\n<td>\"Now say it when you see the card.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">expected for all<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T1 – Training</td>\n<td>Points to the right letter card when the teacher says a sound.</td>\n<td>Points without looking at a neighbour.</td>\n<td>\"You found A by its sound.\"</td>\n<td>\"Next, find the letter in a picture word.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">expected for most<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T2 – Transfer</td>\n<td>Finds the letter at the start of a new word or a name card.</td>\n<td>Spots the letter in a word not taught today.</td>\n<td>\"You found B in a new word!\"</td>\n<td>\"Look for B in your friends' names.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-red\">stretch goal<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"red\" title=\"Rated red\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-xmark\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated red)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"5a2137d2b9\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §4 ¶0\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.2-4-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §4 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §4 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Target vocabulary</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"01c58824d1\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §4 ¶1\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.2-4-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §4 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §4 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶1</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>English</th>\n<th>Khmer</th>\n<th>Sound hint</th>\n<th>Picture idea</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>one</td>\n<td>មួយ</td>\n<td>wun</td>\n<td>one mango</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>two</td>\n<td>ពីរ</td>\n<td>too</td>\n<td>two mangoes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>three</td>\n<td>បី</td>\n<td>three</td>\n<td>three mangoes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>four</td>\n<td>បួន</td>\n<td>for</td>\n<td>four mangoes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>five</td>\n<td>ប្រាំ</td>\n<td>fiyv</td>\n<td>five mangoes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>six</td>\n<td>ប្រាំមួយ</td>\n<td>siks</td>\n<td>birthday cake, six candles</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>seven</td>\n<td>ប្រាំពីរ</td>\n<td>SEV-en</td>\n<td>birthday cake, seven candles</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"f137c97e3d\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §5 ¶0\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.2-5-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §5 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §5 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Target language</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"a6676799bc\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §5 ¶1\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.2-5-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §5 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §5 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>One, two, three, four, five.</li>\n<li>How old are you? – I'm six. / I'm seven.</li>\n<li>How many? – Three!</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3f5171041f\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §6 ¶0\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.2-6-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §6 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §6 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">The letters</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b5d6d64121\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §6 ¶1\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.2-6-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §6 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §6 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Letter recognition and sounds only – no writing yet. Pupils see the capital and small letter, hear the sound and match it to a picture.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"7110c92086\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.2 §6 ¶2\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.2-6-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §6 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §6 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Letter</th>\n<th>Sound</th>\n<th>Picture word</th>\n<th>Khmer-friendly cue</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>A a</td>\n<td>/æ/ – short, mouth wide open</td>\n<td>🍎 apple</td>\n<td>no Khmer letter is the same: open the mouth wide and say it short</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>B b</td>\n<td>/b/</td>\n<td>⚽ ball</td>\n<td>like ប</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"1bd537eb12\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §7 ¶0\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.2-7-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §7 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §7 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Teacher-led lesson (one study hour, 40 min)</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"944fcc6b3e\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §7 ¶1\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.2-7-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §7 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §7 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Warm-up and feed up (5 min):</strong> Say the learning goal and point to the success criteria cues. Hello song. Puppet asks five pupils \"What's your name?\".</li>\n<li><strong>Listen and say (8 min):</strong> Count fingers 1–5 slowly. Hold up mangoes, stones or pencils and count them together.</li>\n<li><strong>Pair work (8 min):</strong> Teacher shows fingers, class shouts the number. Then pupils show fingers in pairs.</li>\n<li><strong>Letter practice (5 min):</strong> Show the letter cards A and B (capital and small). Say the sound and the picture word: A – apple, B – ball. Pupils repeat, draw the letter in the air, and point to the right card when they hear the sound. No writing yet.</li>\n<li><strong>Game (8 min):</strong> <em>Jump and count.</em> Teacher says \"Three!\", pupils jump three times. Then clap, stamp, nod.</li>\n<li><strong>Wrap-up and feed back (6 min):</strong> Point to each success criterion cue; pupils show thumbs up (I can), sideways (with help) or down (not yet). Give one feed-forward tip from the rubric. Puppet asks \"How old are you?\" – class answers together, then a few pupils alone. Goodbye song.</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"beb8224862\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §8 ¶0\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.2-8-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §8 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §8 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Self-paced app lesson</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"aa31e24b1b\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §8 ¶1\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.2-8-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §8 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §8 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Count with me:</strong> mangoes appear one by one with audio \"one, two, three…\".</li>\n<li><strong>How many?:</strong> a picture of three mangoes; the pupil taps 1, 2, 3, 4 or 5. Feedback: \"Yes, three!\" or the mangoes are counted again aloud.</li>\n<li><strong>Drag:</strong> drag four balls into a basket when the audio says \"four\".</li>\n<li><strong>Say it:</strong> record \"I'm six\" (or seven) after a cake with candles.</li>\n<li><strong>Song:</strong> a counting song with finger animation.</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"07cd9e0db6\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §9 ¶0\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.2-9-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §9 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §9 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Activities without electronics</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"4ec498c0e5\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §9 ¶1\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.2-9-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §9 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §9 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Finger flash:</strong> whole class, no materials.</li>\n<li><strong>Number groups:</strong> teacher says \"Three!\", pupils make groups of three. Works in a yard with 50 pupils.</li>\n<li><strong>Chalk dots:</strong> pupils come to the board and draw the number of dots the class says.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"7f57b36be2\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §10 ¶0\" data-sec=\"10\" id=\"p-L.2-10-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §10 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §10 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§10 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Differentiation</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"5ba3b3b63a\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §10 ¶1\" data-sec=\"10\" id=\"p-L.2-10-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §10 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §10 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§10 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Need more support:</strong> show fingers only, without speaking.</li>\n<li><strong>Ready for more:</strong> count backwards from five, or count objects for the class.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3bd9f3865f\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §11 ¶0\" data-sec=\"11\" id=\"p-L.2-11-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §11 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §11 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§11 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Quick assessment</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"673818f161\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §11 ¶1\" data-sec=\"11\" id=\"p-L.2-11-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §11 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §11 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§11 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Teacher shows 1–5 fingers in random order to small groups and ticks who can name them.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9c2963b303\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.2 §11 ¶2\" data-sec=\"11\" id=\"p-L.2-11-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §11 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §11 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§11 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\">Record the RTTI level each pupil reached per success criterion in the progress checklist (R.1).</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"25c86f6a92\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §12 ¶0\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.2-12-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §12 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §12 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Quiz</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"2289a536b9\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §12 ¶1\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.2-12-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §12 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §12 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Each question checks one success criterion at one RTTI level. After <strong>Check</strong>, the quiz shows which levels the pupil reached for each criterion and what to try next.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"c666a8afe4\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.2 §12 ¶2\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.2-12-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §12 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §12 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Success criterion</th>\n<th>RTTI level</th>\n<th>Question</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1 Count 1–5</td>\n<td>R</td>\n<td>1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1 Count 1–5</td>\n<td>T1</td>\n<td>2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2 Say my age</td>\n<td>T1</td>\n<td>3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3 Count new things</td>\n<td>T2</td>\n<td>4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3 Count new things</td>\n<td>I</td>\n<td>5</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4 Letters A and B</td>\n<td>R</td>\n<td>6</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4 Letters A and B</td>\n<td>T1</td>\n<td>7</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-quiz\" data-h=\"f6478a326e\" data-kind=\"quiz\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.2 §12 ¶3\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.2-12-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §12 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §12 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶3</button><div aria-label=\"Quiz\" class=\"quiz\" data-body=\"1\" role=\"group\"><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"R\" data-q=\"1\" data-sc=\"SC1\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">1.</span> Listen: \"one, two, three, …\". What comes next?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 1 · RTTI level R</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">four</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! One, two, three, four.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">five</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Five comes after four. Count again: one, two, three, …</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">two</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Two came already. Count again: one, two, three, …</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T1\" data-q=\"2\" data-sc=\"SC1\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">2.</span> ✋ How many fingers?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 1 · RTTI level T1</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">four</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Count again – every finger and the thumb.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">five</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! A whole hand is five.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">one</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Look again: the whole hand.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T1\" data-q=\"3\" data-sc=\"SC2\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">3.</span> The puppet asks \"How old are you?\". You are six.</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 2 · RTTI level T1</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">I'm six.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! You said your age.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">I'm Chantha.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That is your name. Say your age: I'm six.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Hello!</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That is a greeting. Say your age: I'm six.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T2\" data-q=\"4\" data-sc=\"SC3\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">4.</span> 🪨🪨🪨🪨 How many stones?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 3 · RTTI level T2</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">three</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Point and count each stone again.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">four</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! You counted new things: four stones.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">five</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Point and count each stone again.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"I\" data-q=\"5\" data-sc=\"SC3\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">5.</span> 🥭🥭 You count \"one, two\". How many mangoes are there?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 3 · RTTI level I</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">one</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">The last number we say tells how many.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">two</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! The last number tells how many.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">three</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">We stopped at two. The last number tells how many.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"R\" data-q=\"6\" data-sc=\"SC4\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">6.</span> 🍎 Which letter does \"apple\" start with?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 4 · RTTI level R</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">A</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! \"apple\" starts with A.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">C</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Listen again: \"apple\" – the first sound is A.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">D</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Listen again: \"apple\" – the first sound is A.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T1\" data-q=\"7\" data-sc=\"SC4\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">7.</span> This is the letter B. Which picture starts with B?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 4 · RTTI level T1</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">🍎 apple</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That starts with A. Find the B sound.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">⚽ ball</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! \"ball\" starts with B.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">🐱 cat</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That starts with C. Find the B sound.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><div class=\"quiz-actions\"><button class=\"btn btn-primary quiz-check\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-check-double\"></i> Check</button><button class=\"btn btn-outline-secondary quiz-retry\" hidden=\"\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-rotate-left\"></i> Try again</button><span aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-score\" role=\"status\"></span></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-rtti\" hidden=\"\"></div></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b8efd777f4\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §13 ¶0\" data-sec=\"13\" id=\"p-L.2-13-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §13 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §13 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§13 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">CEFR cross-reference</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9ace50ee5c\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §13 ¶1\" data-sec=\"13\" id=\"p-L.2-13-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §13 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §13 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§13 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Secondary reference only. Pre-A1 can-do statements adapted from the CEFR Companion Volume (2020); not an official CEFR test.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"be424a8047\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.2 §13 ¶2\" data-sec=\"13\" id=\"p-L.2-13-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §13 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §13 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§13 ¶2</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>I can count from 1 to 5 in English.</li>\n<li>I can show a number with my fingers when I hear it.</li>\n<li>I can answer <strong>How old are you?</strong> with <strong>I'm six.</strong> or <strong>I'm seven.</strong></li>\n<li>I can recognise the letters A and B and say their sounds.</li>\n</ul></div>"}, {"id": "L.3", "title": "Lesson 3: Colours", "order": 3, "goals": ["MoEYS (draft lesson outcome): Pupils recognise and name four colours and respond to simple instructions (Listening and Speaking).", "Success criterion 1: I can say red, blue, yellow and green.", "Success criterion 2: I can touch a colour when I hear it.", "Success criterion 3: I can find colours on new things around me.", "Success criterion 4: I can find the letters C and D and say their sounds."], "metadata": {"status": "draft", "grade": "1", "subject": "Foreign Languages (English)", "moeys_reference": "Curriculum Framework of General Education and Technical Education (2016) – framework level verified; Grade 1 English syllabus wording to be checked", "cefr_cross_reference": "Pre-A1 (adapted, CEFR Companion Volume)", "duration": "one study hour (40 min)", "updated": "2026-11-05 (v1.3)"}, "file": "l3-colours.md", "notes": ["<p>Verified in the 2016 Curriculum Framework: core competency 4.2 wording, the four subject components, Grade 1 time allocation (2 study hours a week, 40 minutes each), the assessment principles. The Function / Form / Vocabulary table and the activity names (Listen and say, Pair work, Letter practice) follow the official MoEYS English Grade 4 Student's Book (2020). NOT found: an official MoEYS Grade 1 English syllabus, its outcome wording or codes, and a MoEYS teacher guide with lesson steps. The lesson outcome above is our draft wording, not an official MoEYS outcome. See open-items.md.</p>\n", "<p>Khmer pupil-friendly sentences to be verified by a native speaker (Grade 1 level).</p>\n", "<p>Khmer to be verified by a native speaker: ខៀវ can mean both blue and green in some everyday speech, so check how teachers explain the difference to young children.</p>\n", "<p>Letters follow the alphabet, two or three per lesson from Lesson 2 (A B, C D, E F G, H I J, K L M); the MoEYS English Grade 4 book also starts with \"The letters\" A B C D. The Khmer-friendly cues are approximate and must be checked by a Khmer-speaking teacher.</p>\n", "<p>CEFR Pre-A1 only describes recognising letters (and later spelling one's own name); it does not prescribe an order for teaching the alphabet. The letter order here is our choice (alphabetical, as in the MoEYS English Grade 4 book).</p>\n"], "blocks": [{"ref": "L.3 §0 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-0-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "336aa5250e", "text": "Lesson 3: Colours"}, {"ref": "L.3 §0 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-0-1", "kind": "figure", "h": "da39a3ee5e", "text": ""}, {"ref": "L.3 §0 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.3-0-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "c5d265dfb9", "text": "Pupils learn four colours and use them with things they already know: numbers and classroom things."}, {"ref": "L.3 §1 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-1-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "025eec04ab", "text": "MoEYS frame"}, {"ref": "L.3 §1 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-1-1", "kind": "table", "h": "537f52d094", "text": "MoEYS reference This lesson Framework Curriculum Framework of General Education and Technical Education (MoEYS, 2016) Subject and grade Foreign Languages (English), Grade 1 (primary) Core competency 4.2 Foreign Languages: \"Learners can adequately use foreign languages for communication, research and continued study.\" Foreign Languages goals (section 5.6, quoted) \"Possess competencies in communication in all four skills (listening, speaking, reading and writing).\" \"Become life-long learners with creativity and confidence.\" Expected outcome for primary (quoted) \"Construct basic knowledge of Science, Information and Communications Technology (ICT) and Foreign Languages.\" Subject components Listening and Speaking in this lesson, plus first letter recognition (Reading and Writing come later) Study time Grade 1 has 2 study hours of Foreign Languages per week; one study hour is 40 minutes. This lesson is one study hour. Lesson learning outcome (draft) Pupils recognise and name four colours and respond to simple instructions (Listening and Speaking). Assessment (framework section 8.1) Knowledge, skills, attitude and application skills – observed with the RTTI rubric below"}, {"ref": "L.3 §1 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.3-1-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "3119e881c9", "text": "Lesson syllabus (in the Function / Form / Vocabulary format of the MoEYS English Grade 4 textbook):"}, {"ref": "L.3 §1 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.3-1-3", "kind": "table", "h": "71140a8f11", "text": "Function Form Vocabulary Naming colours What colour is it? – It's red. red, blue, yellow, green; letters C, D"}, {"ref": "L.3 §2 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-2-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "27efc58195", "text": "Feed up: where are we going?"}, {"ref": "L.3 §2 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-2-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "7f85d52461", "text": "Learning goal (say it at the start): Today we learn the colours red, blue, yellow and green."}, {"ref": "L.3 §2 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.3-2-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "8e7ff9d5cf", "text": "In Khmer: ថ្ងៃនេះ យើងរៀនពណ៌ក្រហម ខៀវ លឿង និងបៃតង។"}, {"ref": "L.3 §2 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.3-2-3", "kind": "table", "h": "84433f5b4e", "text": "# Success criterion (pupil words) Khmer (pupil words) Picture or gesture cue 1 I can say red, blue, yellow and green. ខ្ញុំអាចនិយាយ red, blue, yellow, green។ hold up a colour card 2 I can touch a colour when I hear it. ខ្ញុំអាចប៉ះពណ៌ដែលខ្ញុំឮ។ touch your shirt 3 I can find colours on new things around me. ខ្ញុំអាចរកពណ៌នៅលើរបស់ផ្សេងៗជុំវិញខ្ញុំ។ look around, point 4 I can find the letters C and D and say their sounds. ខ្ញុំអាចរកអក្សរ C និង D ហើយនិយាយសំឡេងរបស់វា។ point to the letter card"}, {"ref": "L.3 §2 ¶4", "anchor": "p-L.3-2-4", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "956b1a2721", "text": "Draw the four cues on the board and point to them at the start and at the end of the lesson."}, {"ref": "L.3 §3 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-3-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "a343dabcab", "text": "RTTI rubric for the teacher"}, {"ref": "L.3 §3 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-3-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "ee6f09a57a", "text": "RTTI levels: R Reproduction (repeat what was taught), T1 Training (use it in the practised activity), T2 Transfer (use it in a new situation), I Insight (understand and explain why). The last column shows what to expect after this lesson: green = expected for all or most, yellow = with help, red = stretch goal, not expected yet."}, {"ref": "L.3 §3 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.3-3-2", "kind": "table", "h": "65846f37a9", "text": "Level What the pupil does Teacher looks for Feed back (say) Feed forward (say) Expected after this lesson R – Reproduction Repeats the four colour words with the cards. Says the word as the card is shown. \"You said all four colours!\" \"Now say the colour before I do.\" expected for all (rated green) T1 – Training Touches the right colour in \"Touch something …!\" Moves to the right colour without copying. \"You heard blue and found blue.\" \"Next, tell a friend what to touch.\" expected for most (rated green) T2 – Transfer Names colours of new things (fruit, clothes, a flag). Says \"Green!\" about something not used in the lesson. \"You found a colour we did not practise.\" \"On your way home, find three red things.\" with help (rated yellow) I – Insight Explains that the same thing can have different colours (a red pencil, a blue pencil). Sorts objects by colour, not by kind, and says why. \"You sorted by colour – smart!\" \"Can you sort the pencils another way?\" stretch goal (rated red)"}, {"ref": "L.3 §3 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.3-3-3", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "9c5dfe92f5", "text": "Letters (criterion 4):"}, {"ref": "L.3 §3 ¶4", "anchor": "p-L.3-3-4", "kind": "table", "h": "72dc0de0b3", "text": "Level What the pupil does Teacher looks for Feed back (say) Feed forward (say) Expected after this lesson R – Reproduction Says the letter sounds after the teacher. Clear sound, not the letter name only. \"You said the C sound well!\" \"Now say it when you see the card.\" expected for all (rated green) T1 – Training Points to the right letter card when the teacher says a sound. Points without looking at a neighbour. \"You found C by its sound.\" \"Next, find the letter in a picture word.\" expected for most (rated green) T2 – Transfer Finds the letter at the start of a new word or a name card. Spots the letter in a word not taught today. \"You found D in a new word!\" \"Look for D in your friends' names.\" stretch goal (rated red)"}, {"ref": "L.3 §4 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-4-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "5a2137d2b9", "text": "Target vocabulary"}, {"ref": "L.3 §4 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-4-1", "kind": "table", "h": "e4031d461f", "text": "English Khmer Sound hint Picture idea red ក្រហម red red balloon blue ខៀវ bloo blue balloon yellow លឿង YEL-oh yellow balloon green បៃតង green green balloon colour ពណ៌ KUL-er paint box"}, {"ref": "L.3 §5 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-5-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "f137c97e3d", "text": "Target language"}, {"ref": "L.3 §5 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-5-1", "kind": "list", "h": "952b2b086b", "text": "What colour is it? – Red. Touch something blue! Two yellow balloons. (review of numbers)"}, {"ref": "L.3 §6 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-6-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "3f5171041f", "text": "The letters"}, {"ref": "L.3 §6 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-6-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "b5d6d64121", "text": "Letter recognition and sounds only – no writing yet. Pupils see the capital and small letter, hear the sound and match it to a picture."}, {"ref": "L.3 §6 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.3-6-2", "kind": "table", "h": "74c987e268", "text": "Letter Sound Picture word Khmer-friendly cue C c /k/ (as in cat) 🐱 cat like ក D d /d/ 🐶 dog like ដ"}, {"ref": "L.3 §7 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-7-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "1bd537eb12", "text": "Teacher-led lesson (one study hour, 40 min)"}, {"ref": "L.3 §7 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-7-1", "kind": "list", "h": "5bad339a28", "text": "Warm-up and feed up (5 min): Say the learning goal and point to the success criteria cues. Hello song, finger counting 1–5. Listen and say (8 min): Show coloured paper or balloons one by one. Say the word, class repeats. Practice (8 min): Hide a colour card behind your back, show a corner: \"What colour is it?\". Letter practice (5 min): Show the letter cards C and D (capital and small). Say the sound and the picture word: C – cat, D – dog. Pupils repeat, draw the letter in the air, and point to the right card when they hear the sound. No writing yet. Game (8 min): Touch something… \"Touch something red!\" Pupils touch something red on their clothes, bag or in the room. Wrap-up and feed back (6 min): Point to each success criterion cue; pupils show thumbs up (I can), sideways (with help) or down (not yet). Give one feed-forward tip from the rubric. Colour song. Goodbye song."}, {"ref": "L.3 §8 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-8-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "beb8224862", "text": "Self-paced app lesson"}, {"ref": "L.3 §8 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-8-1", "kind": "list", "h": "3fa85ee450", "text": "Paint: a white balloon; audio \"red\" and the balloon turns red as the pupil taps it. Listen and tap: four balloons; audio \"Tap blue!\". Right: the balloon pops with a happy sound. Wrong: the word plays again and the right balloon glows. Drag: sort crayons into colour boxes. Say it: a balloon appears; the pupil says the colour and hears the model. Mix: \"Two green balloons\" – tap the right picture."}, {"ref": "L.3 §9 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-9-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "07cd9e0db6", "text": "Activities without electronics"}, {"ref": "L.3 §9 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-9-1", "kind": "list", "h": "9fe73a2d3f", "text": "Colour corners: coloured paper in four corners; pupils walk to the colour called. In a big class, send one row at a time. Stand up if…: \"Stand up if you have blue!\". Colour on the board: if no coloured chalk, use coloured paper taped to the board."}, {"ref": "L.3 §10 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-10-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "7f57b36be2", "text": "Differentiation"}, {"ref": "L.3 §10 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-10-1", "kind": "list", "h": "1e3f86ad4a", "text": "Need more support: point to the colour rather than say it. Ready for more: combine number and colour: \"three red pencils\"."}, {"ref": "L.3 §11 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-11-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "3bd9f3865f", "text": "Quick assessment"}, {"ref": "L.3 §11 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-11-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "c204f9445f", "text": "Teacher holds up colour cards to groups of five and ticks who names each one."}, {"ref": "L.3 §11 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.3-11-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "9c2963b303", "text": "Record the RTTI level each pupil reached per success criterion in the progress checklist (R.1)."}, {"ref": "L.3 §12 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-12-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "25c86f6a92", "text": "Quiz"}, {"ref": "L.3 §12 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-12-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "2289a536b9", "text": "Each question checks one success criterion at one RTTI level. After Check , the quiz shows which levels the pupil reached for each criterion and what to try next."}, {"ref": "L.3 §12 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.3-12-2", "kind": "table", "h": "a4ac9c640b", "text": "Success criterion RTTI level Question 1 Say four colours R 1 2 Touch a colour T1 2 3 Colours on new things T2 3 3 Colours on new things T2 4 3 Colours on new things I 5 4 Letters C and D R 6 4 Letters C and D T1 7"}, {"ref": "L.3 §12 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.3-12-3", "kind": "quiz", "h": "5669bbeb03", "text": "1. 🔴 What colour is it? Criterion 1 · RTTI level R red Yes! It is red. blue Blue is like the sky. This is red. green Green is like a leaf. This is red. 2. The teacher says \"Touch something blue!\". What do you touch? Criterion 2 · RTTI level T1 🍌 the banana A banana is yellow. Find something blue, like the sky. 🟦 the blue book Yes! You heard blue and found blue. 🌿 the leaf A leaf is green. Find something blue. 3. 🍌 What colour is a banana? Criterion 3 · RTTI level T2 red Look again – ripe bananas are yellow. purple Bananas are not purple. They are yellow. yellow Yes! You named the colour of something new. 4. 🌿 What colour is the leaf? Criterion 3 · RTTI level T2 green Yes! Leaves are green. yellow Look again at the leaf: it is green. red Look again at the leaf: it is green. 5. ✏️🔴 ✏️🔵 Two pencils. What is different? Criterion 3 · RTTI level I the size They are the same size. Look at the colour. the colour Yes! Same thing, different colour: red and blue. the number There is one of each. Look at the colour. 6. 🐱 Which letter does \"cat\" start with? Criterion 4 · RTTI level R C Yes! \"cat\" starts with C. A Listen again: \"cat\" – the first sound is C. B Listen again: \"cat\" – the first sound is C. 7. This is the letter D. Which picture starts with D? Criterion 4 · RTTI level T1 🐱 cat That starts with C. Find the D sound. 🐶 dog Yes! \"dog\" starts with D. 🍎 apple That starts with A. Find the D sound. Check Try again"}, {"ref": "L.3 §13 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-13-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "b8efd777f4", "text": "CEFR cross-reference"}, {"ref": "L.3 §13 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-13-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "9ace50ee5c", "text": "Secondary reference only. Pre-A1 can-do statements adapted from the CEFR Companion Volume (2020); not an official CEFR test."}, {"ref": "L.3 §13 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.3-13-2", "kind": "list", "h": "443ebf7506", "text": "I can say four colours: red, blue, yellow, green. I can touch something red, blue, yellow or green when the teacher says it. I can answer What colour is it? with one word. I can recognise the letters C and D and say their sounds."}], "html": "<div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"336aa5250e\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §0 ¶0\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.3-0-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §0 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §0 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶0</button><h1 data-body=\"1\">Lesson 3: Colours</h1></div><div class=\"blk blk-figure fl-full\" data-h=\"da39a3ee5e\" data-kind=\"figure\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §0 ¶1\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.3-0-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §0 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §0 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶1</button><figure class=\"fig fig-full\" data-body=\"1\" data-marker=\"full\"><button aria-label=\"Enlarge image: Four colour balloons: red, blue, yellow, green\" class=\"img-zoom\" type=\"button\"><img alt=\"Four colour balloons: red, blue, yellow, green\" data-src=\"images/colours.svg\" loading=\"eager\" src=\"assets/images/images/colours.svg\"/></button></figure></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"c5d265dfb9\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.3 §0 ¶2\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.3-0-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §0 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §0 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\">Pupils learn four colours and use them with things they already know: numbers and classroom things.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"025eec04ab\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §1 ¶0\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.3-1-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §1 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §1 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">MoEYS frame</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"537f52d094\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §1 ¶1\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.3-1-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §1 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §1 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶1</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>MoEYS reference</th>\n<th>This lesson</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Framework</td>\n<td>Curriculum Framework of General Education and Technical Education (MoEYS, 2016)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Subject and grade</td>\n<td>Foreign Languages (English), Grade 1 (primary)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Core competency</td>\n<td>4.2 Foreign Languages: \"Learners can adequately use foreign languages for communication, research and continued study.\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Foreign Languages goals (section 5.6, quoted)</td>\n<td>\"Possess competencies in communication in all four skills (listening, speaking, reading and writing).\" \"Become life-long learners with creativity and confidence.\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Expected outcome for primary (quoted)</td>\n<td>\"Construct basic knowledge of Science, Information and Communications Technology (ICT) and Foreign Languages.\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Subject components</td>\n<td>Listening and Speaking in this lesson, plus first letter recognition (Reading and Writing come later)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Study time</td>\n<td>Grade 1 has 2 study hours of Foreign Languages per week; one study hour is 40 minutes. This lesson is one study hour.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Lesson learning outcome (draft)</td>\n<td>Pupils recognise and name four colours and respond to simple instructions (Listening and Speaking).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Assessment (framework section 8.1)</td>\n<td>Knowledge, skills, attitude and application skills – observed with the RTTI rubric below</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3119e881c9\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.3 §1 ¶2\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.3-1-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §1 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §1 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>Lesson syllabus</strong> (in the Function / Form / Vocabulary format of the MoEYS English Grade 4 textbook):</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"71140a8f11\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.3 §1 ¶3\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.3-1-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §1 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §1 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶3</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Function</th>\n<th>Form</th>\n<th>Vocabulary</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Naming colours</td>\n<td>What colour is it? – It's red.</td>\n<td>red, blue, yellow, green; letters C, D</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"27efc58195\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §2 ¶0\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.3-2-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §2 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §2 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Feed up: where are we going?</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"7f85d52461\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §2 ¶1\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.3-2-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §2 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §2 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>Learning goal (say it at the start):</strong> Today we learn the colours red, blue, yellow and green.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"8e7ff9d5cf\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.3 §2 ¶2\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.3-2-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §2 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §2 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>In Khmer:</strong> ថ្ងៃនេះ យើងរៀនពណ៌ក្រហម ខៀវ លឿង និងបៃតង។</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"84433f5b4e\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.3 §2 ¶3\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.3-2-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §2 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §2 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶3</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>#</th>\n<th>Success criterion (pupil words)</th>\n<th>Khmer (pupil words)</th>\n<th>Picture or gesture cue</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>I can say red, blue, yellow and green.</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំអាចនិយាយ red, blue, yellow, green។</td>\n<td>hold up a colour card</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>I can touch a colour when I hear it.</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំអាចប៉ះពណ៌ដែលខ្ញុំឮ។</td>\n<td>touch your shirt</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>I can find colours on new things around me.</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំអាចរកពណ៌នៅលើរបស់ផ្សេងៗជុំវិញខ្ញុំ។</td>\n<td>look around, point</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>I can find the letters C and D and say their sounds.</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំអាចរកអក្សរ C និង D ហើយនិយាយសំឡេងរបស់វា។</td>\n<td>point to the letter card</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"956b1a2721\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"4\" data-ref=\"L.3 §2 ¶4\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.3-2-4\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §2 ¶4\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §2 ¶4 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶4</button><p data-body=\"1\">Draw the four cues on the board and point to them at the start and at the end of the lesson.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"a343dabcab\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §3 ¶0\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.3-3-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §3 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §3 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">RTTI rubric for the teacher</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"ee6f09a57a\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §3 ¶1\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.3-3-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §3 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §3 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">RTTI levels: <strong>R</strong> Reproduction (repeat what was taught), <strong>T1</strong> Training (use it in the practised activity), <strong>T2</strong> Transfer (use it in a new situation), <strong>I</strong> Insight (understand and explain why). The last column shows what to expect after this lesson: green = expected for all or most, yellow = with help, red = stretch goal, not expected yet.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"65846f37a9\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.3 §3 ¶2\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.3-3-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §3 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §3 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Level</th>\n<th>What the pupil does</th>\n<th>Teacher looks for</th>\n<th>Feed back (say)</th>\n<th>Feed forward (say)</th>\n<th>Expected after this lesson</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>R – Reproduction</td>\n<td>Repeats the four colour words with the cards.</td>\n<td>Says the word as the card is shown.</td>\n<td>\"You said all four colours!\"</td>\n<td>\"Now say the colour before I do.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">expected for all<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T1 – Training</td>\n<td>Touches the right colour in \"Touch something …!\"</td>\n<td>Moves to the right colour without copying.</td>\n<td>\"You heard blue and found blue.\"</td>\n<td>\"Next, tell a friend what to touch.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">expected for most<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T2 – Transfer</td>\n<td>Names colours of new things (fruit, clothes, a flag).</td>\n<td>Says \"Green!\" about something not used in the lesson.</td>\n<td>\"You found a colour we did not practise.\"</td>\n<td>\"On your way home, find three red things.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-yellow\">with help<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"yellow\" title=\"Rated yellow\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated yellow)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>I – Insight</td>\n<td>Explains that the same thing can have different colours (a red pencil, a blue pencil).</td>\n<td>Sorts objects by colour, not by kind, and says why.</td>\n<td>\"You sorted by colour – smart!\"</td>\n<td>\"Can you sort the pencils another way?\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-red\">stretch goal<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"red\" title=\"Rated red\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-xmark\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated red)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9c5dfe92f5\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.3 §3 ¶3\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.3-3-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §3 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §3 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶3</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>Letters (criterion 4):</strong></p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"72dc0de0b3\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"4\" data-ref=\"L.3 §3 ¶4\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.3-3-4\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §3 ¶4\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §3 ¶4 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶4</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Level</th>\n<th>What the pupil does</th>\n<th>Teacher looks for</th>\n<th>Feed back (say)</th>\n<th>Feed forward (say)</th>\n<th>Expected after this lesson</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>R – Reproduction</td>\n<td>Says the letter sounds after the teacher.</td>\n<td>Clear sound, not the letter name only.</td>\n<td>\"You said the C sound well!\"</td>\n<td>\"Now say it when you see the card.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">expected for all<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T1 – Training</td>\n<td>Points to the right letter card when the teacher says a sound.</td>\n<td>Points without looking at a neighbour.</td>\n<td>\"You found C by its sound.\"</td>\n<td>\"Next, find the letter in a picture word.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">expected for most<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T2 – Transfer</td>\n<td>Finds the letter at the start of a new word or a name card.</td>\n<td>Spots the letter in a word not taught today.</td>\n<td>\"You found D in a new word!\"</td>\n<td>\"Look for D in your friends' names.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-red\">stretch goal<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"red\" title=\"Rated red\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-xmark\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated red)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"5a2137d2b9\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §4 ¶0\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.3-4-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §4 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §4 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Target vocabulary</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"e4031d461f\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §4 ¶1\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.3-4-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §4 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §4 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶1</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>English</th>\n<th>Khmer</th>\n<th>Sound hint</th>\n<th>Picture idea</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>red</td>\n<td>ក្រហម</td>\n<td>red</td>\n<td>red balloon</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>blue</td>\n<td>ខៀវ</td>\n<td>bloo</td>\n<td>blue balloon</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>yellow</td>\n<td>លឿង</td>\n<td>YEL-oh</td>\n<td>yellow balloon</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>green</td>\n<td>បៃតង</td>\n<td>green</td>\n<td>green balloon</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>colour</td>\n<td>ពណ៌</td>\n<td>KUL-er</td>\n<td>paint box</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"f137c97e3d\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §5 ¶0\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.3-5-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §5 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §5 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Target language</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"952b2b086b\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §5 ¶1\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.3-5-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §5 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §5 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>What colour is it? – Red.</li>\n<li>Touch something blue!</li>\n<li>Two yellow balloons. (review of numbers)</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3f5171041f\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §6 ¶0\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.3-6-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §6 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §6 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">The letters</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b5d6d64121\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §6 ¶1\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.3-6-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §6 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §6 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Letter recognition and sounds only – no writing yet. Pupils see the capital and small letter, hear the sound and match it to a picture.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"74c987e268\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.3 §6 ¶2\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.3-6-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §6 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §6 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Letter</th>\n<th>Sound</th>\n<th>Picture word</th>\n<th>Khmer-friendly cue</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>C c</td>\n<td>/k/ (as in cat)</td>\n<td>🐱 cat</td>\n<td>like ក</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>D d</td>\n<td>/d/</td>\n<td>🐶 dog</td>\n<td>like ដ</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"1bd537eb12\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §7 ¶0\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.3-7-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §7 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §7 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Teacher-led lesson (one study hour, 40 min)</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"5bad339a28\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §7 ¶1\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.3-7-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §7 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §7 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Warm-up and feed up (5 min):</strong> Say the learning goal and point to the success criteria cues. Hello song, finger counting 1–5.</li>\n<li><strong>Listen and say (8 min):</strong> Show coloured paper or balloons one by one. Say the word, class repeats.</li>\n<li><strong>Practice (8 min):</strong> Hide a colour card behind your back, show a corner: \"What colour is it?\".</li>\n<li><strong>Letter practice (5 min):</strong> Show the letter cards C and D (capital and small). Say the sound and the picture word: C – cat, D – dog. Pupils repeat, draw the letter in the air, and point to the right card when they hear the sound. No writing yet.</li>\n<li><strong>Game (8 min):</strong> <em>Touch something…</em> \"Touch something red!\" Pupils touch something red on their clothes, bag or in the room.</li>\n<li><strong>Wrap-up and feed back (6 min):</strong> Point to each success criterion cue; pupils show thumbs up (I can), sideways (with help) or down (not yet). Give one feed-forward tip from the rubric. Colour song. Goodbye song.</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"beb8224862\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §8 ¶0\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.3-8-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §8 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §8 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Self-paced app lesson</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3fa85ee450\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §8 ¶1\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.3-8-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §8 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §8 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Paint:</strong> a white balloon; audio \"red\" and the balloon turns red as the pupil taps it.</li>\n<li><strong>Listen and tap:</strong> four balloons; audio \"Tap blue!\". Right: the balloon pops with a happy sound. Wrong: the word plays again and the right balloon glows.</li>\n<li><strong>Drag:</strong> sort crayons into colour boxes.</li>\n<li><strong>Say it:</strong> a balloon appears; the pupil says the colour and hears the model.</li>\n<li><strong>Mix:</strong> \"Two green balloons\" – tap the right picture.</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"07cd9e0db6\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §9 ¶0\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.3-9-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §9 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §9 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Activities without electronics</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9fe73a2d3f\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §9 ¶1\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.3-9-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §9 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §9 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Colour corners:</strong> coloured paper in four corners; pupils walk to the colour called. In a big class, send one row at a time.</li>\n<li><strong>Stand up if…:</strong> \"Stand up if you have blue!\".</li>\n<li><strong>Colour on the board:</strong> if no coloured chalk, use coloured paper taped to the board.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"7f57b36be2\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §10 ¶0\" data-sec=\"10\" id=\"p-L.3-10-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §10 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §10 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§10 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Differentiation</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"1e3f86ad4a\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §10 ¶1\" data-sec=\"10\" id=\"p-L.3-10-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §10 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §10 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§10 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Need more support:</strong> point to the colour rather than say it.</li>\n<li><strong>Ready for more:</strong> combine number and colour: \"three red pencils\".</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3bd9f3865f\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §11 ¶0\" data-sec=\"11\" id=\"p-L.3-11-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §11 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §11 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§11 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Quick assessment</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"c204f9445f\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §11 ¶1\" data-sec=\"11\" id=\"p-L.3-11-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §11 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §11 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§11 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Teacher holds up colour cards to groups of five and ticks who names each one.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9c2963b303\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.3 §11 ¶2\" data-sec=\"11\" id=\"p-L.3-11-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §11 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §11 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§11 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\">Record the RTTI level each pupil reached per success criterion in the progress checklist (R.1).</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"25c86f6a92\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §12 ¶0\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.3-12-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §12 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §12 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Quiz</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"2289a536b9\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §12 ¶1\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.3-12-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §12 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §12 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Each question checks one success criterion at one RTTI level. After <strong>Check</strong>, the quiz shows which levels the pupil reached for each criterion and what to try next.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"a4ac9c640b\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.3 §12 ¶2\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.3-12-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §12 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §12 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Success criterion</th>\n<th>RTTI level</th>\n<th>Question</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1 Say four colours</td>\n<td>R</td>\n<td>1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2 Touch a colour</td>\n<td>T1</td>\n<td>2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3 Colours on new things</td>\n<td>T2</td>\n<td>3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3 Colours on new things</td>\n<td>T2</td>\n<td>4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3 Colours on new things</td>\n<td>I</td>\n<td>5</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4 Letters C and D</td>\n<td>R</td>\n<td>6</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4 Letters C and D</td>\n<td>T1</td>\n<td>7</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-quiz\" data-h=\"5669bbeb03\" data-kind=\"quiz\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.3 §12 ¶3\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.3-12-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §12 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §12 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶3</button><div aria-label=\"Quiz\" class=\"quiz\" data-body=\"1\" role=\"group\"><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"R\" data-q=\"1\" data-sc=\"SC1\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">1.</span> 🔴 What colour is it?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 1 · RTTI level R</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">red</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! It is red.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">blue</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Blue is like the sky. This is red.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">green</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Green is like a leaf. This is red.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T1\" data-q=\"2\" data-sc=\"SC2\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">2.</span> The teacher says \"Touch something blue!\". What do you touch?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 2 · RTTI level T1</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">🍌 the banana</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A banana is yellow. Find something blue, like the sky.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">🟦 the blue book</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! You heard blue and found blue.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">🌿 the leaf</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A leaf is green. Find something blue.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T2\" data-q=\"3\" data-sc=\"SC3\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">3.</span> 🍌 What colour is a banana?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 3 · RTTI level T2</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">red</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Look again – ripe bananas are yellow.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">purple</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Bananas are not purple. They are yellow.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">yellow</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! You named the colour of something new.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T2\" data-q=\"4\" data-sc=\"SC3\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">4.</span> 🌿 What colour is the leaf?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 3 · RTTI level T2</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">green</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! Leaves are green.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">yellow</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Look again at the leaf: it is green.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">red</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Look again at the leaf: it is green.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"I\" data-q=\"5\" data-sc=\"SC3\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">5.</span> ✏️🔴 ✏️🔵 Two pencils. What is different?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 3 · RTTI level I</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">the size</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">They are the same size. Look at the colour.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">the colour</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! Same thing, different colour: red and blue.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">the number</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">There is one of each. Look at the colour.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"R\" data-q=\"6\" data-sc=\"SC4\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">6.</span> 🐱 Which letter does \"cat\" start with?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 4 · RTTI level R</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">C</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! \"cat\" starts with C.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">A</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Listen again: \"cat\" – the first sound is C.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">B</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Listen again: \"cat\" – the first sound is C.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T1\" data-q=\"7\" data-sc=\"SC4\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">7.</span> This is the letter D. Which picture starts with D?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 4 · RTTI level T1</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">🐱 cat</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That starts with C. Find the D sound.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">🐶 dog</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! \"dog\" starts with D.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">🍎 apple</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That starts with A. Find the D sound.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><div class=\"quiz-actions\"><button class=\"btn btn-primary quiz-check\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-check-double\"></i> Check</button><button class=\"btn btn-outline-secondary quiz-retry\" hidden=\"\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-rotate-left\"></i> Try again</button><span aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-score\" role=\"status\"></span></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-rtti\" hidden=\"\"></div></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b8efd777f4\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §13 ¶0\" data-sec=\"13\" id=\"p-L.3-13-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §13 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §13 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§13 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">CEFR cross-reference</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9ace50ee5c\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §13 ¶1\" data-sec=\"13\" id=\"p-L.3-13-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §13 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §13 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§13 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Secondary reference only. Pre-A1 can-do statements adapted from the CEFR Companion Volume (2020); not an official CEFR test.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"443ebf7506\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.3 §13 ¶2\" data-sec=\"13\" id=\"p-L.3-13-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §13 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §13 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§13 ¶2</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>I can say four colours: red, blue, yellow, green.</li>\n<li>I can touch something red, blue, yellow or green when the teacher says it.</li>\n<li>I can answer <strong>What colour is it?</strong> with one word.</li>\n<li>I can recognise the letters C and D and say their sounds.</li>\n</ul></div>"}, {"id": "L.4", "title": "Lesson 4: In my classroom", "order": 4, "goals": ["MoEYS (draft lesson outcome): Pupils name classroom objects and follow simple classroom instructions (Listening and Speaking).", "Success criterion 1: I can say pencil, book, bag and desk.", "Success criterion 2: I can do it when the teacher says \"Show me …!\" or \"Open your book!\"", "Success criterion 3: I can say \"It's a …\" about a new picture or thing.", "Success criterion 4: I can find the letters E, F and G and say their sounds."], "metadata": {"status": "draft", "grade": "1", "subject": "Foreign Languages (English)", "moeys_reference": "Curriculum Framework of General Education and Technical Education (2016) – framework level verified; Grade 1 English syllabus wording to be checked", "cefr_cross_reference": "Pre-A1 (adapted, CEFR Companion Volume)", "duration": "one study hour (40 min)", "updated": "2026-11-05 (v1.3)"}, "file": "l4-classroom.md", "notes": ["<p>Verified in the 2016 Curriculum Framework: core competency 4.2 wording, the four subject components, Grade 1 time allocation (2 study hours a week, 40 minutes each), the assessment principles. The Function / Form / Vocabulary table and the activity names (Listen and say, Pair work, Letter practice) follow the official MoEYS English Grade 4 Student's Book (2020). NOT found: an official MoEYS Grade 1 English syllabus, its outcome wording or codes, and a MoEYS teacher guide with lesson steps. The lesson outcome above is our draft wording, not an official MoEYS outcome. See open-items.md.</p>\n", "<p>Khmer pupil-friendly sentences to be verified by a native speaker (Grade 1 level).</p>\n", "<p>Khmer to be verified by a native speaker: is កាបូប or កាបូបស្ពាយ the usual word children use for a school bag? Is ប៊ិច the usual word for a pen?</p>\n", "<p>Letters follow the alphabet, two or three per lesson from Lesson 2 (A B, C D, E F G, H I J, K L M); the MoEYS English Grade 4 book also starts with \"The letters\" A B C D. The Khmer-friendly cues are approximate and must be checked by a Khmer-speaking teacher.</p>\n", "<p>CEFR Pre-A1 only describes recognising letters (and later spelling one's own name); it does not prescribe an order for teaching the alphabet. The letter order here is our choice (alphabetical, as in the MoEYS English Grade 4 book).</p>\n"], "blocks": [{"ref": "L.4 §0 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-0-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "01d9d16b9a", "text": "Lesson 4: In my classroom"}, {"ref": "L.4 §0 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-0-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "ae13d24924", "text": "Pupils name the things on their desk and follow short classroom instructions."}, {"ref": "L.4 §1 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-1-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "025eec04ab", "text": "MoEYS frame"}, {"ref": "L.4 §1 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-1-1", "kind": "table", "h": "6f708a485f", "text": "MoEYS reference This lesson Framework Curriculum Framework of General Education and Technical Education (MoEYS, 2016) Subject and grade Foreign Languages (English), Grade 1 (primary) Core competency 4.2 Foreign Languages: \"Learners can adequately use foreign languages for communication, research and continued study.\" Foreign Languages goals (section 5.6, quoted) \"Possess competencies in communication in all four skills (listening, speaking, reading and writing).\" \"Become life-long learners with creativity and confidence.\" Expected outcome for primary (quoted) \"Construct basic knowledge of Science, Information and Communications Technology (ICT) and Foreign Languages.\" Subject components Listening and Speaking in this lesson, plus first letter recognition (Reading and Writing come later) Study time Grade 1 has 2 study hours of Foreign Languages per week; one study hour is 40 minutes. This lesson is one study hour. Lesson learning outcome (draft) Pupils name classroom objects and follow simple classroom instructions (Listening and Speaking). Assessment (framework section 8.1) Knowledge, skills, attitude and application skills – observed with the RTTI rubric below"}, {"ref": "L.4 §1 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.4-1-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "3119e881c9", "text": "Lesson syllabus (in the Function / Form / Vocabulary format of the MoEYS English Grade 4 textbook):"}, {"ref": "L.4 §1 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.4-1-3", "kind": "table", "h": "783d26a27b", "text": "Function Form Vocabulary Talking about things What's this? – It's a pen. – Show me your book! pen, pencil, book, bag, desk; letters E, F, G"}, {"ref": "L.4 §2 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-2-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "27efc58195", "text": "Feed up: where are we going?"}, {"ref": "L.4 §2 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-2-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "f00f5f1710", "text": "Learning goal (say it at the start): Today we learn the names of things in our classroom."}, {"ref": "L.4 §2 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.4-2-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "836bab8d43", "text": "In Khmer: ថ្ងៃនេះ យើងរៀនឈ្មោះរបស់របរនៅក្នុងថ្នាក់រៀន។"}, {"ref": "L.4 §2 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.4-2-3", "kind": "table", "h": "b2c98373bb", "text": "# Success criterion (pupil words) Khmer (pupil words) Picture or gesture cue 1 I can say pencil, book, bag and desk. ខ្ញុំអាចនិយាយ pencil, book, bag, desk។ hold up your pencil 2 I can do it when the teacher says \"Show me …!\" or \"Open your book!\" ខ្ញុំអាចធ្វើតាម ពេលគ្រូនិយាយ Show me … ឬ Open your book។ open hands like a book 3 I can say \"It's a …\" about a new picture or thing. ខ្ញុំអាចនិយាយ It's a … អំពីរូបភាព ឬរបស់ថ្មី។ point to a picture 4 I can find the letters E, F and G and say their sounds. ខ្ញុំអាចរកអក្សរ E, F និង G ហើយនិយាយសំឡេងរបស់វា។ point to the letter card"}, {"ref": "L.4 §2 ¶4", "anchor": "p-L.4-2-4", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "956b1a2721", "text": "Draw the four cues on the board and point to them at the start and at the end of the lesson."}, {"ref": "L.4 §3 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-3-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "a343dabcab", "text": "RTTI rubric for the teacher"}, {"ref": "L.4 §3 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-3-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "ee6f09a57a", "text": "RTTI levels: R Reproduction (repeat what was taught), T1 Training (use it in the practised activity), T2 Transfer (use it in a new situation), I Insight (understand and explain why). The last column shows what to expect after this lesson: green = expected for all or most, yellow = with help, red = stretch goal, not expected yet."}, {"ref": "L.4 §3 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.4-3-2", "kind": "table", "h": "b3862b1633", "text": "Level What the pupil does Teacher looks for Feed back (say) Feed forward (say) Expected after this lesson R – Reproduction Repeats the four words while holding the objects. Says the word with the right object. \"You named your pencil!\" \"Now name it before I do.\" expected for all (rated green) T1 – Training Follows \"Show me your …!\" and \"Open/Close your book!\" Shows the right object without copying. \"You listened and did it.\" \"Next, give the instruction to your partner.\" expected for most (rated green) T2 – Transfer Answers \"What's this?\" about a new picture or a friend's object: It's a bag. Uses It's a … with an object not shown in class. \"You used It's a … by yourself!\" \"At home, tell someone: It's a book.\" with help (rated yellow) I – Insight Sorts things into \"school things\" and \"not school things\" and explains with a gesture or in Khmer. Can say why a mango does not go in the school bag. \"You know what we need for school.\" \"What else do you need for school?\" stretch goal (rated red)"}, {"ref": "L.4 §3 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.4-3-3", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "9c5dfe92f5", "text": "Letters (criterion 4):"}, {"ref": "L.4 §3 ¶4", "anchor": "p-L.4-3-4", "kind": "table", "h": "34bcd37a07", "text": "Level What the pupil does Teacher looks for Feed back (say) Feed forward (say) Expected after this lesson R – Reproduction Says the letter sounds after the teacher. Clear sound, not the letter name only. \"You said the E sound well!\" \"Now say it when you see the card.\" expected for all (rated green) T1 – Training Points to the right letter card when the teacher says a sound. Points without looking at a neighbour. \"You found E by its sound.\" \"Next, find the letter in a picture word.\" expected for most (rated green) T2 – Transfer Finds the letter at the start of a new word or a name card. Spots the letter in a word not taught today. \"You found F in a new word!\" \"Look for F in your friends' names.\" stretch goal (rated red)"}, {"ref": "L.4 §4 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-4-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "5a2137d2b9", "text": "Target vocabulary"}, {"ref": "L.4 §4 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-4-1", "kind": "table", "h": "0d36d895fd", "text": "English Khmer Sound hint Picture idea pencil ខ្មៅដៃ PEN-sil pencil pen ប៊ិច PEN pen book សៀវភៅ buk book bag កាបូប bag school bag desk តុ desk school desk"}, {"ref": "L.4 §5 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-5-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "f137c97e3d", "text": "Target language"}, {"ref": "L.4 §5 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-5-1", "kind": "list", "h": "ae6a0b10f3", "text": "What's this? – It's a pencil. / It's a pen. Show me your book! Open your book. / Close your book. A red pencil. (review of colours)"}, {"ref": "L.4 §6 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-6-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "3f5171041f", "text": "The letters"}, {"ref": "L.4 §6 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-6-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "b5d6d64121", "text": "Letter recognition and sounds only – no writing yet. Pupils see the capital and small letter, hear the sound and match it to a picture."}, {"ref": "L.4 §6 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.4-6-2", "kind": "table", "h": "0fdfa797c7", "text": "Letter Sound Picture word Khmer-friendly cue E e /e/ – short 🥚 egg short sound, like the vowel in ពេញ but shorter F f /f/ 🐟 fish Khmer has no /f/: top teeth on the bottom lip and blow (as in ហ្វ in loanwords) G g /g/ 🐐 goat like ហ្គ in loanwords (not ក)"}, {"ref": "L.4 §7 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-7-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "1bd537eb12", "text": "Teacher-led lesson (one study hour, 40 min)"}, {"ref": "L.4 §7 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-7-1", "kind": "list", "h": "c3d0c06388", "text": "Warm-up and feed up (5 min): Say the learning goal and point to the success criteria cues. Hello song. \"Touch something red / blue\". Listen and say (8 min): Hold up a real pencil, book and bag; point to a desk. Say each word with the class. Pair work (8 min): \"What's this?\" – class answers \"It's a book.\" Then pairs ask each other with their own things. Letter practice (5 min): Show the letter cards E, F and G (capital and small). Say the sound and the picture word: E – egg, F – fish, G – goat. Pupils repeat, draw the letter in the air, and point to the right card when they hear the sound. No writing yet. Game (8 min): Show me! \"Show me your pencil!\" – pupils hold it up. Teacher says (Simon says): only follow when the teacher says \"Teacher says…\". Wrap-up and feed back (6 min): Point to each success criterion cue; pupils show thumbs up (I can), sideways (with help) or down (not yet). Give one feed-forward tip from the rubric. Mystery bag: one pupil feels an object in a bag and guesses. Goodbye song."}, {"ref": "L.4 §8 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-8-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "beb8224862", "text": "Self-paced app lesson"}, {"ref": "L.4 §8 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-8-1", "kind": "list", "h": "9d3cb0f8db", "text": "Look and listen: a desk with four things; tapping each one plays its name. Find it: audio \"Where's the bag?\" – the pupil taps the bag. Drag: pack the school bag – drag the book and pencil into the bag when asked. Say it: a picture appears; the pupil says \"It's a pencil.\" and hears the model. Colour mix: \"Tap the blue book.\""}, {"ref": "L.4 §9 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-9-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "07cd9e0db6", "text": "Activities without electronics"}, {"ref": "L.4 §9 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-9-1", "kind": "list", "h": "bd9ad1845d", "text": "Show me!: every pupil uses their own things, so it works with any class size. Kim's game: four objects on the teacher's desk; take one away; the class says which is gone. Pass the bag: rows pass a bag while singing; when the song stops, the holder names something inside."}, {"ref": "L.4 §10 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-10-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "7f57b36be2", "text": "Differentiation"}, {"ref": "L.4 §10 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-10-1", "kind": "list", "h": "a98b3228ef", "text": "Need more support: hold up the object instead of saying the word. Ready for more: add a colour and a number: \"Two yellow pencils.\""}, {"ref": "L.4 §11 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-11-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "3bd9f3865f", "text": "Quick assessment"}, {"ref": "L.4 §11 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-11-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "11819dde3b", "text": "During Show me! , the teacher ticks who reacts correctly without copying neighbours."}, {"ref": "L.4 §11 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.4-11-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "9c2963b303", "text": "Record the RTTI level each pupil reached per success criterion in the progress checklist (R.1)."}, {"ref": "L.4 §12 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-12-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "25c86f6a92", "text": "Quiz"}, {"ref": "L.4 §12 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-12-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "2289a536b9", "text": "Each question checks one success criterion at one RTTI level. After Check , the quiz shows which levels the pupil reached for each criterion and what to try next."}, {"ref": "L.4 §12 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.4-12-2", "kind": "table", "h": "191f5a3662", "text": "Success criterion RTTI level Question 1 Name four things R 1 2 Follow instructions T1 2 3 It's a … T2 3 3 It's a … T2 4 3 It's a … I 5 4 Letters E, F and G R 6 4 Letters E, F and G T1 7"}, {"ref": "L.4 §12 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.4-12-3", "kind": "quiz", "h": "ac44ca6f55", "text": "1. ✏️ What's this? Criterion 1 · RTTI level R a pencil Yes! It's a pencil. a bag A bag carries books. This is a pencil. a desk A desk is a school table. This is a pencil. 2. The teacher says \"Open your book!\". What do you do? Criterion 2 · RTTI level T1 Close your book. Open is the opposite of close. Open it! Open your book. Yes! You listened and did it. Say goodbye. Do the action: open your book. 3. 🎒 Your friend shows you this. What do you say? Criterion 3 · RTTI level T2 It's a bag. Yes! You used It's a … for a new picture. It's a desk. A desk is a table. This is a bag. It's a book. A book has pages. This is a bag. 4. 📖 What's this? Criterion 3 · RTTI level T2 It's a pencil. We write with a pencil. We read this. It's a book. Yes! It's a book. It's red. That is a colour. Say the thing: It's a book. 5. Which one does NOT go in your school bag? Criterion 3 · RTTI level I ✏️ a pencil We need a pencil at school. 📖 a book We need a book at school. 🪑 a desk Yes! A desk stays in the classroom. 6. 🥚 Which letter does \"egg\" start with? Criterion 4 · RTTI level R E Yes! \"egg\" starts with E. A Listen again: \"egg\" – the first sound is E. B Listen again: \"egg\" – the first sound is E. 7. This is the letter F. Which picture starts with F? Criterion 4 · RTTI level T1 🥚 egg That starts with E. Find the F sound. 🐟 fish Yes! \"fish\" starts with F. ⚽ ball That starts with B. Find the F sound. Check Try again"}, {"ref": "L.4 §13 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-13-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "b8efd777f4", "text": "CEFR cross-reference"}, {"ref": "L.4 §13 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-13-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "9ace50ee5c", "text": "Secondary reference only. Pre-A1 can-do statements adapted from the CEFR Companion Volume (2020); not an official CEFR test."}, {"ref": "L.4 §13 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.4-13-2", "kind": "list", "h": "910099613e", "text": "I can name a pencil, a book, a bag and a desk. I can follow Show me your pencil! and Open your book! I can say It's a book. about a picture or object. I can recognise the letters E, F and G and say their sounds."}], "html": "<div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"01d9d16b9a\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §0 ¶0\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.4-0-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §0 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §0 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶0</button><h1 data-body=\"1\">Lesson 4: In my classroom</h1></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"ae13d24924\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §0 ¶1\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.4-0-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §0 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §0 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Pupils name the things on their desk and follow short classroom instructions.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"025eec04ab\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §1 ¶0\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.4-1-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §1 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §1 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">MoEYS frame</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"6f708a485f\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §1 ¶1\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.4-1-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §1 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §1 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶1</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>MoEYS reference</th>\n<th>This lesson</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Framework</td>\n<td>Curriculum Framework of General Education and Technical Education (MoEYS, 2016)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Subject and grade</td>\n<td>Foreign Languages (English), Grade 1 (primary)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Core competency</td>\n<td>4.2 Foreign Languages: \"Learners can adequately use foreign languages for communication, research and continued study.\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Foreign Languages goals (section 5.6, quoted)</td>\n<td>\"Possess competencies in communication in all four skills (listening, speaking, reading and writing).\" \"Become life-long learners with creativity and confidence.\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Expected outcome for primary (quoted)</td>\n<td>\"Construct basic knowledge of Science, Information and Communications Technology (ICT) and Foreign Languages.\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Subject components</td>\n<td>Listening and Speaking in this lesson, plus first letter recognition (Reading and Writing come later)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Study time</td>\n<td>Grade 1 has 2 study hours of Foreign Languages per week; one study hour is 40 minutes. This lesson is one study hour.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Lesson learning outcome (draft)</td>\n<td>Pupils name classroom objects and follow simple classroom instructions (Listening and Speaking).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Assessment (framework section 8.1)</td>\n<td>Knowledge, skills, attitude and application skills – observed with the RTTI rubric below</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3119e881c9\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.4 §1 ¶2\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.4-1-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §1 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §1 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>Lesson syllabus</strong> (in the Function / Form / Vocabulary format of the MoEYS English Grade 4 textbook):</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"783d26a27b\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.4 §1 ¶3\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.4-1-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §1 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §1 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶3</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Function</th>\n<th>Form</th>\n<th>Vocabulary</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Talking about things</td>\n<td>What's this? – It's a pen. – Show me your book!</td>\n<td>pen, pencil, book, bag, desk; letters E, F, G</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"27efc58195\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §2 ¶0\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.4-2-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §2 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §2 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Feed up: where are we going?</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"f00f5f1710\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §2 ¶1\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.4-2-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §2 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §2 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>Learning goal (say it at the start):</strong> Today we learn the names of things in our classroom.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"836bab8d43\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.4 §2 ¶2\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.4-2-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §2 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §2 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>In Khmer:</strong> ថ្ងៃនេះ យើងរៀនឈ្មោះរបស់របរនៅក្នុងថ្នាក់រៀន។</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b2c98373bb\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.4 §2 ¶3\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.4-2-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §2 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §2 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶3</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>#</th>\n<th>Success criterion (pupil words)</th>\n<th>Khmer (pupil words)</th>\n<th>Picture or gesture cue</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>I can say pencil, book, bag and desk.</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំអាចនិយាយ pencil, book, bag, desk។</td>\n<td>hold up your pencil</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>I can do it when the teacher says \"Show me …!\" or \"Open your book!\"</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំអាចធ្វើតាម ពេលគ្រូនិយាយ Show me … ឬ Open your book។</td>\n<td>open hands like a book</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>I can say \"It's a …\" about a new picture or thing.</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំអាចនិយាយ It's a … អំពីរូបភាព ឬរបស់ថ្មី។</td>\n<td>point to a picture</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>I can find the letters E, F and G and say their sounds.</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំអាចរកអក្សរ E, F និង G ហើយនិយាយសំឡេងរបស់វា។</td>\n<td>point to the letter card</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"956b1a2721\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"4\" data-ref=\"L.4 §2 ¶4\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.4-2-4\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §2 ¶4\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §2 ¶4 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶4</button><p data-body=\"1\">Draw the four cues on the board and point to them at the start and at the end of the lesson.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"a343dabcab\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §3 ¶0\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.4-3-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §3 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §3 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">RTTI rubric for the teacher</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"ee6f09a57a\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §3 ¶1\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.4-3-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §3 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §3 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">RTTI levels: <strong>R</strong> Reproduction (repeat what was taught), <strong>T1</strong> Training (use it in the practised activity), <strong>T2</strong> Transfer (use it in a new situation), <strong>I</strong> Insight (understand and explain why). The last column shows what to expect after this lesson: green = expected for all or most, yellow = with help, red = stretch goal, not expected yet.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b3862b1633\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.4 §3 ¶2\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.4-3-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §3 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §3 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Level</th>\n<th>What the pupil does</th>\n<th>Teacher looks for</th>\n<th>Feed back (say)</th>\n<th>Feed forward (say)</th>\n<th>Expected after this lesson</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>R – Reproduction</td>\n<td>Repeats the four words while holding the objects.</td>\n<td>Says the word with the right object.</td>\n<td>\"You named your pencil!\"</td>\n<td>\"Now name it before I do.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">expected for all<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T1 – Training</td>\n<td>Follows \"Show me your …!\" and \"Open/Close your book!\"</td>\n<td>Shows the right object without copying.</td>\n<td>\"You listened and did it.\"</td>\n<td>\"Next, give the instruction to your partner.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">expected for most<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T2 – Transfer</td>\n<td>Answers \"What's this?\" about a new picture or a friend's object: It's a bag.</td>\n<td>Uses It's a … with an object not shown in class.</td>\n<td>\"You used It's a … by yourself!\"</td>\n<td>\"At home, tell someone: It's a book.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-yellow\">with help<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"yellow\" title=\"Rated yellow\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated yellow)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>I – Insight</td>\n<td>Sorts things into \"school things\" and \"not school things\" and explains with a gesture or in Khmer.</td>\n<td>Can say why a mango does not go in the school bag.</td>\n<td>\"You know what we need for school.\"</td>\n<td>\"What else do you need for school?\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-red\">stretch goal<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"red\" title=\"Rated red\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-xmark\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated red)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9c5dfe92f5\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.4 §3 ¶3\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.4-3-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §3 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §3 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶3</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>Letters (criterion 4):</strong></p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"34bcd37a07\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"4\" data-ref=\"L.4 §3 ¶4\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.4-3-4\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §3 ¶4\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §3 ¶4 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶4</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Level</th>\n<th>What the pupil does</th>\n<th>Teacher looks for</th>\n<th>Feed back (say)</th>\n<th>Feed forward (say)</th>\n<th>Expected after this lesson</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>R – Reproduction</td>\n<td>Says the letter sounds after the teacher.</td>\n<td>Clear sound, not the letter name only.</td>\n<td>\"You said the E sound well!\"</td>\n<td>\"Now say it when you see the card.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">expected for all<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T1 – Training</td>\n<td>Points to the right letter card when the teacher says a sound.</td>\n<td>Points without looking at a neighbour.</td>\n<td>\"You found E by its sound.\"</td>\n<td>\"Next, find the letter in a picture word.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">expected for most<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T2 – Transfer</td>\n<td>Finds the letter at the start of a new word or a name card.</td>\n<td>Spots the letter in a word not taught today.</td>\n<td>\"You found F in a new word!\"</td>\n<td>\"Look for F in your friends' names.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-red\">stretch goal<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"red\" title=\"Rated red\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-xmark\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated red)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"5a2137d2b9\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §4 ¶0\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.4-4-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §4 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §4 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Target vocabulary</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"0d36d895fd\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §4 ¶1\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.4-4-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §4 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §4 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶1</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>English</th>\n<th>Khmer</th>\n<th>Sound hint</th>\n<th>Picture idea</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>pencil</td>\n<td>ខ្មៅដៃ</td>\n<td>PEN-sil</td>\n<td>pencil</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>pen</td>\n<td>ប៊ិច</td>\n<td>PEN</td>\n<td>pen</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>book</td>\n<td>សៀវភៅ</td>\n<td>buk</td>\n<td>book</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>bag</td>\n<td>កាបូប</td>\n<td>bag</td>\n<td>school bag</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>desk</td>\n<td>តុ</td>\n<td>desk</td>\n<td>school desk</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"f137c97e3d\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §5 ¶0\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.4-5-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §5 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §5 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Target language</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"ae6a0b10f3\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §5 ¶1\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.4-5-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §5 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §5 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>What's this? – It's a pencil. / It's a pen.</li>\n<li>Show me your book!</li>\n<li>Open your book. / Close your book.</li>\n<li>A red pencil. (review of colours)</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3f5171041f\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §6 ¶0\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.4-6-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §6 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §6 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">The letters</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b5d6d64121\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §6 ¶1\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.4-6-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §6 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §6 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Letter recognition and sounds only – no writing yet. Pupils see the capital and small letter, hear the sound and match it to a picture.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"0fdfa797c7\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.4 §6 ¶2\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.4-6-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §6 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §6 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Letter</th>\n<th>Sound</th>\n<th>Picture word</th>\n<th>Khmer-friendly cue</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>E e</td>\n<td>/e/ – short</td>\n<td>🥚 egg</td>\n<td>short sound, like the vowel in ពេញ but shorter</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>F f</td>\n<td>/f/</td>\n<td>🐟 fish</td>\n<td>Khmer has no /f/: top teeth on the bottom lip and blow (as in ហ្វ in loanwords)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>G g</td>\n<td>/g/</td>\n<td>🐐 goat</td>\n<td>like ហ្គ in loanwords (not ក)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"1bd537eb12\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §7 ¶0\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.4-7-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §7 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §7 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Teacher-led lesson (one study hour, 40 min)</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"c3d0c06388\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §7 ¶1\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.4-7-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §7 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §7 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Warm-up and feed up (5 min):</strong> Say the learning goal and point to the success criteria cues. Hello song. \"Touch something red / blue\".</li>\n<li><strong>Listen and say (8 min):</strong> Hold up a real pencil, book and bag; point to a desk. Say each word with the class.</li>\n<li><strong>Pair work (8 min):</strong> \"What's this?\" – class answers \"It's a book.\" Then pairs ask each other with their own things.</li>\n<li><strong>Letter practice (5 min):</strong> Show the letter cards E, F and G (capital and small). Say the sound and the picture word: E – egg, F – fish, G – goat. Pupils repeat, draw the letter in the air, and point to the right card when they hear the sound. No writing yet.</li>\n<li><strong>Game (8 min):</strong> <em>Show me!</em> \"Show me your pencil!\" – pupils hold it up. <em>Teacher says</em> (Simon says): only follow when the teacher says \"Teacher says…\".</li>\n<li><strong>Wrap-up and feed back (6 min):</strong> Point to each success criterion cue; pupils show thumbs up (I can), sideways (with help) or down (not yet). Give one feed-forward tip from the rubric. Mystery bag: one pupil feels an object in a bag and guesses. Goodbye song.</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"beb8224862\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §8 ¶0\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.4-8-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §8 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §8 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Self-paced app lesson</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9d3cb0f8db\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §8 ¶1\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.4-8-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §8 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §8 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Look and listen:</strong> a desk with four things; tapping each one plays its name.</li>\n<li><strong>Find it:</strong> audio \"Where's the bag?\" – the pupil taps the bag.</li>\n<li><strong>Drag:</strong> pack the school bag – drag the book and pencil into the bag when asked.</li>\n<li><strong>Say it:</strong> a picture appears; the pupil says \"It's a pencil.\" and hears the model.</li>\n<li><strong>Colour mix:</strong> \"Tap the blue book.\"</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"07cd9e0db6\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §9 ¶0\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.4-9-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §9 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §9 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Activities without electronics</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"bd9ad1845d\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §9 ¶1\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.4-9-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §9 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §9 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Show me!:</strong> every pupil uses their own things, so it works with any class size.</li>\n<li><strong>Kim's game:</strong> four objects on the teacher's desk; take one away; the class says which is gone.</li>\n<li><strong>Pass the bag:</strong> rows pass a bag while singing; when the song stops, the holder names something inside.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"7f57b36be2\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §10 ¶0\" data-sec=\"10\" id=\"p-L.4-10-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §10 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §10 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§10 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Differentiation</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"a98b3228ef\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §10 ¶1\" data-sec=\"10\" id=\"p-L.4-10-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §10 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §10 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§10 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Need more support:</strong> hold up the object instead of saying the word.</li>\n<li><strong>Ready for more:</strong> add a colour and a number: \"Two yellow pencils.\"</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3bd9f3865f\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §11 ¶0\" data-sec=\"11\" id=\"p-L.4-11-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §11 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §11 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§11 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Quick assessment</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"11819dde3b\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §11 ¶1\" data-sec=\"11\" id=\"p-L.4-11-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §11 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §11 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§11 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">During <em>Show me!</em>, the teacher ticks who reacts correctly without copying neighbours.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9c2963b303\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.4 §11 ¶2\" data-sec=\"11\" id=\"p-L.4-11-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §11 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §11 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§11 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\">Record the RTTI level each pupil reached per success criterion in the progress checklist (R.1).</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"25c86f6a92\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §12 ¶0\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.4-12-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §12 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §12 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Quiz</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"2289a536b9\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §12 ¶1\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.4-12-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §12 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §12 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Each question checks one success criterion at one RTTI level. After <strong>Check</strong>, the quiz shows which levels the pupil reached for each criterion and what to try next.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"191f5a3662\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.4 §12 ¶2\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.4-12-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §12 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §12 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Success criterion</th>\n<th>RTTI level</th>\n<th>Question</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1 Name four things</td>\n<td>R</td>\n<td>1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2 Follow instructions</td>\n<td>T1</td>\n<td>2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3 It's a …</td>\n<td>T2</td>\n<td>3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3 It's a …</td>\n<td>T2</td>\n<td>4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3 It's a …</td>\n<td>I</td>\n<td>5</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4 Letters E, F and G</td>\n<td>R</td>\n<td>6</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4 Letters E, F and G</td>\n<td>T1</td>\n<td>7</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-quiz\" data-h=\"ac44ca6f55\" data-kind=\"quiz\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.4 §12 ¶3\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.4-12-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §12 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §12 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶3</button><div aria-label=\"Quiz\" class=\"quiz\" data-body=\"1\" role=\"group\"><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"R\" data-q=\"1\" data-sc=\"SC1\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">1.</span> ✏️ What's this?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 1 · RTTI level R</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">a pencil</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! It's a pencil.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">a bag</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A bag carries books. This is a pencil.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">a desk</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A desk is a school table. This is a pencil.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T1\" data-q=\"2\" data-sc=\"SC2\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">2.</span> The teacher says \"Open your book!\". What do you do?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 2 · RTTI level T1</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Close your book.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Open is the opposite of close. Open it!</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Open your book.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! You listened and did it.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Say goodbye.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Do the action: open your book.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T2\" data-q=\"3\" data-sc=\"SC3\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">3.</span> 🎒 Your friend shows you this. What do you say?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 3 · RTTI level T2</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">It's a bag.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! You used It's a … for a new picture.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">It's a desk.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A desk is a table. This is a bag.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">It's a book.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A book has pages. This is a bag.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T2\" data-q=\"4\" data-sc=\"SC3\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">4.</span> 📖 What's this?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 3 · RTTI level T2</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">It's a pencil.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">We write with a pencil. We read this.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">It's a book.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! It's a book.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">It's red.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That is a colour. Say the thing: It's a book.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"I\" data-q=\"5\" data-sc=\"SC3\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">5.</span> Which one does NOT go in your school bag?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 3 · RTTI level I</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">✏️ a pencil</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">We need a pencil at school.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">📖 a book</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">We need a book at school.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">🪑 a desk</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! A desk stays in the classroom.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"R\" data-q=\"6\" data-sc=\"SC4\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">6.</span> 🥚 Which letter does \"egg\" start with?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 4 · RTTI level R</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">E</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! \"egg\" starts with E.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">A</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Listen again: \"egg\" – the first sound is E.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">B</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Listen again: \"egg\" – the first sound is E.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T1\" data-q=\"7\" data-sc=\"SC4\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">7.</span> This is the letter F. Which picture starts with F?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 4 · RTTI level T1</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">🥚 egg</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That starts with E. Find the F sound.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">🐟 fish</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! \"fish\" starts with F.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">⚽ ball</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That starts with B. Find the F sound.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><div class=\"quiz-actions\"><button class=\"btn btn-primary quiz-check\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-check-double\"></i> Check</button><button class=\"btn btn-outline-secondary quiz-retry\" hidden=\"\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-rotate-left\"></i> Try again</button><span aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-score\" role=\"status\"></span></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-rtti\" hidden=\"\"></div></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b8efd777f4\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §13 ¶0\" data-sec=\"13\" id=\"p-L.4-13-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §13 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §13 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§13 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">CEFR cross-reference</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9ace50ee5c\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §13 ¶1\" data-sec=\"13\" id=\"p-L.4-13-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §13 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §13 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§13 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Secondary reference only. Pre-A1 can-do statements adapted from the CEFR Companion Volume (2020); not an official CEFR test.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"910099613e\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.4 §13 ¶2\" data-sec=\"13\" id=\"p-L.4-13-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §13 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §13 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§13 ¶2</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>I can name a pencil, a book, a bag and a desk.</li>\n<li>I can follow <strong>Show me your pencil!</strong> and <strong>Open your book!</strong></li>\n<li>I can say <strong>It's a book.</strong> about a picture or object.</li>\n<li>I can recognise the letters E, F and G and say their sounds.</li>\n</ul></div>"}, {"id": "L.5", "title": "Lesson 5: My family", "order": 5, "goals": ["MoEYS (draft lesson outcome): Pupils name family members and introduce them with a simple sentence (Listening and Speaking).", "Success criterion 1: I can say mother, father, sister and brother.", "Success criterion 2: I can show a picture and say \"This is my …\"", "Success criterion 3: I can talk about a new family picture.", "Success criterion 4: I can find the letters H, I and J and say their sounds."], "metadata": {"status": "draft", "grade": "1", "subject": "Foreign Languages (English)", "moeys_reference": "Curriculum Framework of General Education and Technical Education (2016) – framework level verified; Grade 1 English syllabus wording to be checked", "cefr_cross_reference": "Pre-A1 (adapted, CEFR Companion Volume)", "duration": "one study hour (40 min)", "updated": "2026-11-05 (v1.3)"}, "file": "l5-family.md", "notes": ["<p>Verified in the 2016 Curriculum Framework: core competency 4.2 wording, the four subject components, Grade 1 time allocation (2 study hours a week, 40 minutes each), the assessment principles. The Function / Form / Vocabulary table and the activity names (Listen and say, Pair work, Letter practice) follow the official MoEYS English Grade 4 Student's Book (2020). NOT found: an official MoEYS Grade 1 English syllabus, its outcome wording or codes, and a MoEYS teacher guide with lesson steps. The lesson outcome above is our draft wording, not an official MoEYS outcome. See open-items.md.</p>\n", "<p>Khmer pupil-friendly sentences to be verified by a native speaker (Grade 1 level).</p>\n", "<p>Khmer to be verified by a native speaker. Khmer separates older (បង) and younger (ប្អូន) siblings; English does not. Teachers should explain this once in Khmer. Children also say ម៉ែ / ប៉ា at home – check which words to show. Be sensitive to pupils who do not live with both parents: accept grandmother, aunt and others (add as extra words if needed).</p>\n", "<p>Letters follow the alphabet, two or three per lesson from Lesson 2 (A B, C D, E F G, H I J, K L M); the MoEYS English Grade 4 book also starts with \"The letters\" A B C D. The Khmer-friendly cues are approximate and must be checked by a Khmer-speaking teacher.</p>\n", "<p>CEFR Pre-A1 only describes recognising letters (and later spelling one's own name); it does not prescribe an order for teaching the alphabet. The letter order here is our choice (alphabetical, as in the MoEYS English Grade 4 book).</p>\n"], "blocks": [{"ref": "L.5 §0 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-0-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "4dd86b95a4", "text": "Lesson 5: My family"}, {"ref": "L.5 §0 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-0-1", "kind": "figure", "h": "da39a3ee5e", "text": ""}, {"ref": "L.5 §0 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.5-0-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "009968bf95", "text": "Pupils talk about the people at home, using a drawing of their own family."}, {"ref": "L.5 §1 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-1-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "025eec04ab", "text": "MoEYS frame"}, {"ref": "L.5 §1 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-1-1", "kind": "table", "h": "485b1d4191", "text": "MoEYS reference This lesson Framework Curriculum Framework of General Education and Technical Education (MoEYS, 2016) Subject and grade Foreign Languages (English), Grade 1 (primary) Core competency 4.2 Foreign Languages: \"Learners can adequately use foreign languages for communication, research and continued study.\" Foreign Languages goals (section 5.6, quoted) \"Possess competencies in communication in all four skills (listening, speaking, reading and writing).\" \"Become life-long learners with creativity and confidence.\" Expected outcome for primary (quoted) \"Construct basic knowledge of Science, Information and Communications Technology (ICT) and Foreign Languages.\" Subject components Listening and Speaking in this lesson, plus first letter recognition (Reading and Writing come later) Study time Grade 1 has 2 study hours of Foreign Languages per week; one study hour is 40 minutes. This lesson is one study hour. Lesson learning outcome (draft) Pupils name family members and introduce them with a simple sentence (Listening and Speaking). Assessment (framework section 8.1) Knowledge, skills, attitude and application skills – observed with the RTTI rubric below"}, {"ref": "L.5 §1 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.5-1-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "3119e881c9", "text": "Lesson syllabus (in the Function / Form / Vocabulary format of the MoEYS English Grade 4 textbook):"}, {"ref": "L.5 §1 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.5-1-3", "kind": "table", "h": "1b826a6556", "text": "Function Form Vocabulary Introducing family members This is my mother. – Who is this? mother, father, sister, brother, grandmother, grandfather; letters H, I, J"}, {"ref": "L.5 §2 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-2-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "27efc58195", "text": "Feed up: where are we going?"}, {"ref": "L.5 §2 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-2-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "4df9d5f9c3", "text": "Learning goal (say it at the start): Today we learn to talk about our family."}, {"ref": "L.5 §2 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.5-2-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "c5cc653c28", "text": "In Khmer: ថ្ងៃនេះ យើងរៀននិយាយអំពីក្រុមគ្រួសាររបស់យើង។"}, {"ref": "L.5 §2 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.5-2-3", "kind": "table", "h": "b18cb3c994", "text": "# Success criterion (pupil words) Khmer (pupil words) Picture or gesture cue 1 I can say mother, father, sister and brother. ខ្ញុំអាចនិយាយ mother, father, sister, brother។ hold up four fingers, one per person 2 I can show a picture and say \"This is my …\" ខ្ញុំអាចបង្ហាញរូបភាព ហើយនិយាយ This is my …។ show your drawing 3 I can talk about a new family picture. ខ្ញុំអាចនិយាយអំពីរូបភាពគ្រួសារថ្មី។ point to a new picture 4 I can find the letters H, I and J and say their sounds. ខ្ញុំអាចរកអក្សរ H, I និង J ហើយនិយាយសំឡេងរបស់វា។ point to the letter card"}, {"ref": "L.5 §2 ¶4", "anchor": "p-L.5-2-4", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "956b1a2721", "text": "Draw the four cues on the board and point to them at the start and at the end of the lesson."}, {"ref": "L.5 §3 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-3-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "a343dabcab", "text": "RTTI rubric for the teacher"}, {"ref": "L.5 §3 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-3-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "ee6f09a57a", "text": "RTTI levels: R Reproduction (repeat what was taught), T1 Training (use it in the practised activity), T2 Transfer (use it in a new situation), I Insight (understand and explain why). The last column shows what to expect after this lesson: green = expected for all or most, yellow = with help, red = stretch goal, not expected yet."}, {"ref": "L.5 §3 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.5-3-2", "kind": "table", "h": "6d56c2d22f", "text": "Level What the pupil does Teacher looks for Feed back (say) Feed forward (say) Expected after this lesson R – Reproduction Repeats the four family words with the pictures. Says the word as the picture is shown. \"You know the family words!\" \"Now say them with your finger song.\" expected for all (rated green) T1 – Training Answers \"Who is this?\" about the puppet's family: This is my mother. Uses This is my … with the class pictures. \"You said a whole sentence.\" \"Next, show your own drawing.\" expected for most (rated green) T2 – Transfer Introduces their own drawing or a new family photo. Uses This is my … about their own family. \"You told us about your family!\" \"Add one more: My brother is seven.\" with help (rated yellow) I – Insight Notices that English has one word for sister, but Khmer has bong srey and p'oun srey (older and younger). Explains the difference in Khmer. \"You found a difference between Khmer and English!\" \"What other words are different?\" stretch goal (rated red)"}, {"ref": "L.5 §3 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.5-3-3", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "9c5dfe92f5", "text": "Letters (criterion 4):"}, {"ref": "L.5 §3 ¶4", "anchor": "p-L.5-3-4", "kind": "table", "h": "664fc3a8f5", "text": "Level What the pupil does Teacher looks for Feed back (say) Feed forward (say) Expected after this lesson R – Reproduction Says the letter sounds after the teacher. Clear sound, not the letter name only. \"You said the H sound well!\" \"Now say it when you see the card.\" expected for all (rated green) T1 – Training Points to the right letter card when the teacher says a sound. Points without looking at a neighbour. \"You found H by its sound.\" \"Next, find the letter in a picture word.\" expected for most (rated green) T2 – Transfer Finds the letter at the start of a new word or a name card. Spots the letter in a word not taught today. \"You found I in a new word!\" \"Look for I in your friends' names.\" stretch goal (rated red)"}, {"ref": "L.5 §4 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-4-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "5a2137d2b9", "text": "Target vocabulary"}, {"ref": "L.5 §4 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-4-1", "kind": "table", "h": "d2d2b47da1", "text": "English Khmer Sound hint Picture idea mother ម្ដាយ MUH-ther mother father ឪពុក FAH-ther father sister បងស្រី / ប្អូនស្រី SIS-ter girl brother បងប្រុស / ប្អូនប្រុស BRUH-ther boy family គ្រួសារ FAM-i-lee whole family"}, {"ref": "L.5 §5 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-5-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "f137c97e3d", "text": "Target language"}, {"ref": "L.5 §5 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-5-1", "kind": "list", "h": "3b480d0909", "text": "Who is this? – This is my mother. I have a sister. My brother is seven. (review of numbers) Dialogue: Chantha: \"Who is this?\" – Piseth: \"This is my grandmother.\""}, {"ref": "L.5 §6 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-6-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "3f5171041f", "text": "The letters"}, {"ref": "L.5 §6 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-6-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "b5d6d64121", "text": "Letter recognition and sounds only – no writing yet. Pupils see the capital and small letter, hear the sound and match it to a picture."}, {"ref": "L.5 §6 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.5-6-2", "kind": "table", "h": "b8b699be98", "text": "Letter Sound Picture word Khmer-friendly cue H h /h/ 🐔 hen like ហ I i /ɪ/ – short 🐛 insect short, lips a little smiling J j /dʒ/ 🦘 jump close to ជ, but softer"}, {"ref": "L.5 §7 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-7-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "1bd537eb12", "text": "Teacher-led lesson (one study hour, 40 min)"}, {"ref": "L.5 §7 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-7-1", "kind": "list", "h": "f8f7933800", "text": "Warm-up and feed up (5 min): Say the learning goal and point to the success criteria cues. Hello song. \"Show me your pencil!\" Listen and say (8 min): Draw a simple family on the board, or show the puppet's family. Name each one. Practice (8 min): Point and ask \"Who is this?\". Then pupils draw their own family in their exercise book. Letter practice (5 min): Show the letter cards H, I and J (capital and small). Say the sound and the picture word: H – hen, I – insect, J – jump. Pupils repeat, draw the letter in the air, and point to the right card when they hear the sound. No writing yet. Game (8 min): Family finger song: each finger is a family member, sing and wiggle. Wrap-up and feed back (6 min): Point to each success criterion cue; pupils show thumbs up (I can), sideways (with help) or down (not yet). Give one feed-forward tip from the rubric. Three pupils show their drawing: \"This is my father.\" Goodbye song."}, {"ref": "L.5 §8 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-8-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "beb8224862", "text": "Self-paced app lesson"}, {"ref": "L.5 §8 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-8-1", "kind": "list", "h": "cbf17430e3", "text": "Meet Teddy's family: tap each person to hear \"This is my mother\" and so on. Listen and tap: \"Tap the brother!\" Build a family: drag figures into a house; each one says its name. Say it: the pupil records \"This is my …\" for each figure. Song: family finger song."}, {"ref": "L.5 §9 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-9-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "07cd9e0db6", "text": "Activities without electronics"}, {"ref": "L.5 §9 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-9-1", "kind": "list", "h": "dc63b052f9", "text": "Draw and tell: paper and pencil only; pairs show drawings to each other. Family line: five pupils act as a family at the front; the class names each one."}, {"ref": "L.5 §10 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-10-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "7f57b36be2", "text": "Differentiation"}, {"ref": "L.5 §10 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-10-1", "kind": "list", "h": "16831d5fa9", "text": "Need more support: point to the picture when the teacher says the word. Ready for more: add age and colour: \"My sister is five. She has a red bag.\""}, {"ref": "L.5 §11 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-11-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "3bd9f3865f", "text": "Quick assessment"}, {"ref": "L.5 §11 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-11-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "35026a9b80", "text": "During Draw and tell , the teacher ticks who can say \"This is my …\" with one family word."}, {"ref": "L.5 §11 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.5-11-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "9c2963b303", "text": "Record the RTTI level each pupil reached per success criterion in the progress checklist (R.1)."}, {"ref": "L.5 §12 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-12-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "25c86f6a92", "text": "Quiz"}, {"ref": "L.5 §12 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-12-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "2289a536b9", "text": "Each question checks one success criterion at one RTTI level. After Check , the quiz shows which levels the pupil reached for each criterion and what to try next."}, {"ref": "L.5 §12 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.5-12-2", "kind": "table", "h": "eaf7e474d6", "text": "Success criterion RTTI level Question 1 Family words R 1 1 Family words T1 2 2 This is my … T1 3 3 New family picture T2 4 3 New family picture I 5 4 Letters H, I and J R 6 4 Letters H, I and J T1 7"}, {"ref": "L.5 §12 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.5-12-3", "kind": "quiz", "h": "3b439dc2ed", "text": "1. 👩 Listen: \"mother\". Which picture? Criterion 1 · RTTI level R 👩 a woman Yes! Mother. 👨 a man That is father. Mother is a woman. 👦 a boy That is brother. Mother is a woman. 2. 👦 A boy in your family is your… Criterion 1 · RTTI level T1 sister A sister is a girl. brother Yes! A boy in your family is your brother. mother A mother is a woman. 3. 👨 Teddy points at his father. What does Teddy say? Criterion 2 · RTTI level T1 This is my sister. A sister is a girl. This is a man. This is my book. A book is not a person. This is my father. Yes! This is my father. 4. 👵 A new picture: Piseth's grandmother. What can Piseth say? Criterion 3 · RTTI level T2 This is my grandmother. Yes! You used This is my … for a new person. This is my pencil. A grandmother is a person, not a pencil. This is my teacher. Look again: it is Piseth's grandmother. 5. In English, an older and a younger sister are both… Criterion 3 · RTTI level I mother Mother is a parent, not a sister. sister Yes! English has one word: sister. Khmer has two. brother Brother is a boy. 6. 🐔 Which letter does \"hen\" start with? Criterion 4 · RTTI level R H Yes! \"hen\" starts with H. A Listen again: \"hen\" – the first sound is H. B Listen again: \"hen\" – the first sound is H. 7. This is the letter I. Which picture starts with I? Criterion 4 · RTTI level T1 🐔 hen That starts with H. Find the I sound. 🐛 insect Yes! \"insect\" starts with I. 🐘 elephant That starts with E. Find the I sound. Check Try again"}, {"ref": "L.5 §13 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-13-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "b8efd777f4", "text": "CEFR cross-reference"}, {"ref": "L.5 §13 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-13-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "9ace50ee5c", "text": "Secondary reference only. Pre-A1 can-do statements adapted from the CEFR Companion Volume (2020); not an official CEFR test."}, {"ref": "L.5 §13 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.5-13-2", "kind": "list", "h": "092e6285fe", "text": "I can say mother, father, sister and brother. I can show a picture and say This is my mother. I can understand Who is this? when the teacher points at a picture. I can recognise the letters H, I and J and say their sounds."}], "html": "<div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"4dd86b95a4\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §0 ¶0\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.5-0-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §0 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §0 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶0</button><h1 data-body=\"1\">Lesson 5: My family</h1></div><div class=\"blk blk-figure fl-right\" data-h=\"da39a3ee5e\" data-kind=\"figure\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §0 ¶1\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.5-0-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §0 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §0 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶1</button><figure class=\"fig fig-right\" data-body=\"1\" data-marker=\"right\"><button aria-label=\"Enlarge image: Stick-figure family: father, mother, brother, sister\" class=\"img-zoom\" type=\"button\"><img alt=\"Stick-figure family: father, mother, brother, sister\" data-src=\"images/family.svg\" loading=\"eager\" src=\"assets/images/images/family.svg\"/></button></figure></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"009968bf95\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.5 §0 ¶2\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.5-0-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §0 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §0 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\">Pupils talk about the people at home, using a drawing of their own family.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"025eec04ab\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §1 ¶0\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.5-1-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §1 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §1 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">MoEYS frame</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"485b1d4191\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §1 ¶1\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.5-1-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §1 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §1 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶1</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>MoEYS reference</th>\n<th>This lesson</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Framework</td>\n<td>Curriculum Framework of General Education and Technical Education (MoEYS, 2016)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Subject and grade</td>\n<td>Foreign Languages (English), Grade 1 (primary)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Core competency</td>\n<td>4.2 Foreign Languages: \"Learners can adequately use foreign languages for communication, research and continued study.\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Foreign Languages goals (section 5.6, quoted)</td>\n<td>\"Possess competencies in communication in all four skills (listening, speaking, reading and writing).\" \"Become life-long learners with creativity and confidence.\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Expected outcome for primary (quoted)</td>\n<td>\"Construct basic knowledge of Science, Information and Communications Technology (ICT) and Foreign Languages.\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Subject components</td>\n<td>Listening and Speaking in this lesson, plus first letter recognition (Reading and Writing come later)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Study time</td>\n<td>Grade 1 has 2 study hours of Foreign Languages per week; one study hour is 40 minutes. This lesson is one study hour.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Lesson learning outcome (draft)</td>\n<td>Pupils name family members and introduce them with a simple sentence (Listening and Speaking).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Assessment (framework section 8.1)</td>\n<td>Knowledge, skills, attitude and application skills – observed with the RTTI rubric below</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3119e881c9\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.5 §1 ¶2\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.5-1-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §1 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §1 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>Lesson syllabus</strong> (in the Function / Form / Vocabulary format of the MoEYS English Grade 4 textbook):</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"1b826a6556\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.5 §1 ¶3\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.5-1-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §1 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §1 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶3</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Function</th>\n<th>Form</th>\n<th>Vocabulary</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Introducing family members</td>\n<td>This is my mother. – Who is this?</td>\n<td>mother, father, sister, brother, grandmother, grandfather; letters H, I, J</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"27efc58195\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §2 ¶0\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.5-2-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §2 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §2 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Feed up: where are we going?</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"4df9d5f9c3\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §2 ¶1\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.5-2-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §2 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §2 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>Learning goal (say it at the start):</strong> Today we learn to talk about our family.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"c5cc653c28\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.5 §2 ¶2\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.5-2-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §2 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §2 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>In Khmer:</strong> ថ្ងៃនេះ យើងរៀននិយាយអំពីក្រុមគ្រួសាររបស់យើង។</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b18cb3c994\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.5 §2 ¶3\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.5-2-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §2 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §2 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶3</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>#</th>\n<th>Success criterion (pupil words)</th>\n<th>Khmer (pupil words)</th>\n<th>Picture or gesture cue</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>I can say mother, father, sister and brother.</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំអាចនិយាយ mother, father, sister, brother។</td>\n<td>hold up four fingers, one per person</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>I can show a picture and say \"This is my …\"</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំអាចបង្ហាញរូបភាព ហើយនិយាយ This is my …។</td>\n<td>show your drawing</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>I can talk about a new family picture.</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំអាចនិយាយអំពីរូបភាពគ្រួសារថ្មី។</td>\n<td>point to a new picture</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>I can find the letters H, I and J and say their sounds.</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំអាចរកអក្សរ H, I និង J ហើយនិយាយសំឡេងរបស់វា។</td>\n<td>point to the letter card</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"956b1a2721\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"4\" data-ref=\"L.5 §2 ¶4\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.5-2-4\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §2 ¶4\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §2 ¶4 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶4</button><p data-body=\"1\">Draw the four cues on the board and point to them at the start and at the end of the lesson.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"a343dabcab\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §3 ¶0\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.5-3-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §3 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §3 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">RTTI rubric for the teacher</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"ee6f09a57a\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §3 ¶1\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.5-3-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §3 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §3 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">RTTI levels: <strong>R</strong> Reproduction (repeat what was taught), <strong>T1</strong> Training (use it in the practised activity), <strong>T2</strong> Transfer (use it in a new situation), <strong>I</strong> Insight (understand and explain why). The last column shows what to expect after this lesson: green = expected for all or most, yellow = with help, red = stretch goal, not expected yet.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"6d56c2d22f\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.5 §3 ¶2\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.5-3-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §3 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §3 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Level</th>\n<th>What the pupil does</th>\n<th>Teacher looks for</th>\n<th>Feed back (say)</th>\n<th>Feed forward (say)</th>\n<th>Expected after this lesson</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>R – Reproduction</td>\n<td>Repeats the four family words with the pictures.</td>\n<td>Says the word as the picture is shown.</td>\n<td>\"You know the family words!\"</td>\n<td>\"Now say them with your finger song.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">expected for all<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T1 – Training</td>\n<td>Answers \"Who is this?\" about the puppet's family: This is my mother.</td>\n<td>Uses This is my … with the class pictures.</td>\n<td>\"You said a whole sentence.\"</td>\n<td>\"Next, show your own drawing.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">expected for most<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T2 – Transfer</td>\n<td>Introduces their own drawing or a new family photo.</td>\n<td>Uses This is my … about their own family.</td>\n<td>\"You told us about your family!\"</td>\n<td>\"Add one more: My brother is seven.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-yellow\">with help<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"yellow\" title=\"Rated yellow\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated yellow)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>I – Insight</td>\n<td>Notices that English has one word for sister, but Khmer has bong srey and p'oun srey (older and younger).</td>\n<td>Explains the difference in Khmer.</td>\n<td>\"You found a difference between Khmer and English!\"</td>\n<td>\"What other words are different?\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-red\">stretch goal<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"red\" title=\"Rated red\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-xmark\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated red)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9c5dfe92f5\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.5 §3 ¶3\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.5-3-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §3 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §3 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶3</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>Letters (criterion 4):</strong></p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"664fc3a8f5\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"4\" data-ref=\"L.5 §3 ¶4\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.5-3-4\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §3 ¶4\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §3 ¶4 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶4</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Level</th>\n<th>What the pupil does</th>\n<th>Teacher looks for</th>\n<th>Feed back (say)</th>\n<th>Feed forward (say)</th>\n<th>Expected after this lesson</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>R – Reproduction</td>\n<td>Says the letter sounds after the teacher.</td>\n<td>Clear sound, not the letter name only.</td>\n<td>\"You said the H sound well!\"</td>\n<td>\"Now say it when you see the card.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">expected for all<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T1 – Training</td>\n<td>Points to the right letter card when the teacher says a sound.</td>\n<td>Points without looking at a neighbour.</td>\n<td>\"You found H by its sound.\"</td>\n<td>\"Next, find the letter in a picture word.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">expected for most<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T2 – Transfer</td>\n<td>Finds the letter at the start of a new word or a name card.</td>\n<td>Spots the letter in a word not taught today.</td>\n<td>\"You found I in a new word!\"</td>\n<td>\"Look for I in your friends' names.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-red\">stretch goal<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"red\" title=\"Rated red\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-xmark\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated red)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"5a2137d2b9\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §4 ¶0\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.5-4-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §4 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §4 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Target vocabulary</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"d2d2b47da1\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §4 ¶1\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.5-4-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §4 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §4 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶1</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>English</th>\n<th>Khmer</th>\n<th>Sound hint</th>\n<th>Picture idea</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>mother</td>\n<td>ម្ដាយ</td>\n<td>MUH-ther</td>\n<td>mother</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>father</td>\n<td>ឪពុក</td>\n<td>FAH-ther</td>\n<td>father</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>sister</td>\n<td>បងស្រី / ប្អូនស្រី</td>\n<td>SIS-ter</td>\n<td>girl</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>brother</td>\n<td>បងប្រុស / ប្អូនប្រុស</td>\n<td>BRUH-ther</td>\n<td>boy</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>family</td>\n<td>គ្រួសារ</td>\n<td>FAM-i-lee</td>\n<td>whole family</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"f137c97e3d\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §5 ¶0\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.5-5-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §5 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §5 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Target language</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3b480d0909\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §5 ¶1\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.5-5-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §5 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §5 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>Who is this? – This is my mother.</li>\n<li>I have a sister.</li>\n<li>My brother is seven. (review of numbers)</li>\n<li>Dialogue: <strong>Chantha:</strong> \"Who is this?\" – <strong>Piseth:</strong> \"This is my grandmother.\"</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3f5171041f\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §6 ¶0\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.5-6-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §6 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §6 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">The letters</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b5d6d64121\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §6 ¶1\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.5-6-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §6 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §6 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Letter recognition and sounds only – no writing yet. Pupils see the capital and small letter, hear the sound and match it to a picture.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b8b699be98\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.5 §6 ¶2\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.5-6-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §6 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §6 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Letter</th>\n<th>Sound</th>\n<th>Picture word</th>\n<th>Khmer-friendly cue</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>H h</td>\n<td>/h/</td>\n<td>🐔 hen</td>\n<td>like ហ</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>I i</td>\n<td>/ɪ/ – short</td>\n<td>🐛 insect</td>\n<td>short, lips a little smiling</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>J j</td>\n<td>/dʒ/</td>\n<td>🦘 jump</td>\n<td>close to ជ, but softer</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"1bd537eb12\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §7 ¶0\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.5-7-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §7 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §7 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Teacher-led lesson (one study hour, 40 min)</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"f8f7933800\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §7 ¶1\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.5-7-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §7 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §7 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Warm-up and feed up (5 min):</strong> Say the learning goal and point to the success criteria cues. Hello song. \"Show me your pencil!\"</li>\n<li><strong>Listen and say (8 min):</strong> Draw a simple family on the board, or show the puppet's family. Name each one.</li>\n<li><strong>Practice (8 min):</strong> Point and ask \"Who is this?\". Then pupils draw their own family in their exercise book.</li>\n<li><strong>Letter practice (5 min):</strong> Show the letter cards H, I and J (capital and small). Say the sound and the picture word: H – hen, I – insect, J – jump. Pupils repeat, draw the letter in the air, and point to the right card when they hear the sound. No writing yet.</li>\n<li><strong>Game (8 min):</strong> <em>Family finger song:</em> each finger is a family member, sing and wiggle.</li>\n<li><strong>Wrap-up and feed back (6 min):</strong> Point to each success criterion cue; pupils show thumbs up (I can), sideways (with help) or down (not yet). Give one feed-forward tip from the rubric. Three pupils show their drawing: \"This is my father.\" Goodbye song.</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"beb8224862\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §8 ¶0\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.5-8-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §8 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §8 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Self-paced app lesson</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"cbf17430e3\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §8 ¶1\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.5-8-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §8 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §8 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Meet Teddy's family:</strong> tap each person to hear \"This is my mother\" and so on.</li>\n<li><strong>Listen and tap:</strong> \"Tap the brother!\"</li>\n<li><strong>Build a family:</strong> drag figures into a house; each one says its name.</li>\n<li><strong>Say it:</strong> the pupil records \"This is my …\" for each figure.</li>\n<li><strong>Song:</strong> family finger song.</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"07cd9e0db6\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §9 ¶0\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.5-9-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §9 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §9 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Activities without electronics</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"dc63b052f9\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §9 ¶1\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.5-9-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §9 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §9 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Draw and tell:</strong> paper and pencil only; pairs show drawings to each other.</li>\n<li><strong>Family line:</strong> five pupils act as a family at the front; the class names each one.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"7f57b36be2\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §10 ¶0\" data-sec=\"10\" id=\"p-L.5-10-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §10 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §10 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§10 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Differentiation</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"16831d5fa9\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §10 ¶1\" data-sec=\"10\" id=\"p-L.5-10-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §10 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §10 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§10 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Need more support:</strong> point to the picture when the teacher says the word.</li>\n<li><strong>Ready for more:</strong> add age and colour: \"My sister is five. She has a red bag.\"</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3bd9f3865f\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §11 ¶0\" data-sec=\"11\" id=\"p-L.5-11-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §11 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §11 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§11 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Quick assessment</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"35026a9b80\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §11 ¶1\" data-sec=\"11\" id=\"p-L.5-11-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §11 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §11 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§11 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">During <em>Draw and tell</em>, the teacher ticks who can say \"This is my …\" with one family word.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9c2963b303\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.5 §11 ¶2\" data-sec=\"11\" id=\"p-L.5-11-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §11 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §11 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§11 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\">Record the RTTI level each pupil reached per success criterion in the progress checklist (R.1).</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"25c86f6a92\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §12 ¶0\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.5-12-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §12 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §12 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Quiz</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"2289a536b9\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §12 ¶1\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.5-12-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §12 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §12 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Each question checks one success criterion at one RTTI level. After <strong>Check</strong>, the quiz shows which levels the pupil reached for each criterion and what to try next.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"eaf7e474d6\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.5 §12 ¶2\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.5-12-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §12 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §12 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Success criterion</th>\n<th>RTTI level</th>\n<th>Question</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1 Family words</td>\n<td>R</td>\n<td>1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1 Family words</td>\n<td>T1</td>\n<td>2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2 This is my …</td>\n<td>T1</td>\n<td>3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3 New family picture</td>\n<td>T2</td>\n<td>4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3 New family picture</td>\n<td>I</td>\n<td>5</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4 Letters H, I and J</td>\n<td>R</td>\n<td>6</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4 Letters H, I and J</td>\n<td>T1</td>\n<td>7</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-quiz\" data-h=\"3b439dc2ed\" data-kind=\"quiz\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.5 §12 ¶3\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.5-12-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §12 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §12 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶3</button><div aria-label=\"Quiz\" class=\"quiz\" data-body=\"1\" role=\"group\"><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"R\" data-q=\"1\" data-sc=\"SC1\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">1.</span> 👩 Listen: \"mother\". Which picture?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 1 · RTTI level R</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">👩 a woman</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! Mother.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">👨 a man</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That is father. Mother is a woman.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">👦 a boy</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That is brother. Mother is a woman.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T1\" data-q=\"2\" data-sc=\"SC1\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">2.</span> 👦 A boy in your family is your…</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 1 · RTTI level T1</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">sister</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A sister is a girl.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">brother</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! A boy in your family is your brother.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">mother</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A mother is a woman.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T1\" data-q=\"3\" data-sc=\"SC2\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">3.</span> 👨 Teddy points at his father. What does Teddy say?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 2 · RTTI level T1</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">This is my sister.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A sister is a girl. This is a man.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">This is my book.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A book is not a person.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">This is my father.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! This is my father.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T2\" data-q=\"4\" data-sc=\"SC3\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">4.</span> 👵 A new picture: Piseth's grandmother. What can Piseth say?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 3 · RTTI level T2</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">This is my grandmother.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! You used This is my … for a new person.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">This is my pencil.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A grandmother is a person, not a pencil.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">This is my teacher.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Look again: it is Piseth's grandmother.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"I\" data-q=\"5\" data-sc=\"SC3\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">5.</span> In English, an older and a younger sister are both…</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 3 · RTTI level I</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">mother</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Mother is a parent, not a sister.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">sister</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! English has one word: sister. Khmer has two.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">brother</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Brother is a boy.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"R\" data-q=\"6\" data-sc=\"SC4\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">6.</span> 🐔 Which letter does \"hen\" start with?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 4 · RTTI level R</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">H</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! \"hen\" starts with H.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">A</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Listen again: \"hen\" – the first sound is H.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">B</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Listen again: \"hen\" – the first sound is H.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T1\" data-q=\"7\" data-sc=\"SC4\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">7.</span> This is the letter I. Which picture starts with I?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 4 · RTTI level T1</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">🐔 hen</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That starts with H. Find the I sound.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">🐛 insect</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! \"insect\" starts with I.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">🐘 elephant</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That starts with E. Find the I sound.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><div class=\"quiz-actions\"><button class=\"btn btn-primary quiz-check\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-check-double\"></i> Check</button><button class=\"btn btn-outline-secondary quiz-retry\" hidden=\"\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-rotate-left\"></i> Try again</button><span aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-score\" role=\"status\"></span></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-rtti\" hidden=\"\"></div></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b8efd777f4\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §13 ¶0\" data-sec=\"13\" id=\"p-L.5-13-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §13 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §13 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§13 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">CEFR cross-reference</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9ace50ee5c\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §13 ¶1\" data-sec=\"13\" id=\"p-L.5-13-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §13 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §13 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§13 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Secondary reference only. Pre-A1 can-do statements adapted from the CEFR Companion Volume (2020); not an official CEFR test.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"092e6285fe\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.5 §13 ¶2\" data-sec=\"13\" id=\"p-L.5-13-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §13 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §13 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§13 ¶2</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>I can say mother, father, sister and brother.</li>\n<li>I can show a picture and say <strong>This is my mother.</strong></li>\n<li>I can understand <strong>Who is this?</strong> when the teacher points at a picture.</li>\n<li>I can recognise the letters H, I and J and say their sounds.</li>\n</ul></div>"}, {"id": "L.6", "title": "Lesson 6: Animals – numbers to 10", "order": 6, "goals": ["MoEYS (draft lesson outcome): Pupils name common animals, ask and answer What's this? about animals, and count to ten (Listening and Speaking).", "Success criterion 1: I can say cat, dog, fish and bird.", "Success criterion 2: I can ask and answer: What's this? – It's a cat.", "Success criterion 3: I can count animals up to ten.", "Success criterion 4: I can find the letters K, L and M and say their sounds."], "metadata": {"status": "draft", "grade": "1", "subject": "Foreign Languages (English)", "moeys_reference": "Curriculum Framework of General Education and Technical Education (2016) – framework level verified; Grade 1 English syllabus wording to be checked", "cefr_cross_reference": "Pre-A1 (adapted, CEFR Companion Volume)", "duration": "one study hour (40 min)", "updated": "2026-11-05 (v1.3)"}, "file": "l6-animals.md", "notes": ["<p>Verified in the 2016 Curriculum Framework: core competency 4.2 wording, the four subject components, Grade 1 time allocation (2 study hours a week, 40 minutes each), the assessment principles. The Function / Form / Vocabulary table and the activity names (Listen and say, Pair work, Letter practice) follow the official MoEYS English Grade 4 Student's Book (2020). NOT found: an official MoEYS Grade 1 English syllabus, its outcome wording or codes, and a MoEYS teacher guide with lesson steps. The lesson outcome above is our draft wording, not an official MoEYS outcome. See open-items.md.</p>\n", "<p>Khmer pupil-friendly sentences to be verified by a native speaker (Grade 1 level).</p>\n", "<p>Khmer to be verified by a native speaker: is សត្វស្លាប or បក្សី the more natural word for \"bird\" for small children? The \"sh\" in fish and the \"r\" in bird are hard for Khmer speakers; accept close sounds.</p>\n", "<p>Letters follow the alphabet, two or three per lesson from Lesson 2 (A B, C D, E F G, H I J, K L M); the MoEYS English Grade 4 book also starts with \"The letters\" A B C D. The Khmer-friendly cues are approximate and must be checked by a Khmer-speaking teacher.</p>\n", "<p>CEFR Pre-A1 only describes recognising letters (and later spelling one's own name); it does not prescribe an order for teaching the alphabet. The letter order here is our choice (alphabetical, as in the MoEYS English Grade 4 book).</p>\n"], "blocks": [{"ref": "L.6 §0 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.6-0-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "a29ea4a3ec", "text": "Lesson 6: Animals – numbers to 10"}, {"ref": "L.6 §0 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.6-0-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "e4922db823", "text": "Pupils meet four animals they know from home and the village, and count to ten. The topic leads into Unit 3 \"Animals\" of the MoEYS English Grade 4 book."}, {"ref": "L.6 §1 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.6-1-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "025eec04ab", "text": "MoEYS frame"}, {"ref": "L.6 §1 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.6-1-1", "kind": "table", "h": "f5d0ec1e03", "text": "MoEYS reference This lesson Framework Curriculum Framework of General Education and Technical Education (MoEYS, 2016) Subject and grade Foreign Languages (English), Grade 1 (primary) Core competency 4.2 Foreign Languages: \"Learners can adequately use foreign languages for communication, research and continued study.\" Foreign Languages goals (section 5.6, quoted) \"Possess competencies in communication in all four skills (listening, speaking, reading and writing).\" \"Become life-long learners with creativity and confidence.\" Expected outcome for primary (quoted) \"Construct basic knowledge of Science, Information and Communications Technology (ICT) and Foreign Languages.\" Subject components Listening and Speaking in this lesson, plus first letter recognition (Reading and Writing come later) Study time Grade 1 has 2 study hours of Foreign Languages per week; one study hour is 40 minutes. This lesson is one study hour. Lesson learning outcome (draft) Pupils name common animals, ask and answer What's this? about animals, and count to ten (Listening and Speaking). Assessment (framework section 8.1) Knowledge, skills, attitude and application skills – observed with the RTTI rubric below"}, {"ref": "L.6 §1 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.6-1-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "3119e881c9", "text": "Lesson syllabus (in the Function / Form / Vocabulary format of the MoEYS English Grade 4 textbook):"}, {"ref": "L.6 §1 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.6-1-3", "kind": "table", "h": "fbbe4177c0", "text": "Function Form Vocabulary Asking and answering about animals; counting to ten What's this? – It's a cat. – How many? – Ten! cat, dog, fish, bird, eight, nine, ten; letters K, L, M"}, {"ref": "L.6 §2 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.6-2-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "27efc58195", "text": "Feed up: where are we going?"}, {"ref": "L.6 §2 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.6-2-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "588b764232", "text": "Learning goal (say it at the start): Today we learn animal words and count animals to ten."}, {"ref": "L.6 §2 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.6-2-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "ecc410ecc1", "text": "In Khmer: ថ្ងៃនេះ យើងរៀនឈ្មោះសត្វ និងរាប់សត្វដល់ដប់។"}, {"ref": "L.6 §2 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.6-2-3", "kind": "table", "h": "c3f8eda659", "text": "# Success criterion (pupil words) Khmer (pupil words) Picture or gesture cue 1 I can say cat, dog, fish and bird. ខ្ញុំអាចនិយាយ cat, dog, fish និង bird។ animal gestures (whiskers, paws, fish hands, wings) 2 I can ask and answer: What's this? – It's a cat. ខ្ញុំអាចសួរ និងឆ្លើយ៖ What's this? – It's a cat។ hand open, question face 3 I can count animals up to ten. ខ្ញុំអាចរាប់សត្វដល់ដប់។ ten fingers 4 I can find the letters K, L and M and say their sounds. ខ្ញុំអាចរកអក្សរ K, L និង M ហើយនិយាយសំឡេងរបស់វា។ point to the letter card"}, {"ref": "L.6 §2 ¶4", "anchor": "p-L.6-2-4", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "956b1a2721", "text": "Draw the four cues on the board and point to them at the start and at the end of the lesson."}, {"ref": "L.6 §3 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.6-3-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "a343dabcab", "text": "RTTI rubric for the teacher"}, {"ref": "L.6 §3 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.6-3-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "ee6f09a57a", "text": "RTTI levels: R Reproduction (repeat what was taught), T1 Training (use it in the practised activity), T2 Transfer (use it in a new situation), I Insight (understand and explain why). The last column shows what to expect after this lesson: green = expected for all or most, yellow = with help, red = stretch goal, not expected yet."}, {"ref": "L.6 §3 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.6-3-2", "kind": "table", "h": "f3764118d4", "text": "Level What the pupil does Teacher looks for Feed back (say) Feed forward (say) Expected after this lesson R – Reproduction Says the four animal words and counts 1–10 with the class. Word matches the picture and gesture; no numbers skipped. \"You know the animal words!\" \"Now say them without my gesture.\" expected for all (rated green) T1 – Training Answers \"What's this?\" with \"It's a dog.\" in the card game. Uses It's a … with the class cards. \"You answered with a whole sentence.\" \"Next, you ask the question.\" expected for most (rated green) T2 – Transfer Asks a partner \"What's this?\" about a new picture and counts animals in a new picture up to ten. Asks the question by themselves; counts a new set correctly. \"You asked like a teacher!\" \"At home, count the chickens or the fish.\" with help (rated yellow) I – Insight Explains that we say \"a cat\" for one, and \"two cats\" with an s for more. Notices the -s in Khmer or with fingers. \"You found an English rule!\" \"Listen for the s in other words.\" stretch goal (rated red)"}, {"ref": "L.6 §3 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.6-3-3", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "9c5dfe92f5", "text": "Letters (criterion 4):"}, {"ref": "L.6 §3 ¶4", "anchor": "p-L.6-3-4", "kind": "table", "h": "dccb42afb3", "text": "Level What the pupil does Teacher looks for Feed back (say) Feed forward (say) Expected after this lesson R – Reproduction Says the letter sounds after the teacher. Clear sound, not the letter name only. \"You said the K sound well!\" \"Now say it when you see the card.\" expected for all (rated green) T1 – Training Points to the right letter card when the teacher says a sound. Points without looking at a neighbour. \"You found K by its sound.\" \"Next, find the letter in a picture word.\" expected for most (rated green) T2 – Transfer Finds the letter at the start of a new word or a name card. Spots the letter in a word not taught today. \"You found L in a new word!\" \"Look for L in your friends' names.\" stretch goal (rated red)"}, {"ref": "L.6 §4 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.6-4-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "5a2137d2b9", "text": "Target vocabulary"}, {"ref": "L.6 §4 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.6-4-1", "kind": "table", "h": "151fa29587", "text": "English Khmer Sound hint Picture idea cat ឆ្មា kat cat dog ឆ្កែ dog dog fish ត្រី fish fish bird សត្វស្លាប berd bird eight ប្រាំបី ayt eight birds nine ប្រាំបួន nayn nine fish ten ដប់ ten ten fingers"}, {"ref": "L.6 §5 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.6-5-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "f137c97e3d", "text": "Target language"}, {"ref": "L.6 §5 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.6-5-1", "kind": "list", "h": "e735133035", "text": "What's this? – It's a cat. How many birds? – Eight! One, two, … ten. Dialogue: Chantha: \"What's this?\" – Piseth: \"It's a dog!\""}, {"ref": "L.6 §6 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.6-6-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "3f5171041f", "text": "The letters"}, {"ref": "L.6 §6 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.6-6-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "b5d6d64121", "text": "Letter recognition and sounds only – no writing yet. Pupils see the capital and small letter, hear the sound and match it to a picture."}, {"ref": "L.6 §6 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.6-6-2", "kind": "table", "h": "37cd70fdb9", "text": "Letter Sound Picture word Khmer-friendly cue K k /k/ 🪁 kite like ក L l /l/ 🍋 lemon like ល M m /m/ 🥭 mango like ម"}, {"ref": "L.6 §7 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.6-7-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "1bd537eb12", "text": "Teacher-led lesson (one study hour, 40 min)"}, {"ref": "L.6 §7 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.6-7-1", "kind": "list", "h": "1d9b15ac63", "text": "Warm-up and feed up (5 min): Say the learning goal and point to the success criteria cues. Hello song. Count 1–7 with fingers (review). Listen and say (8 min): Show the animal flashcards with a sound and a gesture for each animal. Add eight, nine, ten with fingers. Pair work (8 min): \"What's this?\" – class answers \"It's a cat.\" Then pairs ask each other with small animal cards. Letter practice (5 min): Show the letter cards K, L and M (capital and small). Say the sound and the picture word: K – kite, L – lemon, M – mango. Pupils repeat, draw the letter in the air, and point to the right card when they hear the sound. No writing yet. Game (8 min): Animal moves: \"Fish!\" – pupils swim with their hands; \"Bird!\" – fly. Then \"Eight birds!\" – eight pupils fly. Wrap-up and feed back (6 min): Point to each success criterion cue; pupils show thumbs up (I can), sideways (with help) or down (not yet). Give one feed-forward tip from the rubric. Count to ten together. Goodbye song."}, {"ref": "L.6 §8 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.6-8-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "beb8224862", "text": "Self-paced app lesson"}, {"ref": "L.6 §8 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.6-8-1", "kind": "list", "h": "7cc8bff90d", "text": "Listen and tap: the audio says \"dog\"; the pupil taps the dog. What's this?: an animal appears; the pupil records \"It's a fish.\" and hears it back. How many?: a picture of 6–10 birds; the pupil taps the number. Feedback: the birds are counted aloud. Song: an animal counting song."}, {"ref": "L.6 §9 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.6-9-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "07cd9e0db6", "text": "Activities without electronics"}, {"ref": "L.6 §9 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.6-9-1", "kind": "list", "h": "40b0021d2c", "text": "Animal moves: whole class, no materials. Count the chalk animals: the teacher draws 6–10 simple fish on the board; pupils count aloud. Animal sounds guess: a pupil makes an animal sound, the class says \"It's a dog!\"."}, {"ref": "L.6 §10 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.6-10-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "7f57b36be2", "text": "Differentiation"}, {"ref": "L.6 §10 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.6-10-1", "kind": "list", "h": "a77179b5b2", "text": "Need more support: point to the picture and do the gesture; numbers 1–5 only. Ready for more: ask \"What's this?\" to the class, or count backwards from ten."}, {"ref": "L.6 §11 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.6-11-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "3bd9f3865f", "text": "Quick assessment"}, {"ref": "L.6 §11 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.6-11-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "b2655375ea", "text": "Show four animal cards in random order to small groups; tick who can say \"It's a …\". Show 6–10 fingers and tick who can name the number."}, {"ref": "L.6 §12 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.6-12-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "25c86f6a92", "text": "Quiz"}, {"ref": "L.6 §12 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.6-12-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "2289a536b9", "text": "Each question checks one success criterion at one RTTI level. After Check , the quiz shows which levels the pupil reached for each criterion and what to try next."}, {"ref": "L.6 §12 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.6-12-2", "kind": "table", "h": "a7eb1bcba1", "text": "Success criterion RTTI level Question 1 Animal words R 1 2 What's this? T1 2 3 Count to ten T1 3 2 What's this? T2 4 3 Count to ten I 5 4 Letters K, L and M R 6 4 Letters K, L and M T1 7"}, {"ref": "L.6 §12 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.6-12-3", "kind": "quiz", "h": "5fdb1d639f", "text": "1. 🐱 What animal is it? Criterion 1 · RTTI level R cat Yes! It's a cat. dog A dog says woof. This one says meow. fish A fish swims. This one says meow. 2. 🐶 Your friend asks \"What's this?\". You say: Criterion 2 · RTTI level T1 It's a fish. A fish swims. This animal says woof. It's a dog. Yes! A whole sentence: It's a dog. I'm a dog. I'm is for you. Say It's a dog. 3. 🐦🐦🐦🐦🐦🐦🐦🐦 How many birds? Criterion 3 · RTTI level T1 seven Point and count each bird again. eight Yes! Eight birds. ten Point and count each bird again. 4. You see a new animal picture and want to know its name. What do you ask? Criterion 2 · RTTI level T2 What's this? Yes! Ask What's this? How old are you? That asks about age. Goodbye, friend! That is for leaving. 5. You count ten fingers, then you hide one. How many now? Criterion 3 · RTTI level I nine Yes! One less than ten is nine. ten You hid one, so there is one less. eight You hid only one finger. Count again. 6. 🪁 Which letter does \"kite\" start with? Criterion 4 · RTTI level R K Yes! \"kite\" starts with K. A Listen again: \"kite\" – the first sound is K. B Listen again: \"kite\" – the first sound is K. 7. This is the letter L. Which picture starts with L? Criterion 4 · RTTI level T1 🪁 kite That starts with K. Find the L sound. 🍋 lemon Yes! \"lemon\" starts with L. 🐟 fish That starts with F. Find the L sound. Check Try again"}, {"ref": "L.6 §13 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.6-13-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "b8efd777f4", "text": "CEFR cross-reference"}, {"ref": "L.6 §13 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.6-13-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "9ace50ee5c", "text": "Secondary reference only. Pre-A1 can-do statements adapted from the CEFR Companion Volume (2020); not an official CEFR test."}, {"ref": "L.6 §13 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.6-13-2", "kind": "list", "h": "c3dbf4df9b", "text": "I can name a few animals in English when I see a picture. I can answer What's this? with It's a … . I can count to ten. I can recognise the letters K, L and M and say their sounds."}], "html": "<div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"a29ea4a3ec\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.6 §0 ¶0\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.6-0-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §0 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §0 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶0</button><h1 data-body=\"1\">Lesson 6: Animals – numbers to 10</h1></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"e4922db823\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.6 §0 ¶1\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.6-0-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §0 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §0 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Pupils meet four animals they know from home and the village, and count to ten. The topic leads into Unit 3 \"Animals\" of the MoEYS English Grade 4 book.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"025eec04ab\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.6 §1 ¶0\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.6-1-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §1 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §1 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">MoEYS frame</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"f5d0ec1e03\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.6 §1 ¶1\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.6-1-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §1 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §1 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶1</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>MoEYS reference</th>\n<th>This lesson</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Framework</td>\n<td>Curriculum Framework of General Education and Technical Education (MoEYS, 2016)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Subject and grade</td>\n<td>Foreign Languages (English), Grade 1 (primary)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Core competency</td>\n<td>4.2 Foreign Languages: \"Learners can adequately use foreign languages for communication, research and continued study.\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Foreign Languages goals (section 5.6, quoted)</td>\n<td>\"Possess competencies in communication in all four skills (listening, speaking, reading and writing).\" \"Become life-long learners with creativity and confidence.\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Expected outcome for primary (quoted)</td>\n<td>\"Construct basic knowledge of Science, Information and Communications Technology (ICT) and Foreign Languages.\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Subject components</td>\n<td>Listening and Speaking in this lesson, plus first letter recognition (Reading and Writing come later)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Study time</td>\n<td>Grade 1 has 2 study hours of Foreign Languages per week; one study hour is 40 minutes. This lesson is one study hour.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Lesson learning outcome (draft)</td>\n<td>Pupils name common animals, ask and answer What's this? about animals, and count to ten (Listening and Speaking).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Assessment (framework section 8.1)</td>\n<td>Knowledge, skills, attitude and application skills – observed with the RTTI rubric below</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3119e881c9\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.6 §1 ¶2\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.6-1-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §1 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §1 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>Lesson syllabus</strong> (in the Function / Form / Vocabulary format of the MoEYS English Grade 4 textbook):</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"fbbe4177c0\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.6 §1 ¶3\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.6-1-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §1 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §1 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶3</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Function</th>\n<th>Form</th>\n<th>Vocabulary</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Asking and answering about animals; counting to ten</td>\n<td>What's this? – It's a cat. – How many? – Ten!</td>\n<td>cat, dog, fish, bird, eight, nine, ten; letters K, L, M</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"27efc58195\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.6 §2 ¶0\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.6-2-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §2 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §2 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Feed up: where are we going?</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"588b764232\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.6 §2 ¶1\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.6-2-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §2 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §2 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>Learning goal (say it at the start):</strong> Today we learn animal words and count animals to ten.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"ecc410ecc1\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.6 §2 ¶2\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.6-2-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §2 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §2 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>In Khmer:</strong> ថ្ងៃនេះ យើងរៀនឈ្មោះសត្វ និងរាប់សត្វដល់ដប់។</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"c3f8eda659\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.6 §2 ¶3\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.6-2-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §2 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §2 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶3</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>#</th>\n<th>Success criterion (pupil words)</th>\n<th>Khmer (pupil words)</th>\n<th>Picture or gesture cue</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>I can say cat, dog, fish and bird.</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំអាចនិយាយ cat, dog, fish និង bird។</td>\n<td>animal gestures (whiskers, paws, fish hands, wings)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>I can ask and answer: What's this? – It's a cat.</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំអាចសួរ និងឆ្លើយ៖ What's this? – It's a cat។</td>\n<td>hand open, question face</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>I can count animals up to ten.</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំអាចរាប់សត្វដល់ដប់។</td>\n<td>ten fingers</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>I can find the letters K, L and M and say their sounds.</td>\n<td>ខ្ញុំអាចរកអក្សរ K, L និង M ហើយនិយាយសំឡេងរបស់វា។</td>\n<td>point to the letter card</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"956b1a2721\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"4\" data-ref=\"L.6 §2 ¶4\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.6-2-4\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §2 ¶4\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §2 ¶4 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶4</button><p data-body=\"1\">Draw the four cues on the board and point to them at the start and at the end of the lesson.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"a343dabcab\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.6 §3 ¶0\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.6-3-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §3 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §3 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">RTTI rubric for the teacher</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"ee6f09a57a\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.6 §3 ¶1\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.6-3-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §3 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §3 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">RTTI levels: <strong>R</strong> Reproduction (repeat what was taught), <strong>T1</strong> Training (use it in the practised activity), <strong>T2</strong> Transfer (use it in a new situation), <strong>I</strong> Insight (understand and explain why). The last column shows what to expect after this lesson: green = expected for all or most, yellow = with help, red = stretch goal, not expected yet.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"f3764118d4\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.6 §3 ¶2\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.6-3-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §3 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §3 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Level</th>\n<th>What the pupil does</th>\n<th>Teacher looks for</th>\n<th>Feed back (say)</th>\n<th>Feed forward (say)</th>\n<th>Expected after this lesson</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>R – Reproduction</td>\n<td>Says the four animal words and counts 1–10 with the class.</td>\n<td>Word matches the picture and gesture; no numbers skipped.</td>\n<td>\"You know the animal words!\"</td>\n<td>\"Now say them without my gesture.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">expected for all<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T1 – Training</td>\n<td>Answers \"What's this?\" with \"It's a dog.\" in the card game.</td>\n<td>Uses It's a … with the class cards.</td>\n<td>\"You answered with a whole sentence.\"</td>\n<td>\"Next, you ask the question.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">expected for most<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T2 – Transfer</td>\n<td>Asks a partner \"What's this?\" about a new picture and counts animals in a new picture up to ten.</td>\n<td>Asks the question by themselves; counts a new set correctly.</td>\n<td>\"You asked like a teacher!\"</td>\n<td>\"At home, count the chickens or the fish.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-yellow\">with help<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"yellow\" title=\"Rated yellow\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated yellow)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>I – Insight</td>\n<td>Explains that we say \"a cat\" for one, and \"two cats\" with an s for more.</td>\n<td>Notices the -s in Khmer or with fingers.</td>\n<td>\"You found an English rule!\"</td>\n<td>\"Listen for the s in other words.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-red\">stretch goal<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"red\" title=\"Rated red\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-xmark\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated red)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9c5dfe92f5\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.6 §3 ¶3\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.6-3-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §3 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §3 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶3</button><p data-body=\"1\"><strong>Letters (criterion 4):</strong></p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"dccb42afb3\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"4\" data-ref=\"L.6 §3 ¶4\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.6-3-4\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §3 ¶4\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §3 ¶4 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶4</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Level</th>\n<th>What the pupil does</th>\n<th>Teacher looks for</th>\n<th>Feed back (say)</th>\n<th>Feed forward (say)</th>\n<th>Expected after this lesson</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>R – Reproduction</td>\n<td>Says the letter sounds after the teacher.</td>\n<td>Clear sound, not the letter name only.</td>\n<td>\"You said the K sound well!\"</td>\n<td>\"Now say it when you see the card.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">expected for all<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T1 – Training</td>\n<td>Points to the right letter card when the teacher says a sound.</td>\n<td>Points without looking at a neighbour.</td>\n<td>\"You found K by its sound.\"</td>\n<td>\"Next, find the letter in a picture word.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">expected for most<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T2 – Transfer</td>\n<td>Finds the letter at the start of a new word or a name card.</td>\n<td>Spots the letter in a word not taught today.</td>\n<td>\"You found L in a new word!\"</td>\n<td>\"Look for L in your friends' names.\"</td>\n<td class=\"cell-red\">stretch goal<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"red\" title=\"Rated red\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-xmark\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated red)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"5a2137d2b9\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.6 §4 ¶0\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.6-4-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §4 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §4 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Target vocabulary</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"151fa29587\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.6 §4 ¶1\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.6-4-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §4 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §4 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶1</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>English</th>\n<th>Khmer</th>\n<th>Sound hint</th>\n<th>Picture idea</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>cat</td>\n<td>ឆ្មា</td>\n<td>kat</td>\n<td>cat</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>dog</td>\n<td>ឆ្កែ</td>\n<td>dog</td>\n<td>dog</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>fish</td>\n<td>ត្រី</td>\n<td>fish</td>\n<td>fish</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>bird</td>\n<td>សត្វស្លាប</td>\n<td>berd</td>\n<td>bird</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>eight</td>\n<td>ប្រាំបី</td>\n<td>ayt</td>\n<td>eight birds</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>nine</td>\n<td>ប្រាំបួន</td>\n<td>nayn</td>\n<td>nine fish</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>ten</td>\n<td>ដប់</td>\n<td>ten</td>\n<td>ten fingers</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"f137c97e3d\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.6 §5 ¶0\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.6-5-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §5 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §5 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Target language</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"e735133035\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.6 §5 ¶1\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.6-5-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §5 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §5 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>What's this? – It's a cat.</li>\n<li>How many birds? – Eight!</li>\n<li>One, two, … ten.</li>\n<li>Dialogue: <strong>Chantha:</strong> \"What's this?\" – <strong>Piseth:</strong> \"It's a dog!\"</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3f5171041f\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.6 §6 ¶0\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.6-6-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §6 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §6 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">The letters</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b5d6d64121\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.6 §6 ¶1\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.6-6-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §6 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §6 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Letter recognition and sounds only – no writing yet. Pupils see the capital and small letter, hear the sound and match it to a picture.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"37cd70fdb9\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.6 §6 ¶2\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.6-6-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §6 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §6 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Letter</th>\n<th>Sound</th>\n<th>Picture word</th>\n<th>Khmer-friendly cue</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>K k</td>\n<td>/k/</td>\n<td>🪁 kite</td>\n<td>like ក</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>L l</td>\n<td>/l/</td>\n<td>🍋 lemon</td>\n<td>like ល</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>M m</td>\n<td>/m/</td>\n<td>🥭 mango</td>\n<td>like ម</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"1bd537eb12\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.6 §7 ¶0\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.6-7-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §7 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §7 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Teacher-led lesson (one study hour, 40 min)</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"1d9b15ac63\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.6 §7 ¶1\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.6-7-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §7 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §7 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Warm-up and feed up (5 min):</strong> Say the learning goal and point to the success criteria cues. Hello song. Count 1–7 with fingers (review).</li>\n<li><strong>Listen and say (8 min):</strong> Show the animal flashcards with a sound and a gesture for each animal. Add eight, nine, ten with fingers.</li>\n<li><strong>Pair work (8 min):</strong> \"What's this?\" – class answers \"It's a cat.\" Then pairs ask each other with small animal cards.</li>\n<li><strong>Letter practice (5 min):</strong> Show the letter cards K, L and M (capital and small). Say the sound and the picture word: K – kite, L – lemon, M – mango. Pupils repeat, draw the letter in the air, and point to the right card when they hear the sound. No writing yet.</li>\n<li><strong>Game (8 min):</strong> <em>Animal moves:</em> \"Fish!\" – pupils swim with their hands; \"Bird!\" – fly. Then \"Eight birds!\" – eight pupils fly.</li>\n<li><strong>Wrap-up and feed back (6 min):</strong> Point to each success criterion cue; pupils show thumbs up (I can), sideways (with help) or down (not yet). Give one feed-forward tip from the rubric. Count to ten together. Goodbye song.</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"beb8224862\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.6 §8 ¶0\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.6-8-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §8 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §8 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Self-paced app lesson</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"7cc8bff90d\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.6 §8 ¶1\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.6-8-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §8 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §8 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Listen and tap:</strong> the audio says \"dog\"; the pupil taps the dog.</li>\n<li><strong>What's this?:</strong> an animal appears; the pupil records \"It's a fish.\" and hears it back.</li>\n<li><strong>How many?:</strong> a picture of 6–10 birds; the pupil taps the number. Feedback: the birds are counted aloud.</li>\n<li><strong>Song:</strong> an animal counting song.</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"07cd9e0db6\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.6 §9 ¶0\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.6-9-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §9 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §9 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Activities without electronics</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"40b0021d2c\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.6 §9 ¶1\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.6-9-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §9 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §9 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Animal moves:</strong> whole class, no materials.</li>\n<li><strong>Count the chalk animals:</strong> the teacher draws 6–10 simple fish on the board; pupils count aloud.</li>\n<li><strong>Animal sounds guess:</strong> a pupil makes an animal sound, the class says \"It's a dog!\".</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"7f57b36be2\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.6 §10 ¶0\" data-sec=\"10\" id=\"p-L.6-10-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §10 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §10 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§10 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Differentiation</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"a77179b5b2\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.6 §10 ¶1\" data-sec=\"10\" id=\"p-L.6-10-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §10 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §10 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§10 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Need more support:</strong> point to the picture and do the gesture; numbers 1–5 only.</li>\n<li><strong>Ready for more:</strong> ask \"What's this?\" to the class, or count backwards from ten.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3bd9f3865f\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.6 §11 ¶0\" data-sec=\"11\" id=\"p-L.6-11-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §11 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §11 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§11 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Quick assessment</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b2655375ea\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.6 §11 ¶1\" data-sec=\"11\" id=\"p-L.6-11-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §11 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §11 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§11 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Show four animal cards in random order to small groups; tick who can say \"It's a …\". Show 6–10 fingers and tick who can name the number.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"25c86f6a92\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.6 §12 ¶0\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.6-12-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §12 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §12 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Quiz</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"2289a536b9\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.6 §12 ¶1\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.6-12-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §12 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §12 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Each question checks one success criterion at one RTTI level. After <strong>Check</strong>, the quiz shows which levels the pupil reached for each criterion and what to try next.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"a7eb1bcba1\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.6 §12 ¶2\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.6-12-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §12 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §12 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Success criterion</th>\n<th>RTTI level</th>\n<th>Question</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1 Animal words</td>\n<td>R</td>\n<td>1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2 What's this?</td>\n<td>T1</td>\n<td>2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3 Count to ten</td>\n<td>T1</td>\n<td>3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2 What's this?</td>\n<td>T2</td>\n<td>4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3 Count to ten</td>\n<td>I</td>\n<td>5</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4 Letters K, L and M</td>\n<td>R</td>\n<td>6</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4 Letters K, L and M</td>\n<td>T1</td>\n<td>7</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-quiz\" data-h=\"5fdb1d639f\" data-kind=\"quiz\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.6 §12 ¶3\" data-sec=\"12\" id=\"p-L.6-12-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §12 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §12 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§12 ¶3</button><div aria-label=\"Quiz\" class=\"quiz\" data-body=\"1\" role=\"group\"><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"R\" data-q=\"1\" data-sc=\"SC1\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">1.</span> 🐱 What animal is it?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 1 · RTTI level R</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">cat</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! It's a cat.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">dog</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A dog says woof. This one says meow.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">fish</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A fish swims. This one says meow.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T1\" data-q=\"2\" data-sc=\"SC2\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">2.</span> 🐶 Your friend asks \"What's this?\". You say:</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 2 · RTTI level T1</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">It's a fish.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A fish swims. This animal says woof.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">It's a dog.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! A whole sentence: It's a dog.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">I'm a dog.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">I'm is for you. Say It's a dog.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T1\" data-q=\"3\" data-sc=\"SC3\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">3.</span> 🐦🐦🐦🐦🐦🐦🐦🐦 How many birds?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 3 · RTTI level T1</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">seven</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Point and count each bird again.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">eight</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! Eight birds.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">ten</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Point and count each bird again.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T2\" data-q=\"4\" data-sc=\"SC2\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">4.</span> You see a new animal picture and want to know its name. What do you ask?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 2 · RTTI level T2</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">What's this?</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! Ask What's this?</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">How old are you?</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That asks about age.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Goodbye, friend!</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That is for leaving.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"I\" data-q=\"5\" data-sc=\"SC3\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">5.</span> You count ten fingers, then you hide one. How many now?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 3 · RTTI level I</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">nine</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! One less than ten is nine.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">ten</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">You hid one, so there is one less.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">eight</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">You hid only one finger. Count again.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"R\" data-q=\"6\" data-sc=\"SC4\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">6.</span> 🪁 Which letter does \"kite\" start with?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 4 · RTTI level R</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">K</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! \"kite\" starts with K.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">A</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Listen again: \"kite\" – the first sound is K.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">B</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Listen again: \"kite\" – the first sound is K.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T1\" data-q=\"7\" data-sc=\"SC4\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">7.</span> This is the letter L. Which picture starts with L?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 4 · RTTI level T1</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">🪁 kite</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That starts with K. Find the L sound.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">🍋 lemon</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! \"lemon\" starts with L.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">🐟 fish</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That starts with F. Find the L sound.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><div class=\"quiz-actions\"><button class=\"btn btn-primary quiz-check\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-check-double\"></i> Check</button><button class=\"btn btn-outline-secondary quiz-retry\" hidden=\"\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-rotate-left\"></i> Try again</button><span aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-score\" role=\"status\"></span></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-rtti\" hidden=\"\"></div></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b8efd777f4\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.6 §13 ¶0\" data-sec=\"13\" id=\"p-L.6-13-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §13 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §13 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§13 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">CEFR cross-reference</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9ace50ee5c\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.6 §13 ¶1\" data-sec=\"13\" id=\"p-L.6-13-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §13 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §13 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§13 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Secondary reference only. Pre-A1 can-do statements adapted from the CEFR Companion Volume (2020); not an official CEFR test.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"c3dbf4df9b\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.6 §13 ¶2\" data-sec=\"13\" id=\"p-L.6-13-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.6 §13 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.6 §13 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§13 ¶2</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>I can name a few animals in English when I see a picture.</li>\n<li>I can answer <strong>What's this?</strong> with <strong>It's a …</strong>.</li>\n<li>I can count to ten.</li>\n<li>I can recognise the letters K, L and M and say their sounds.</li>\n</ul></div>"}, {"id": "R.1", "title": "Progress checklist and review quiz (Lessons 1–5)", "order": 7, "goals": ["Record each pupil's RTTI level per success criterion after Lessons 1–5.", "Review all five lessons with one quiz that maps back to the checklist."], "metadata": {"status": "draft", "grade": "1", "subject": "Foreign Languages (English)", "moeys_reference": "assessment principle 8.1 of the Curriculum Framework (2016); Grade 1 English syllabus to be checked", "cefr_cross_reference": "Pre-A1 (adapted)", "updated": "2026-11-05"}, "file": "r1-progress-checklist.md", "notes": [], "blocks": [{"ref": "R.1 §0 ¶0", "anchor": "p-R.1-0-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "8700d44294", "text": "Progress checklist and review quiz (Lessons 1–5)"}, {"ref": "R.1 §0 ¶1", "anchor": "p-R.1-0-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "4ac5f895f7", "text": "Use this checklist after Lesson 5. It follows the MoEYS principle that teachers assess regularly and use the results to give feedback (Curriculum Framework 2016, section 8). Watch pupils during games and pair work; do not give a written test."}, {"ref": "R.1 §1 ¶0", "anchor": "p-R.1-1-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "9bd2e9ce63", "text": "Progress checklist"}, {"ref": "R.1 §1 ¶1", "anchor": "p-R.1-1-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "691208db17", "text": "Example record for one pupil: the highest RTTI level reached per lesson goal. Green = reached the expected level, yellow = with help, red = not yet."}, {"ref": "R.1 §1 ¶2", "anchor": "p-R.1-1-2", "kind": "table", "h": "f5ce150e25", "text": "# Review criterion Lesson Highest level (example) 1 I can greet and say my name. 1 T2 (rated green) 2 I can count to 5 and say my age. 2 T1 (rated green) 3 I can name four colours. 3 R (rated yellow) 4 I can name classroom things and follow \"Show me …!\". 4 not yet (rated red) 5 I can say \"This is my mother / father / sister / brother\". 5 T1 (rated green)"}, {"ref": "R.1 §2 ¶0", "anchor": "p-R.1-2-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "681b0b187b", "text": "Feed back and feed forward after the review"}, {"ref": "R.1 §2 ¶1", "anchor": "p-R.1-2-1", "kind": "table", "h": "25dadb9eb0", "text": "Result Feed back (say) Feed forward (do) Mostly green \"You can do a lot of English already!\" Go on to the next unit; try the T2 and I tasks. Some yellow \"You can do it with help.\" Repeat the T1 games from those lessons in the review lesson. Red \"We will practise this together.\" Pair with a green partner; R-level drills; app at home if possible."}, {"ref": "R.1 §3 ¶0", "anchor": "p-R.1-3-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "bed7b0b1ee", "text": "Review quiz"}, {"ref": "R.1 §3 ¶1", "anchor": "p-R.1-3-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "1454abe8d3", "text": "Each question checks one review criterion at one RTTI level."}, {"ref": "R.1 §3 ¶2", "anchor": "p-R.1-3-2", "kind": "table", "h": "19757bd272", "text": "Review criterion RTTI level Question 1 Greet and name T2 1 2 Count and age T1 2 3 Colours R 3 4 Classroom things T2 4 5 Family I 5"}, {"ref": "R.1 §3 ¶3", "anchor": "p-R.1-3-3", "kind": "quiz", "h": "acb24be444", "text": "1. You meet a new teacher in the morning. What do you say? Criterion 1 · RTTI level T2 Hello! I'm Vichea. Yes! You greeted a new person and said your name. Goodbye! I am six. Goodbye is for when you leave. Red pencil, please. That is not a greeting. Say Hello and your name. 2. 🖐️ How many fingers? Criterion 2 · RTTI level T1 three Count again: one, two, three, four, five. four Count again – do not forget the thumb. five Yes! Five fingers. 3. 🟦 What colour is it? Criterion 3 · RTTI level R yellow Yellow is like a banana. This is blue. blue Yes! It is blue. red Red is like a chilli. This is blue. 4. 🎒 Your friend shows you this. What's this? Criterion 4 · RTTI level T2 It's a bag. Yes! It's a bag. It's a desk. A desk is a table. This is a bag. It's a book. A book has pages. This is a bag. 5. Your older sister and your younger sister: in English both are… Criterion 5 · RTTI level I brother A brother is a boy. sister Yes! English uses one word: sister. father A father is a man. Check Try again"}], "html": "<div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"8700d44294\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"R.1 §0 ¶0\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-R.1-0-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference R.1 §0 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"R.1 §0 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶0</button><h1 data-body=\"1\">Progress checklist and review quiz (Lessons 1–5)</h1></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"4ac5f895f7\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"R.1 §0 ¶1\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-R.1-0-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference R.1 §0 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"R.1 §0 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Use this checklist after Lesson 5. It follows the MoEYS principle that teachers assess regularly and use the results to give feedback (Curriculum Framework 2016, section 8). Watch pupils during games and pair work; do not give a written test.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9bd2e9ce63\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"R.1 §1 ¶0\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-R.1-1-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference R.1 §1 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"R.1 §1 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Progress checklist</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"691208db17\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"R.1 §1 ¶1\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-R.1-1-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference R.1 §1 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"R.1 §1 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Example record for one pupil: the highest RTTI level reached per lesson goal. <strong>Green</strong> = reached the expected level, <strong>yellow</strong> = with help, <strong>red</strong> = not yet.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"f5ce150e25\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"R.1 §1 ¶2\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-R.1-1-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference R.1 §1 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"R.1 §1 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>#</th>\n<th>Review criterion</th>\n<th>Lesson</th>\n<th>Highest level (example)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>I can greet and say my name.</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">T2<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>I can count to 5 and say my age.</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">T1<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>I can name four colours.</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td class=\"cell-yellow\">R<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"yellow\" title=\"Rated yellow\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated yellow)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>I can name classroom things and follow \"Show me …!\".</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td class=\"cell-red\">not yet<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"red\" title=\"Rated red\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-xmark\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated red)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>I can say \"This is my mother / father / sister / brother\".</td>\n<td>5</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">T1<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"681b0b187b\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"R.1 §2 ¶0\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-R.1-2-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference R.1 §2 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"R.1 §2 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Feed back and feed forward after the review</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"25dadb9eb0\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"R.1 §2 ¶1\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-R.1-2-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference R.1 §2 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"R.1 §2 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶1</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Result</th>\n<th>Feed back (say)</th>\n<th>Feed forward (do)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Mostly green</td>\n<td>\"You can do a lot of English already!\"</td>\n<td>Go on to the next unit; try the T2 and I tasks.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Some yellow</td>\n<td>\"You can do it with help.\"</td>\n<td>Repeat the T1 games from those lessons in the review lesson.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Red</td>\n<td>\"We will practise this together.\"</td>\n<td>Pair with a green partner; R-level drills; app at home if possible.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"bed7b0b1ee\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"R.1 §3 ¶0\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-R.1-3-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference R.1 §3 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"R.1 §3 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Review quiz</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"1454abe8d3\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"R.1 §3 ¶1\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-R.1-3-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference R.1 §3 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"R.1 §3 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Each question checks one review criterion at one RTTI level.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"19757bd272\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"R.1 §3 ¶2\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-R.1-3-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference R.1 §3 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"R.1 §3 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Review criterion</th>\n<th>RTTI level</th>\n<th>Question</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1 Greet and name</td>\n<td>T2</td>\n<td>1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2 Count and age</td>\n<td>T1</td>\n<td>2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3 Colours</td>\n<td>R</td>\n<td>3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4 Classroom things</td>\n<td>T2</td>\n<td>4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5 Family</td>\n<td>I</td>\n<td>5</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-quiz\" data-h=\"acb24be444\" data-kind=\"quiz\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"R.1 §3 ¶3\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-R.1-3-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference R.1 §3 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"R.1 §3 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶3</button><div aria-label=\"Quiz\" class=\"quiz\" data-body=\"1\" role=\"group\"><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T2\" data-q=\"1\" data-sc=\"SC1\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">1.</span> You meet a new teacher in the morning. What do you say?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 1 · RTTI level T2</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Hello! I'm Vichea.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! You greeted a new person and said your name.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Goodbye! I am six.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Goodbye is for when you leave.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Red pencil, please.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That is not a greeting. Say Hello and your name.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T1\" data-q=\"2\" data-sc=\"SC2\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">2.</span> 🖐️ How many fingers?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 2 · RTTI level T1</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">three</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Count again: one, two, three, four, five.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">four</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Count again – do not forget the thumb.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">five</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! Five fingers.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"R\" data-q=\"3\" data-sc=\"SC3\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">3.</span> 🟦 What colour is it?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 3 · RTTI level R</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">yellow</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yellow is like a banana. This is blue.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">blue</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! It is blue.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">red</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Red is like a chilli. This is blue.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"T2\" data-q=\"4\" data-sc=\"SC4\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">4.</span> 🎒 Your friend shows you this. What's this?</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 4 · RTTI level T2</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">It's a bag.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! It's a bag.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">It's a desk.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A desk is a table. This is a bag.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">It's a book.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A book has pages. This is a bag.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-level=\"I\" data-q=\"5\" data-sc=\"SC5\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">5.</span> Your older sister and your younger sister: in English both are…</legend><div class=\"quiz-tag small text-body-secondary\">Criterion 5 · RTTI level I</div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">brother</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A brother is a boy.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">sister</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yes! English uses one word: sister.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">father</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A father is a man.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><div class=\"quiz-actions\"><button class=\"btn btn-primary quiz-check\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-check-double\"></i> Check</button><button class=\"btn btn-outline-secondary quiz-retry\" hidden=\"\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-rotate-left\"></i> Try again</button><span aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-score\" role=\"status\"></span></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-rtti\" hidden=\"\"></div></div></div>"}], "pages": {"help": "<h1>Help</h1>\n<p>This is a <strong>review reader</strong> for <em>tli.cloud: English in Cambodia</em>. You can read every part, propose changes, propose removals and leave comments. Everything you do is saved <strong>only in this browser on this device</strong> until you export it.</p>\n<h2>Reading</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The <strong>Parts</strong> list on the left (the ☰ button on a phone) opens one part at a time.</li>\n<li>Every block has a reference in the margin, like <strong>§2 ¶3</strong>. Section 0 is the part title and the text before the first <code>##</code> heading. Each <code>##</code>/<code>###</code> heading starts a new section and is ¶0 of it. The full reference is <code>PART §section ¶paragraph</code>, for example <code>L.3 §2 ¶3</code>.</li>\n<li>Click a reference to copy it and to show the action buttons (useful on touch screens).</li>\n<li><strong>Editor notes</strong> for the open part are in the right-hand panel (below the text on small screens). They are never shown in the lesson text.</li>\n<li><strong>Search</strong> in the top bar searches all parts. Click a result to jump to the paragraph.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Editing a paragraph</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Click a paragraph, heading, list item or table cell (or use the ✎ button). It turns yellow.</li>\n<li>Type your change. <strong>Enter</strong> saves (in lists Enter starts a new item; use <strong>Ctrl+Enter</strong> to save). <strong>Shift+Enter</strong> makes a line break. <strong>Esc</strong> cancels.</li>\n<li><strong>Save</strong>, <strong>Cancel</strong> or <strong>Reset to source</strong>. An edited block is marked <em>Edited</em> with a brown bar; <em>Show original</em> lets you compare.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Only one block can be edited at a time. Use <strong>Editing on/off</strong> in the top bar to read without accidental edits. Links still work with a normal click.</p>\n<p>If the source text changes after you edited it (a new build), the block shows <strong>Source changed since…</strong> and your edit is not applied. You can <em>Edit again</em> or <em>Discard</em>. The item stays in your feedback until you remove it.</p>\n<h2>Removing and commenting</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>🗑 <strong>Propose removal</strong>: the block is struck through. Click <strong>Restore</strong> to undo. The original text is recorded for the export.</li>\n<li>💬 <strong>Comment</strong>: write a note; it appears under the block with a blue bar.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>My feedback and export</h2>\n<p>The <strong>My feedback</strong> tab lists all your changes, removals and comments, grouped by part, with counts and links back to the text. Each item has <strong>Undo</strong> / <strong>Delete</strong>. <strong>Clear all</strong> asks for confirmation first.</p>\n<p>Export with <strong>Copy to clipboard</strong>, <strong>Download .md</strong> or <strong>Download .json</strong> and send the file to the editor. The Markdown export looks like this:</p>\n<pre><code># Feedback on tli.cloud: English in Cambodia\nExported 2026-11-04 14:05 · reader built 2026-11-04 12:00 · reader v1.0\nContent: 1 changes, 1 removed, 1 comments\n## L.1 Lesson 1: Hello!\n### L.1 §1 ¶2 — CHANGED\nBefore: \"old text\"\nAfter: \"new text\"\n### L.1 §1 ¶3 — REMOVED\nBefore: \"text\"\n- L.1 §2 ¶1 — COMMENT: my comment\n  &gt; «start of the paragraph»\n</code></pre>\n<p>Table edits are exported as a whole Markdown table; list edits as the whole list.</p>\n<h2>Images and markers (for authors)</h2>\n<p>Put an image on its own line in the Markdown:</p>\n<table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Markdown</th>\n<th>Result</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>![Alt text](images/x.svg)</code></td>\n<td>floats right, at most 40% wide and about 18rem high</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>![Alt text](images/x.svg){right}</code></td>\n<td>same as the default</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>![Alt text](images/x.svg){left}</code></td>\n<td>floats left</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>![Alt text](images/x.svg){full}</code></td>\n<td>full width, no float</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Two images in a row are stacked, never side by side. Headings, tables, quizzes and code always start below a floating image. On phones (narrower than 576px) nothing floats. The alt text is required: it is the caption in the lightbox and is read by screen readers.</p>\n<h2>Lightbox</h2>\n<p>Click or tap an image to enlarge it on a dark background (up to 95% of the screen; small images are enlarged up to 2×). The caption is the alt text. Close with the <strong>✕</strong> button, <strong>Esc</strong>, or a click on the dark background. Pinch-zoom works on phones.</p>\n<h2>Colour tags in tables (for authors)</h2>\n<p>End a table cell with <code>{green}</code>, <code>{yellow}</code> or <code>{red}</code>. The cell gets a colour <strong>and</strong> an icon and a hidden text (\"rated green\") so the meaning does not depend on colour alone.</p>\n<h2>Quiz syntax (for authors)</h2>\n<pre><code>```quiz\nQ: What does CEFR describe?\n- [ ] A school timetable | No: CEFR does not set timetables.\n- [x] Levels of language ability from A1 to C2\n- [ ] A Cambodian exam | No: CEFR is European and used worldwide.\n```\n</code></pre>\n<ul>\n<li><code>Q:</code> starts a question. Each option is <code>- [ ] text | explanation</code>; mark exactly one correct option with <code>- [x]</code>.</li>\n<li>At least 3 options per question, and every wrong option needs an explanation after <code>|</code>.</li>\n<li>There is one <strong>Check</strong> button per quiz. After checking you see ✔ or ✘ per question, the explanation under a wrong answer, \"N of M correct\", \"Not answered\" for skipped questions, and <strong>Try again</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Editor notes (for authors)</h2>\n<p>Write notes for editors as an HTML comment <code>&lt;!-- … --&gt;</code> or a fenced block with the language <code>EDITOR-NOTE</code>. They are removed from the lesson text and shown in the Editor notes panel.</p>\n<h2>Privacy</h2>\n<p>Nothing is sent anywhere. Your feedback is stored in this browser's local storage; clearing browser data deletes it, so export first.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p>reader v1.3 · built 2026-11-05 09:04</p>\n<h2>Feed-up quizzes</h2>\n<p>A quiz question can carry a tag line right after <code>Q:</code>, for example <code>Tag: SC2 T1</code>: success criterion 2, RTTI level T1 (levels R, T1, T2, I). Tag all questions of a quiz or none. After <strong>Check</strong>, the quiz shows per criterion which levels were reached and what to try next.</p>\n", "changes": "<h2>Plan</h2><p>This is a review copy of the course. The change log and the list of open items are kept by the course team and are not part of this copy.</p>", "openItems": ""}, "stats": {"parts": 8, "blocks": 286, "images": 4, "quizzes": 7, "questions": 45, "notes": 33, "links_internal": 0, "links_external": 0, "cell_tags": 44}};
